window.KB4IT_INDEX = [{"u":"ab.html","t":"ab","s":"from (a time)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Samstag ab neun Uhr kommen die Handwerker. :: On Saturday from nine o'clock the workmen are coming."]]},{"u":"abends.html","t":"abends","s":"in the evening","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Abends lese ich gern. :: In the evening I like reading."]]},{"u":"aber.html","t":"aber","s":"but","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Schön, aber anstrengend. :: Nice, but tiring. Ich will spielen, aber ich muss Hausaufgaben machen. :: I want to play, but I have to do homework."]]},{"u":"abfahren.html","t":"abfahren","s":"to depart","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Bus fährt um acht Uhr ab. :: The bus leaves at eight o'clock."]]},{"u":"abgeben.html","t":"abgeben","s":"to hand in / to leave with someone","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Paketbote hat es bei mir abgegeben. :: The delivery man left it with me."]]},{"u":"abgemacht.html","t":"Abgemacht!","s":"Deal!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Gut, abgemacht! :: OK, it's a deal! Ist das abgemacht? :: Is that agreed?"],["usage","Usage","When you agree on a plan, such as who drives to training."]]},{"u":"abholen.html","t":"abholen","s":"to pick up","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich hole sie um Viertel nach vier ab. :: I will pick her up at quarter past four. Wer hat die Kinder abgeholt? :: Who picked up the children?"],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich abhole meine Tochter. :: Ich hole meine Tochter ab."]]},{"u":"abnahme.html","t":"Abnahme","s":"acceptance (of finished work)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Laufzeit beträgt 15 Jahre beginnend mit dem Monat, der auf die Abnahme der Anlage folgt. :: The term is 15 years, starting with the month after the acceptance of the system. Über die Abnahme ist ein Protokoll zu erstellen. :: A record must be made of the acceptance. Nach der Abnahme bekommen wir die Rechnung. :: After the acceptance we get the invoice."],["notes","Notes","After building work, the customer checks the result and signs that it is accepted: that is the Abnahme . Payments and the warranty usually start from that day. In other contexts Abnahme means a decrease, such as weight loss ( abnehmen : to lose weight)."]]},{"u":"absage-training-wegen-hitze.html","t":"Absage: Training wegen Hitze","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Hallo, ich wollte kurz Bescheid geben, dass Kind A. heute leider nicht zum Training kommen kann. :: Hello, I just wanted to let you know that child A. sadly cannot come to training today. ich: Bei den hohen Temperaturen möchte ich ihn lieber nicht trainieren lassen, auch wenn er sich riesig darauf gefreut hat. :: With these high temperatures I would rather not let him train, even though he was really looking forward to it. ich: Ich hoffe auf euer Verständnis. Vielen Dank und liebe Grüße! :: I hope you understand. Many thanks and best wishes! Trainer: Hallo, ist ok. Wir machen heute nur lockere Übungen. :: Hello, that's OK. Today we are only doing light exercises. ich: Danke! Beim nächsten Training ist er wieder dabei. :: Thanks! He'll be there again at the next training."],["variations","Variations","1 ich: Hallo, Kind A. kann heute wegen der großen Hitze nicht zum Training kommen. :: Hello, child A. cannot come to training today because of the great heat. 4 Trainer: Schade, aber verständlich. Bis zum nächsten Mal! :: A pity, but understandable. See you next time!"],["notes","Notes","Turns 1 to 3 follow the message drafted for the learner; the coach's real answer is in the text Antwort des Trainers: Training bei Hitze . sich freuen auf (+ Akkusativ) is about something in the future: Er freut sich auf das Training. sich freuen über is about something that already happened."]]},{"u":"ach.html","t":"ach","s":"oh","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ach so, jetzt verstehe ich. :: Oh I see, now I understand."]]},{"u":"acht.html","t":"acht","s":"eight","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Es ist acht Uhr. Zeit fürs Bett! :: It's eight o'clock. Time for bed!"]]},{"u":"achten.html","t":"achten","s":"to pay attention to","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Achten Sie bitte auf den Verkehr. :: Please watch the traffic. Achten Sie auf absterbende oder lose Baumteile. :: Watch out for dying or loose parts of trees."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Achten Sie den Verkehr. :: Achten Sie auf den Verkehr."],["notes","Notes","Without auf , jemanden achten means to respect someone. Achtung! on a sign comes from the same verb."]]},{"u":"achtung-liebe-wanderer.html","t":"Achtung! Liebe Wanderer","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Photo"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["transcription","Transcription","Achtung! Liebe Wanderer, der Wanderweg quert hier eine stark befahrene Straße oder verläuft seitlich an dieser entlang. Leider wird hier oft sehr schnell gefahren. Achten Sie bitte auf den Verkehr und überqueren Sie die Straße möglichst zügig und auf direktem Weg. \"Der Sinn des Reisens ist es, an ein Ziel zu kommen, der Sinn des Wanderns, unterwegs zu sein.\" (Theodor Heuss) Deutsch-Luxemburgische Tourist-Information, Tel. [Telefon], [Website]"],["meaning","Meaning","Attention! Dear hikers, here the trail crosses a busy road or runs along its side. Sadly, people often drive very fast here. Please watch the traffic and cross the road as quickly as possible and straight across. The quote by Theodor Heuss, the first Federal President: the point of travelling is to arrive somewhere, the point of hiking is to be on the way. wird ... gefahren is a passive without a subject: it says that driving happens, not who drives."]]},{"u":"achtzehn.html","t":"achtzehn","s":"eighteen","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Baby ist achtzehn Monate alt. :: The baby is eighteen months old."]]},{"u":"achtzehnte.html","t":"achtzehnte","s":"eighteenth","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Heute ist der achtzehnte Juli. :: Today is the eighteenth of July."]]},{"u":"achtzig.html","t":"achtzig","s":"eighty","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Fahrrad kostet achtzig Euro. :: The bike costs eighty euros."]]},{"u":"adjektivendungen.html","t":"Adjektivendungen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","An adjective after the noun has no ending: Der Ball ist . Before a noun it takes an ending, which depends on the article. neu After der, die, das (and dieser, jeder ): mostly -e , and -en in the Akkusativ masculine, in the Dativ and in the plural: der neu . e Ball, den neu en Ball, mit dem neu en Ball, die neu en Bälle After ein, kein, mein : the adjective shows the gender when the article does not: ein neu . er Ball, ein neu es Trikot, eine neu e Tasche With no article, the adjective takes the ending of der, die, das : warm . es Wasser, kalt e Milch"],["simple-german","Simple German","Vor dem Nomen hat das Adjektiv eine Endung: der kleine Sohn, ein kleiner Sohn, ein kleines Kind ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","ein neu Trikot :: ein neues Trikot mit dem neue Ball :: mit dem neuen Ball"]]},{"u":"adresse.html","t":"Adresse","s":"address","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wie ist Ihre Adresse? :: What is your address?"]]},{"u":"akkusativ.html","t":"Akkusativ","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","The Akkusativ is the case of the direct object: the person or thing the action goes to. Only the masculine article changes: der becomes den , ein becomes einen . Ich brauche einen Termin. Ich hole den Sohn ab. Hast du einen Ball? Verbs such as haben, brauchen, abholen, anrufen, besuchen and es gibt take the Akkusativ, and so do the prepositions für, ohne, um, gegen : für . den Trainer"],["simple-german","Simple German","Akkusativ: der wird den , ein wird einen . Ich brauche einen Termin. Nach für, ohne, um, gegen steht der Akkusativ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich brauche ein Termin. :: Ich brauche einen Termin. Das ist für der Trainer. :: Das ist für den Trainer."]]},{"u":"alle.html","t":"alle","s":"everybody, all","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Alle sind da. Wir können anfangen. :: Everybody is here. We can start. Hallo, alle zusammen! :: Hello, everybody!"],["notes","Notes","alle is plural: Alle sind da . For things, alles : Alles ist gut ."]]},{"u":"allein.html","t":"allein","s":"alone, on one's own","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn geht allein zur Schule. :: My son walks to school on his own."],["notes","Notes","In speech also alleine ."]]},{"u":"alles.html","t":"alles","s":"everything","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Trainer schreibt alles in den Chat. :: The coach writes everything in the chat. Heute ist alles voll. :: Everything is full today."],["notes","Notes","alle means everybody or all : Alle Kinder kommen mit."]]},{"u":"als.html","t":"als","s":"when (in the past) / than","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Als ich klein war, habe ich Handball gespielt. :: When I was little, I played handball. Die andere Mannschaft ist stärker als wir. :: The other team is stronger than us."],["notes","Notes","als for one moment in the past, wenn for the present, the future and repeated events. After a comparative, als means than ."]]},{"u":"alt.html","t":"alt","s":"old","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wie alt ist dein Sohn? :: How old is your son? Ich bin 40 Jahre alt. :: I am 40 years old."],["notes","Notes","Age is said with sein and alt : Er ist acht Jahre alt."]]},{"u":"am-elternabend.html","t":"Am Elternabend","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Lehrerin: Guten Abend und herzlich willkommen! Schön, dass Sie alle da sind. :: Good evening and welcome! Nice that you are all here. Lehrerin: Im Dezember machen wir einen Ausflug ins Museum. Der Ausflug kostet fünf Euro. :: In December we are going on a trip to the museum. The trip costs five euros. ich: Entschuldigung, ich habe eine Frage. Wann kommen die Kinder zurück? :: Excuse me, I have a question. When do the children come back? Lehrerin: Um halb eins, also ganz normal. :: At half past twelve, so as usual. Vater: Müssen die Kinder etwas mitbringen? :: Do the children have to bring anything? Lehrerin: Ja, eine Brotdose, etwas zu trinken und warme Kleidung. :: Yes, a lunch box, something to drink and warm clothes. ich: Ich kann gern als Begleitung mitkommen. :: I'm happy to come along as a helper. Lehrerin: Wunderbar, vielen Dank! :: Wonderful, thank you very much!"],["variations","Variations","4 Lehrerin: Wir sind um zwölf Uhr zurück. Sie können die Kinder dann an der Schule abholen. :: We'll be back at twelve. You can pick up the children at school then."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Begleitung : a parent who goes along on a trip to help the teacher."]]},{"u":"am-fahrkartenschalter.html","t":"Am Fahrkartenschalter","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Mitarbeiterin: Guten Tag! Was kann ich für Sie tun? :: Hello! What can I do for you? ich: Eine Fahrkarte nach Berlin, bitte. :: A ticket to Berlin, please. Mitarbeiterin: Wann möchten Sie fahren? :: When would you like to travel? ich: Morgen früh, so um acht Uhr. :: Tomorrow morning, around eight o'clock. Mitarbeiterin: Der Zug fährt um acht Uhr zehn ab. Sie müssen einmal umsteigen. :: The train leaves at ten past eight. You have to change once. ich: Gut. Wann kommt der Zug an? :: Good. When does the train arrive? Mitarbeiterin: Um zwölf Uhr dreißig. Das kostet neunundfünfzig Euro. :: At twelve thirty. That costs fifty-nine euros. ich: Okay. Ich bezahle mit Karte. :: OK. I am paying by card."],["variations","Variations","4 ich: Heute Nachmittag, bitte. :: This afternoon, please."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. abfahren and ankommen are separable: Der Zug fährt um acht ab. Er kommt um zwölf an."]]},{"u":"am-montagetag-der-waermepumpe.html","t":"Am Montagetag der Wärmepumpe","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Monteur: Guten Morgen! Wir kommen wegen der Wärmepumpe. :: Good morning! We are here about the heat pump. ich: Guten Morgen! Kommen Sie herein. Der Heizungsraum ist im Keller. :: Good morning! Come in. The boiler room is in the basement. Monteur: Danke. Sind der Zählerschrank und die Heizkörper frei? :: Thank you. Are the meter cabinet and the radiators free? ich: Ja, wir haben alles frei geräumt. Wie lange dauert die Montage? :: Yes, we have cleared everything. How long does the installation take? Monteur: Zwei bis drei Tage. In dieser Zeit bleiben Heizung und Warmwasser kalt. :: Two to three days. During that time heating and hot water stay cold. ich: Alles klar. Wann machen wir die Abnahme? :: All right. When do we do the acceptance? Monteur: Am letzten Tag. Dann gehen wir alles zusammen durch, und Sie unterschreiben das Protokoll. :: On the last day. Then we go through everything together and you sign the record."],["variations","Variations","4 ich: Ja, alles ist frei. Brauchen Sie Strom oder Wasser von uns? :: Yes, everything is free. Do you need electricity or water from us? 5 Monteur: Heute stellen wir nur die Außeneinheit auf, morgen kommt der Rest. :: Today we only set up the outdoor unit; the rest comes tomorrow. 7 Monteur: Das macht die Bauleitung. Sie meldet sich bei Ihnen. :: The site manager does that. They will get in touch with you."],["notes","Notes","A model to practise before the installation day; it did not happen like this. frei räumen : to clear a space so the workers can reach it."]]},{"u":"ampel.html","t":"Ampel","s":"traffic light","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","An der Ampel gehen Sie links. :: At the traffic light, go left."]]},{"u":"an-schultagen-halteverbot.html","t":"An Schultagen Halteverbot","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Photo"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["transcription","Transcription","an Schultagen von 7-9h von 11-16h ausgenommen Linienbusse"],["meaning","Meaning","Three signs on one pole: The red triangle with two children: watch out, children (a school is near). The blue sign with a red cross: absolute no stopping ( absolutes Halteverbot ). You may not even stop for a moment. The arrow shows the direction in which the ban applies from the sign. The extra plate ( Zusatzzeichen ): the ban only applies on school days, from 7 to 9 and from 11 to 16 o'clock. Scheduled public buses ( Linienbusse ) are allowed to stop."]]},{"u":"an.html","t":"an","s":"at / on","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Treffpunkt ist um neun Uhr am Vereinsheim. :: The meeting point is at nine o'clock at the clubhouse."],["notes","Notes","am is an dem . Days take am : am Montag ."]]},{"u":"anfangen.html","t":"anfangen","s":"to begin / to start","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Weißt du, wann der Elternabend anfängt? :: Do you know when the parents' evening starts? Wir fangen um sechs Uhr an. :: We start at six o'clock."]]},{"u":"ankommen.html","t":"ankommen","s":"to arrive","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Zug kommt um zehn Uhr an. :: The train arrives at ten o'clock."]]},{"u":"anlagendruck.html","t":"Anlagendruck","s":"system pressure","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Anlagendruck sollte zwischen 1,5 und 2 bar liegen. :: The system pressure should be between 1.5 and 2 bar. Liegt der Anlagendruck unter 1,5 bar, füllen Sie Wasser nach. :: If the system pressure is below 1.5 bar, top up water."],["notes","Notes","die Anlage here is the installation (the heating system). In a letter, die Anlage is an enclosure: in der Anlage finden Sie..."]]},{"u":"anmeldung.html","t":"Anmeldung","s":"registration, sign-up","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Zur Anmeldung: Der Preis wird per Überweisung bezahlt. :: About registration: the price is paid by bank transfer. Die Überweisung gilt als verbindliche Anmeldung. :: The transfer counts as a binding registration."],["notes","Notes","verbindlich means binding: once you have signed up, you have to pay."]]},{"u":"anruf-im-sekretariat.html","t":"Anruf im Sekretariat","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Sekretärin: Grundschule, Sekretariat, guten Morgen. :: Primary school, office, good morning. ich: Guten Morgen. Hier ist Familie B. Meine Tochter geht in die Klasse 2b. :: Good morning. This is the B. family. My daughter is in class 2b. Sekretärin: Ja, was kann ich für Sie tun? :: Yes, what can I do for you? ich: Meine Tochter ist krank. Sie hat Fieber und bleibt heute zu Hause. :: My daughter is ill. She has a temperature and is staying at home today. Sekretärin: Oh, gute Besserung! Wie lange bleibt sie zu Hause? :: Oh, get well soon! How long will she stay at home? ich: Ich weiß es noch nicht. Wir gehen heute zum Kinderarzt. :: I don't know yet. We are going to the paediatrician today. Sekretärin: Gut. Bitte rufen Sie wieder an, wenn sie länger krank ist. :: All right. Please call again if she is ill for longer. ich: Ja, mache ich. Auf Wiederhören! :: Yes, I will. Goodbye!"],["variations","Variations","5 Sekretärin: Danke für den Anruf. Ich sage der Lehrerin Bescheid. :: Thanks for the call. I'll let the teacher know."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Call before school starts. Many schools also accept an e-mail or a message in the school app. Auf Wiederhören is the goodbye of the phone."]]},{"u":"anrufen.html","t":"anrufen","s":"to phone","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Lehrerin hat heute angerufen. :: The teacher called today. Bitte rufen Sie wieder an. :: Please call again."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich anrufe die Schule. :: Ich rufe die Schule an."]]},{"u":"antwort-trainer-training-bei-hitze.html","t":"Antwort des Trainers: Training bei Hitze","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Text"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Hallo, ist ok, für alle zur Info: Hello, that's OK. For everyone's information: Wir werden nur lockere Übungen machen und ein paar Standards, keine großartigen anstrengenden Dinge. We will only do light exercises and a few set pieces, nothing very strenuous. Gruß Regards"],["notes","Notes","Standards in football are set pieces: free kicks, corners, throw-ins. locker here means light, relaxed. keine großartigen ... Dinge is colloquial for \"nothing big\". für alle zur Info tells you the coach answers one parent but writes for the whole group."]]},{"u":"antworten.html","t":"antworten","s":"to answer","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte antworten Sie bis Freitag. :: Please answer by Friday."],["notes","Notes","The person is in the Dativ: Ich antworte dir."]]},{"u":"anziehen.html","t":"anziehen","s":"to put on / to dress","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Zieh dich bitte an! :: Please get dressed! Ich ziehe die Jacke an. :: I put on the jacket."],["notes","Notes","sich anziehen : to get dressed. Zieh dich an! to a child."]]},{"u":"apfel.html","t":"Apfel","s":"apple","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ein Kilo Äpfel, bitte. :: A kilo of apples, please."]]},{"u":"arbeit.html","t":"Arbeit","s":"work / job","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Nach der Arbeit hole ich die Kinder ab. :: After work I pick up the children."]]},{"u":"arbeiten.html","t":"arbeiten","s":"to work","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich muss bis sechs arbeiten. :: I have to work until six. Können Sie morgen von zu Hause arbeiten? :: Can you work from home tomorrow?"]]},{"u":"arzt.html","t":"Arzt","s":"doctor","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich gehe heute zum Arzt. :: I am going to the doctor today."],["notes","Notes","A woman doctor is die Ärztin ."]]},{"u":"aua.html","t":"aua","s":"ouch","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Aua! Mein Knie tut weh. :: Ouch! My knee hurts."]]},{"u":"auch.html","t":"auch","s":"also / too","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Möchtest du auch einen Kaffee? :: Would you like a coffee too? Ich dich auch. :: Me too."]]},{"u":"auf-der-tribuene.html","t":"Auf der Tribüne","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Vater: Hallo! Spielt deine Tochter heute auch? :: Hi! Is your daughter playing today too? ich: Ja, sie ist die Nummer sieben, im Tor. :: Yes, she's number seven, in goal. Vater: Toll! Wie steht es? :: Great! What's the score? ich: Zwölf zu zehn für uns. Aber die andere Mannschaft ist sehr stark. :: Twelve to ten for us. But the other team is very strong. Vater: Oh, ein Foul! Das war doch kein Siebenmeter! :: Oh, a foul! That was no penalty! ich: Doch, der Schiedsrichter hat recht. :: Yes it was, the referee is right. Vater: Na ja. Noch fünf Minuten. Hoffentlich gewinnen wir! :: Oh well. Five more minutes. Hopefully we'll win!"],["variations","Variations","4 ich: Zehn zu zehn. Es ist sehr spannend! :: Ten all. It's very exciting!"],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Siebenmeter is the penalty throw in handball. Doch says yes against a negative sentence."]]},{"u":"auf-eigene-gefahr.html","t":"auf eigene Gefahr","s":"at your own risk","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Sie betreten den Wald auf eigene Gefahr. :: You enter the forest at your own risk. Unbefugtes Parken auf eigene Gefahr! :: Parking without permission at your own risk! Benutzung auf eigene Gefahr. :: Use at your own risk."],["usage","Usage","On signs and notices: the owner says they are not responsible if something happens to you or your car. Always eigene without article."]]},{"u":"auf-wiederhoeren.html","t":"Auf Wiederhören!","s":"Goodbye! (on the phone)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Danke, auf Wiederhören! :: Thank you, goodbye! Auf Wiedersehen! :: Goodbye! (face to face)"],["usage","Usage","On the phone you hear each other again, so Wiederhören ."]]},{"u":"auf.html","t":"auf","s":"on / onto","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Spiel ist auf unserem Platz. :: The match is on our pitch."]]},{"u":"aufmachen.html","t":"aufmachen","s":"to open","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mach bitte das Fenster auf! :: Please open the window! Die Bäckerei macht um sechs Uhr auf. :: The bakery opens at six o'clock."]]},{"u":"aufraeumen.html","t":"aufräumen","s":"to tidy up","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Räum bitte dein Zimmer auf! :: Please tidy up your room!"]]},{"u":"aufstehen.html","t":"aufstehen","s":"to get up","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir stehen um halb sieben auf. :: We get up at half past six."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich aufstehe um sechs. :: Ich stehe um sechs auf."]]},{"u":"aus.html","t":"aus","s":"from / out of","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Kollegin kommt aus Spanien. :: My colleague comes from Spain."],["notes","Notes","aus for where someone comes from: Ich komme aus Spanien."]]},{"u":"ausfallen.html","t":"ausfallen","s":"to be cancelled","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wegen Regen fällt das Training heute leider aus. :: Because of rain, training is cancelled today."]]},{"u":"ausflug.html","t":"Ausflug","s":"trip / outing","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Im Dezember machen wir einen Ausflug ins Museum. :: In December we are going on a trip to the museum."]]},{"u":"ausgenommen.html","t":"ausgenommen","s":"except","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Halteverbot gilt für alle, ausgenommen Linienbusse. :: The no-stopping rule applies to everyone except scheduled buses. Die Durchfahrt ist verboten, Anlieger ausgenommen. :: No through traffic, residents excepted."],["notes","Notes","Very common on extra plates under traffic signs. It can come before or after the noun. Anlieger frei says the same thing for residents."]]},{"u":"ausrichten.html","t":"ausrichten","s":"to host, to organise (an event)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am JSG-Tag richten alle teilnehmenden Mannschaften ein Spiel aus. :: On JSG day all participating teams host a match. Kannst du dem Trainer etwas ausrichten? :: Can you pass a message on to the coach?"],["notes","Notes","Two meanings: to host an event ( ein Turnier ausrichten ), and to pass on a message ( jemandem etwas ausrichten , + Dativ for the person)."]]},{"u":"ausseneinheit.html","t":"Außeneinheit","s":"outdoor unit","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Rund um die Außeneinheit muss ein Meter frei bleiben. :: One metre around the outdoor unit must stay clear. Im Winter entferne ich den Schnee rund um die Außeneinheit. :: In winter I remove the snow around the outdoor unit."]]},{"u":"aussteigen.html","t":"aussteigen","s":"to get off (a vehicle)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir steigen am Bahnhof aus. :: We get off at the station."]]},{"u":"auto.html","t":"Auto","s":"car","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Auto steht vor dem Haus. :: The car is parked in front of the house."]]},{"u":"backup-bedienelement.html","t":"Backup-Bedienelement","s":"backup control unit","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B2"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wenn man das Backup-Bedienelement anschließt, erlischt die Garantie. :: If you connect the backup control unit, the warranty expires."],["notes","Notes","erlöschen ( erlischt , ist erloschen ) is used for rights and contracts that end: die Garantie erlischt ."]]},{"u":"baeckerei.html","t":"Bäckerei","s":"bakery","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Bäckerei macht um sechs Uhr auf. :: The bakery opens at six o'clock."],["notes","Notes","Also der Bäcker : Ich gehe zum Bäcker."]]},{"u":"bahnhof.html","t":"Bahnhof","s":"station","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wo ist der Bahnhof, bitte? :: Where is the station, please?"]]},{"u":"bald.html","t":"bald","s":"soon","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bis bald! :: See you soon!"]]},{"u":"ball.html","t":"Ball","s":"ball","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Ball ist im Tor. :: The ball is in the goal."]]},{"u":"beantragen.html","t":"beantragen","s":"to apply for","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Eine der Vertragsparteien wird die Förderung innerhalb von 14 Tagen nach Vertragsschluss beantragen. :: One of the parties to the contract will apply for the subsidy within 14 days of signing. Wir haben die Förderung bei der KfW beantragt. :: We have applied for the subsidy from the KfW. Ich beantrage einen Grundbuchauszug. :: I am applying for an extract from the land register."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Wir haben für die Förderung beantragt. :: Wir haben die Förderung beantragt. Ich antrage die Förderung. :: Ich beantrage die Förderung."],["notes","Notes","be- is never separated: ich beantrage , beantragt . The thing you apply for is in the accusative, without für . The same with a noun: einen Antrag stellen , einen Antrag auf Förderung stellen ."]]},{"u":"beeil-dich.html","t":"Beeil dich!","s":"Hurry up!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Beeilt euch, der Bus kommt! :: Hurry up, the bus is coming! (to several) Wir müssen uns beeilen. :: We have to hurry."],["usage","Usage","To a child in the morning. sich beeilen is reflexive."]]},{"u":"bei-bedarf.html","t":"bei Bedarf","s":"if needed","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Der Zug hält dort nur bei Bedarf. :: The train only stops there on request. Bei Bedarf rufen Sie mich bitte an. :: Call me if needed."],["usage","Usage","In a train, Halt bei Bedarf means the train only stops when someone presses the stop button ( Haltewunsch ) or waits on the platform. In letters and offices it means \"if you need it\"."]]},{"u":"bei.html","t":"bei","s":"at / with","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Paket ist bei mir. :: The parcel is at my place."],["notes","Notes","beim Arzt : at the doctor's. bei mir : at my place."]]},{"u":"beim-baecker.html","t":"Beim Bäcker","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Verkäuferin: Guten Morgen! Was bekommen Sie? :: Good morning! What would you like? ich: Guten Morgen! Vier Brötchen, bitte. :: Good morning! Four rolls, please. Verkäuferin: Gern. Noch etwas? :: Sure. Anything else? ich: Ja, ein Brot, bitte. Ist das Brot frisch? :: Yes, a loaf of bread, please. Is the bread fresh? Verkäuferin: Ja, ganz frisch. Das macht fünf Euro zwanzig. :: Yes, very fresh. That comes to five euros twenty. ich: Hier, bitte. Ich bezahle mit Karte. :: Here you are. I am paying by card. Verkäuferin: Danke schön! Schönen Tag noch! :: Thank you! Have a nice day! ich: Danke, Ihnen auch. Tschüss! :: Thank you, you too. Bye!"],["variations","Variations","4 ich: Nein, danke. Das ist alles. :: No, thanks. That is all. 6 ich: Hier sind zehn Euro. :: Here are ten euros."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Was bekommen Sie? is how shop staff ask what you want. You answer with the thing and bitte . Das macht ... gives the total price."]]},{"u":"bekommen.html","t":"bekommen","s":"to get, to receive","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich bekomme vier Brötchen, bitte. :: I'll have four bread rolls, please."],["notes","Notes","A false friend: bekommen is to get , not to become . To become is werden ."]]},{"u":"bescheid-geben.html","t":"Bescheid geben","s":"to let someone know","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Ich wollte kurz Bescheid geben, dass er heute nicht kommt. :: I just wanted to let you know that he isn't coming today. Gib mir bitte Bescheid, wenn das Training ausfällt. :: Please let me know if training is cancelled. Geben Sie uns bitte bis Freitag Bescheid. :: Please let us know by Friday. (formal)"],["usage","Usage","The usual way to tell the coach that your child is missing. The person gets the dative: mir, dir, Ihnen, euch . Bescheid sagen means the same."]]},{"u":"bescheid-sagen.html","t":"Bescheid sagen","s":"to let someone know","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Sag mir Bescheid! :: Let me know! Danke, dass Sie Bescheid sagen. :: Thank you for letting me know. Wer keine Zeit hat, sagt mir bitte bis Montag Bescheid. :: Whoever has no time, please let me know by Monday."],["usage","Usage","When you promise to tell someone later, or thank someone for telling you. The person is in the Dativ: mir , dir , Ihnen ."]]},{"u":"besonders.html","t":"besonders","s":"especially / particularly","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Spiel war besonders spannend. :: The match was particularly exciting."],["notes","Notes","Before a noun the adjective is besondere : Heute ist ein besonderer Tag."]]},{"u":"besprechung-verschoben.html","t":"Besprechung verschoben","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Text"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Hallo zusammen, Hello everyone, die Besprechung am Montag ist leider verschoben. Monday's meeting has unfortunately been postponed. Wir treffen uns jetzt am Dienstag um 14 Uhr im Raum 3. We now meet on Tuesday at 2 pm in room 3. Bitte bringt eure Zahlen vom Oktober mit. Please bring your figures from October. Wer keine Zeit hat, sagt mir bitte bis Montag Bescheid. Whoever has no time, please let me know by Monday. Viele Grüße Best regards Die Teamleiterin The team leader"],["notes","Notes","A model text, written for this course. A real one names people: replace them with placeholders before you save it. verschoben is the participle of verschieben : to postpone. In Germany, times at work are written with the 24-hour clock: 14 Uhr is 2 pm."]]},{"u":"besprechung.html","t":"Besprechung","s":"meeting","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Um zehn habe ich eine Besprechung. :: At ten I have a meeting."]]},{"u":"bestellen.html","t":"bestellen","s":"to order","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich bestelle eine Pizza. :: I am ordering a pizza."]]},{"u":"besuchen.html","t":"besuchen","s":"to visit","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Wochenende besuchen wir die Großeltern. :: At the weekend we visit the grandparents."],["notes","Notes","Verbs with be- have no ge- in the Perfekt: besucht ."]]},{"u":"betreten.html","t":"betreten","s":"to enter","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Sie betreten den Wald auf eigene Gefahr. :: You enter the forest at your own risk. Unbefugtes Betreten ist verboten. :: Entry without permission is forbidden."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich betrete in den Wald. :: Ich betrete den Wald."],["notes","Notes","betreten takes a direct object, without in . It sounds formal: in everyday speech you say in den Wald gehen . On signs: Betreten verboten , Rasen nicht betreten ."]]},{"u":"bett.html","t":"Bett","s":"bed","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Es ist acht Uhr. Zeit fürs Bett! :: It is eight o'clock. Time for bed!"]]},{"u":"bezahlen.html","t":"bezahlen","s":"to pay","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich bezahle mit Karte. :: I am paying by card. Kann ich bar bezahlen? :: Can I pay cash?"]]},{"u":"billig.html","t":"billig","s":"cheap","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Im Supermarkt ist der Kaffee billiger. :: Coffee is cheaper in the supermarket."],["notes","Notes","günstig sounds more positive: good value."]]},{"u":"bis-morgen.html","t":"Bis morgen!","s":"See you tomorrow!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Bis später! :: See you later! Bis bald! :: See you soon! Bis Samstag! :: See you on Saturday!"],["usage","Usage","bis plus a time says when you will see each other again."]]},{"u":"bis.html","t":"bis","s":"until / by","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte geben Sie den Zettel bis Dienstag zurück. :: Please return the slip by Tuesday. Ich muss bis sechs arbeiten. :: I have to work until six."],["notes","Notes","Usually without an article: bis Montag , bis acht Uhr . With an article it needs zu : bis zum Ende ."]]},{"u":"bisschen.html","t":"bisschen","s":"a little, a bit","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich spreche ein bisschen Deutsch. :: I speak a little German. Ich bin ein bisschen müde. :: I am a bit tired."],["notes","Notes","Almost always with ein : ein bisschen ."]]},{"u":"bitte.html","t":"bitte","s":"please / you're welcome","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Noch fünf Minuten, bitte! :: Five more minutes, please! Ja, bitte. Was gibt's? :: Yes, please. What is it?"],["notes","Notes","Bitte? alone means Pardon? . Bitte! also answers Danke!"]]},{"u":"blau.html","t":"blau","s":"blue","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Himmel ist heute blau. :: The sky is blue today."]]},{"u":"bleiben.html","t":"bleiben","s":"to stay","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Sie bleibt heute zu Hause. :: She is staying at home today."]]},{"u":"bleibt-sportlich.html","t":"Bleibt sportlich!","s":"stay sporty (sports-club sign-off)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Bis dahin, bleibt sportlich! :: Until then, stay sporty! Mit sportlichen Grüßen :: With sporting regards"],["usage","Usage","A friendly closing in sports clubs, like Viele Grüße . Mit sportlichen Grüßen is the written, slightly more formal version."]]},{"u":"brauchen.html","t":"brauchen","s":"to need","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich brauche heute einen Termin. :: I need an appointment today. Wir brauchen noch zwei Autos. :: We still need two cars."]]},{"u":"braun.html","t":"braun","s":"brown","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Tisch ist braun. :: The table is brown."]]},{"u":"bringen.html","t":"bringen","s":"to bring, to take","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich bringe die Kinder zur Schule. :: I take the children to school."]]},{"u":"broetchen.html","t":"Brötchen","s":"bread roll","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Zum Frühstück gibt es Brötchen. :: There are bread rolls for breakfast."],["notes","Notes","Regional words for the same thing: Semmel in the south, Schrippe in Berlin."]]},{"u":"brot.html","t":"Brot","s":"bread","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich kaufe ein Brot und vier Brötchen. :: I buy a loaf of bread and four rolls."]]},{"u":"brotdose.html","t":"Brotdose","s":"lunch box","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Hast du deine Brotdose? :: Do you have your lunch box?"]]},{"u":"bruder.html","t":"Bruder","s":"brother","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Bruder wohnt in Spanien. :: My brother lives in Spain."]]},{"u":"buch.html","t":"Buch","s":"book","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Buch liegt auf dem Tisch. :: The book is on the table."]]},{"u":"buchstabieren.html","t":"buchstabieren","s":"to spell","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Können Sie das bitte buchstabieren? :: Can you spell that, please?"],["notes","Notes","Verbs in -ieren have no ge- : buchstabiert ."]]},{"u":"buero.html","t":"Büro","s":"office","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Morgen arbeite ich nicht im Büro. Ich arbeite zu Hause. :: Tomorrow I am not working in the office. I am working at home."]]},{"u":"bus.html","t":"Bus","s":"bus","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Bus kommt um acht Uhr. :: The bus comes at eight o'clock. Ich fahre mit dem Bus zur Arbeit. :: I go to work by bus."]]},{"u":"cafe.html","t":"Café","s":"café","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir treffen uns im Café. :: We meet at the café."]]},{"u":"chat-der-fussballeltern.html","t":"Chat der Fußballeltern","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Text"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Trainer: Hallo zusammen! Wegen Regen fällt das Training heute leider aus. Coach: Hello everyone! Because of the rain, training is cancelled today. Trainer: Am Samstag spielen wir um zehn Uhr in der Nachbarstadt. Treffpunkt ist um neun Uhr am Vereinsheim. Coach: On Saturday we play at ten o'clock in the neighbouring town. The meeting point is at nine o'clock at the clubhouse. Trainer: Wer kann fahren? Wir brauchen noch zwei Autos. Coach: Who can drive? We still need two cars. Mutter: Ich kann fahren und habe drei Plätze frei. Mother: I can drive and have three free seats. Vater: Mein Sohn ist krank und kann leider nicht mitspielen. Father: My son is ill and unfortunately cannot play. Trainer: Danke euch! Gute Besserung an deinen Sohn. Coach: Thank you all! Get well soon to your son."],["notes","Notes","A model text, written for this course. A real one names people: replace them with placeholders before you save it. fällt aus comes from ausfallen , a separable verb: to be cancelled. To answer, one short line is enough: Ich kann auch fahren. or Mein Sohn kommt."]]},{"u":"chefin.html","t":"Chefin","s":"boss (woman)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich frage die Chefin: Kann ich heute früher gehen? :: I ask the boss: can I leave earlier today?"],["notes","Notes","A man is der Chef , plural die Chefs ."]]},{"u":"da.html","t":"da","s":"there / then","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Er muss um halb zehn da sein. :: He has to be there at half past nine. Am Vormittag nicht, da hat mein Sohn ein Spiel. :: Not in the morning, my son has a match then."],["notes","Notes","da sein : to be there, to be present."]]},{"u":"danach.html","t":"danach","s":"afterwards","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Danach essen wir zusammen Pizza. :: Afterwards we eat pizza together."]]},{"u":"danke.html","t":"danke","s":"thank you / thanks","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Danke, das ist nett. :: Thanks, that's kind. Vielen Dank! :: Thank you very much!"],["notes","Notes","The answer is Bitte! or Gern geschehen!"]]},{"u":"dann.html","t":"dann","s":"then","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Zuerst die Hausaufgaben, dann darfst du spielen. :: Homework first, then you may play."]]},{"u":"darf-ich-kurz-stoeren.html","t":"Darf ich kurz stören?","s":"May I interrupt for a moment?","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Entschuldigung, darf ich kurz stören? :: Excuse me, may I interrupt for a moment? Haben Sie kurz Zeit? :: Do you have a moment?"],["usage","Usage","Before you ask a boss or a teacher something, at the door of their office."]]},{"u":"das-tut-mir-leid.html","t":"Das tut mir leid.","s":"I'm sorry.","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Oh, das tut mir leid! :: Oh, I'm sorry! Es tut mir leid, ich bin zu spät. :: I'm sorry, I'm late."],["usage","Usage","When something bad happened, or to apologise. For a small thing, Entschuldigung! is enough."]]},{"u":"das-wetter-am-wochenende.html","t":"Das Wetter am Wochenende","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Freund: Was machst du am Samstag? :: What are you doing on Saturday? ich: Ich weiß noch nicht. Wie ist das Wetter? :: I don't know yet. What is the weather like? Freund: Am Samstag ist es warm und sonnig. :: On Saturday it is warm and sunny. ich: Toll! Dann gehen wir schwimmen. :: Great! Then let's go swimming. Freund: Gute Idee! Und am Sonntag? :: Good idea! And on Sunday? ich: Am Sonntag kommt Regen. Dann bleiben wir zu Hause. :: On Sunday rain is coming. Then we will stay at home."],["variations","Variations","3 Freund: Am Samstag ist es kalt und es regnet. :: On Saturday it is cold and it rains. 4 ich: Schade! Dann gehen wir ins Kino. :: Pity! Then let's go to the cinema."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Weather sentences start with es : Es ist warm. Es regnet."]]},{"u":"das.html","t":"das","s":"the (neuter)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Training fällt aus. :: Training is cancelled."],["notes","Notes","Neuter: das , das , dem . das also means that : Das ist nett."]]},{"u":"dass.html","t":"dass","s":"that","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Danke, dass Sie Bescheid sagen. :: Thank you for letting me know."]]},{"u":"dativ.html","t":"Dativ","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","The Dativ is the case of the person who receives or is helped, and the case after mit, bei, nach, von, zu, seit, aus . masculine feminine neuter plural Nominativ der / ein die / eine das / ein die Dativ dem / einem der / einer dem / einem den (+ n) Ich spiele mit meinem Sohn. Wir gehen zum Arzt. Ich helfe dir . Ich gebe den Kinder n einen Apfel. Short forms: zum = zu dem , zur = zu der , beim = bei dem , vom = von dem ."],["simple-german","Simple German","Nach mit, bei, nach, von, zu, seit, aus steht der Dativ: mit dem Ball, mit der Mannschaft . Verben wie helfen haben den Dativ: Ich helfe dir ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich spiele mit mein Sohn. :: Ich spiele mit meinem Sohn. Wir fahren zu die Halle. :: Wir fahren zur Halle."]]},{"u":"dauern.html","t":"dauern","s":"to last, to take (time)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wie lange dauert das? :: How long does that take?"]]},{"u":"dein.html","t":"dein","s":"your (informal)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Hast du deine Brotdose? :: Do you have your lunch box?"],["notes","Notes","Endings like ein ."]]},{"u":"denn.html","t":"denn","s":"because","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich komme nicht, denn ich muss arbeiten. :: I am not coming because I have to work."],["notes","Notes","denn and weil both mean because . After denn the verb stays in position 2."]]},{"u":"der-die-das.html","t":"Der, die, das","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Every German noun has a gender: masculine der , feminine die or neuter das . In the plural all nouns take die . Learn each noun with its article: der Ball, die Mannschaft, das Tor . Some endings help: -ung , -heit , -keit and -in are always die ( die Wohnung , die Lehrerin ); -chen is always das ( das Mädchen ). The site colours nouns by gender: blue der , red die , green das , orange plural."],["simple-german","Simple German","Jedes Nomen hat einen Artikel: der , die oder das . Im Plural ist der Artikel immer die . Lerne das Nomen immer mit Artikel."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","die Training :: das Training der Wohnung :: die Wohnung"]]},{"u":"der.html","t":"der","s":"the (masculine)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Trainer schreibt alles in den Chat. :: The coach writes everything in the chat."],["notes","Notes","Masculine: der (Nominativ), den (Akkusativ), dem (Dativ). der is also the Dativ of die : mit der Mannschaft ."]]},{"u":"deshalb.html","t":"deshalb","s":"that is why","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn ist krank, deshalb bleibt er zu Hause. :: My son is ill, that is why he is staying at home."]]},{"u":"die-neue-nachbarin.html","t":"Die neue Nachbarin","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Nachbarin: Guten Tag! Ich bin die neue Nachbarin. Ich wohne im zweiten Stock. :: Hello! I'm the new neighbour. I live on the second floor. ich: Guten Tag und herzlich willkommen! Wir wohnen hier im Erdgeschoss. :: Hello and welcome! We live here on the ground floor. Nachbarin: Freut mich. Wohnen Sie schon lange hier? :: Nice to meet you. Have you lived here long? ich: Ja, schon drei Jahre. Das Haus ist sehr ruhig. :: Yes, three years already. The house is very quiet. Nachbarin: Wann kommt hier die Müllabfuhr? :: When does the rubbish collection come here? ich: Am Mittwoch. Die Mülltonnen stehen im Hof. :: On Wednesday. The bins are in the yard. Nachbarin: Danke schön! Einen schönen Tag noch. :: Thank you! Have a nice day. ich: Danke, gleichfalls! :: Thanks, you too!"],["variations","Variations","4 ich: Nein, erst ein Jahr. Die Nachbarn sind sehr nett. :: No, only one year. The neighbours are very nice."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. seit plus the present tense: Wir wohnen seit drei Jahren hier means we have lived here for three years . The German Erdgeschoss is the ground floor; der erste Stock is the floor above it."]]},{"u":"die.html","t":"die","s":"the (feminine / plural)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Lehrerin hat angerufen. :: The teacher called. Die Kinder spielen im Garten. :: The children are playing in the garden."],["notes","Notes","Feminine and all plurals. The Dativ plural is den and the noun gets -n : mit den Kindern ."]]},{"u":"dieser.html","t":"dieser","s":"this","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Diese Woche fährt die Oma. :: This week grandma is driving. Dieses Spiel war toll. :: This match was great."],["notes","Notes","Endings like der, die, das : dieser, diese, dieses ."]]},{"u":"doch.html","t":"doch","s":"yes (contradicting) / just","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kommst du nicht? Doch, ich komme! :: Aren't you coming? Yes, I am coming!"],["notes","Notes","Doch answers yes to a negative question or sentence. In Frag doch mal! it makes a suggestion softer."]]},{"u":"dort.html","t":"dort","s":"there","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Café am Marktplatz? Dort treffen wir uns. :: The café on the market square? We'll meet there."]]},{"u":"draussen.html","t":"draußen","s":"outside","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Kinder spielen draußen im Garten. :: The children are playing outside in the garden."]]},{"u":"drei.html","t":"drei","s":"three","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe drei Plätze frei. :: I have three free seats."]]},{"u":"dreissig.html","t":"dreißig","s":"thirty","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das kostet dreißig Euro. :: That costs thirty euros."],["notes","Notes","With ß , not z : dreißig . The other tens end in -zig ."]]},{"u":"dreissigste.html","t":"dreißigste","s":"thirtieth","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am dreißigsten bezahle ich die Miete. :: On the thirtieth I pay the rent."]]},{"u":"dreizehn.html","t":"dreizehn","s":"thirteen","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Tochter ist dreizehn Jahre alt. :: My daughter is thirteen years old."]]},{"u":"dreizehnte.html","t":"dreizehnte","s":"thirteenth","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Heute ist der dreizehnte März. :: Today is the thirteenth of March."]]},{"u":"drinnen.html","t":"drinnen","s":"inside","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Es regnet. Die Kinder spielen drinnen. :: It is raining. The children are playing inside."],["notes","Notes","The opposite is draußen ."]]},{"u":"dritte.html","t":"dritte","s":"third","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am dritten Tag ist er wieder gesund. :: On the third day he is healthy again."],["notes","Notes","Irregular, like erste : not dreite ."]]},{"u":"du.html","t":"du","s":"you (informal)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich rufe dich morgen an. :: I will call you tomorrow. Ich helfe dir gern. :: I am happy to help you."],["notes","Notes","du for children, family, friends, and often parents at school and in the sports club."]]},{"u":"duerfen.html","t":"dürfen","s":"may / to be allowed to","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Darf ich noch zehn Minuten fernsehen? :: May I watch TV for ten more minutes?"],["notes","Notes","nicht dürfen means must not : Du darfst hier nicht spielen ."]]},{"u":"dunkel.html","t":"dunkel","s":"dark","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Im Winter ist es um fünf Uhr schon dunkel. :: In winter it is already dark at five o'clock."],["notes","Notes","The comparative drops the e : dunkler , not dunkeler ."]]},{"u":"durch.html","t":"durch","s":"through","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir gehen durch den Park zur Schule. :: We walk through the park to school."]]},{"u":"durst.html","t":"Durst","s":"thirst","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Hast du Durst? :: Are you thirsty?"]]},{"u":"duschen.html","t":"duschen","s":"to shower","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich dusche am Morgen. :: I shower in the morning."]]},{"u":"eigentlich.html","t":"eigentlich","s":"actually","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Was machst du eigentlich am Wochenende? :: So what are you doing at the weekend? Eigentlich habe ich keine Zeit, aber ich komme. :: Actually I have no time, but I'll come."],["notes","Notes","In a question it makes it softer and more personal."]]},{"u":"ein-paket-fuer-die-nachbarn.html","t":"Ein Paket für die Nachbarn","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Guten Abend! Ich habe ein Paket für Sie. Der Paketbote hat es heute Morgen bei mir abgegeben. :: Good evening! I have a parcel for you. The delivery man left it with me this morning. Nachbar: Oh, vielen Dank! Das ist sehr nett von Ihnen. :: Oh, thank you very much! That's very kind of you. ich: Gern geschehen. :: You're welcome. Nachbar: Übrigens, am Samstag feiern wir den Geburtstag von unserem Sohn. Es wird vielleicht ein bisschen laut. :: By the way, on Saturday we are celebrating our son's birthday. It might get a bit loud. ich: Kein Problem. Bis wann geht die Party? :: No problem. Until when does the party go on? Nachbar: Bis zehn Uhr, versprochen! :: Until ten o'clock, I promise! ich: Dann viel Spaß beim Feiern! :: Then have fun celebrating!"],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Accepting a parcel for a neighbour is normal in Germany. The delivery service leaves a card in the neighbour's letter box."]]},{"u":"ein-tor-schiessen.html","t":"ein Tor schießen","s":"to score a goal","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Er hat zwei Tore geschossen. :: He scored two goals. Wer hat das Tor geschossen? :: Who scored the goal?"],["usage","Usage","In football. In handball people say ein Tor werfen : to throw a goal."]]},{"u":"ein.html","t":"ein","s":"a / an","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe ein Paket für Sie. :: I have a parcel for you."],["notes","Notes","ein for der and das words, eine for die words. Akkusativ masculine: einen Termin ."]]},{"u":"einen-termin-vereinbaren.html","t":"einen Termin vereinbaren","s":"to make an appointment","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Ich möchte einen Termin vereinbaren. :: I would like to make an appointment. Ich brauche einen Termin beim Kinderarzt. :: I need an appointment with the paediatrician."],["usage","Usage","On the phone with a practice, the school or an office."]]},{"u":"einfach.html","t":"einfach","s":"simple / easy","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Aufgabe ist ganz einfach. :: The task is very easy. Komm doch einfach mit! :: Just come along!"],["notes","Notes","As a particle, einfach means just : Ruf einfach an!"]]},{"u":"einkaufen.html","t":"einkaufen","s":"to go shopping","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Nach der Arbeit kaufe ich schnell ein. :: After work I do some quick shopping."]]},{"u":"einkaufsliste.html","t":"Einkaufsliste","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Ich gehe gleich einkaufen. Was brauchen wir? :: I am going shopping soon. What do we need? Kind: Wir haben keine Milch mehr. :: We have no more milk. ich: Gut, Milch. Und was noch? :: OK, milk. And what else? Kind: Äpfel und Käse. Und ein Kuchen für Sonntag! :: Apples and cheese. And a cake for Sunday! ich: Ja, gut. Am Sonntag kommt die Oma. :: Yes, OK. Grandma is coming on Sunday. Kind: Super! Ich helfe dir. :: Great! I'll help you. ich: Ja, klar. Zieh deine Schuhe und deine Jacke an! :: Yes, of course. Put on your shoes and your jacket!"],["variations","Variations","6 Kind: Toll! Ich mache die Liste. :: Great! I'll make the list."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. keine ... mehr : no more. Wir haben keine Milch mehr."]]},{"u":"einladen.html","t":"einladen","s":"to invite","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich lade dich und deine Familie herzlich ein! :: I warmly invite you and your family!"]]},{"u":"einladung-zum-geburtstag.html","t":"Einladung zum Geburtstag","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Text"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Hallo! Wie geht es dir? Wir haben uns so lange nicht gesehen. Hi! How are you? We haven't seen each other for so long. Am Freitag mache ich eine kleine Party, weil ich Geburtstag habe. On Friday I'm having a small party because it's my birthday. Ich lade dich und deine Familie herzlich ein! I warmly invite you and your family! Wir fangen um sechs Uhr an. Die Kinder können im Garten spielen. We start at six o'clock. The children can play in the garden. Kannst du mir bis Mittwoch Bescheid sagen, ob ihr kommt? Can you let me know by Wednesday whether you are coming? Liebe Grüße! Love!"],["notes","Notes","A model text, written for this course. A real one names people: replace them with placeholders before you save it. The message asks for an answer by Wednesday. A short reply: Danke für die Einladung! Wir kommen gern."]]},{"u":"einmal.html","t":"einmal","s":"once","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich gehe einmal in der Woche schwimmen. :: I go swimming once a week. Bitte noch einmal! :: Once more, please!"],["notes","Notes","Also zweimal , dreimal . In speech einmal often becomes mal ."]]},{"u":"eins.html","t":"eins","s":"one","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir kommen um eins. :: We are coming at one."],["notes","Notes","Counting and alone: eins . Before a noun it is the article ein, eine . With Uhr : ein Uhr ."]]},{"u":"einsteigen.html","t":"einsteigen","s":"to get on (a vehicle)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte schnell einsteigen! :: Please get on quickly!"]]},{"u":"elf.html","t":"elf","s":"eleven","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kommen Sie bitte um elf Uhr. :: Please come at eleven o'clock."]]},{"u":"elfte.html","t":"elfte","s":"eleventh","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Heute ist der elfte November. :: Today is the eleventh of November."]]},{"u":"eltern.html","t":"Eltern","s":"parents","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Eltern kommen am Donnerstag in die Schule. :: The parents come to school on Thursday."],["notes","Notes","Only plural: die Eltern . One parent is der Elternteil , but people usually say Mutter or Vater ."]]},{"u":"elternabend.html","t":"Elternabend","s":"parents' evening","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kommst du am Donnerstag zum Elternabend? :: Are you coming to the parents' evening on Thursday?"]]},{"u":"entlueften.html","t":"entlüften","s":"to bleed","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Im Oktober entlüfte ich alle Heizkörper. :: In October I bleed all the radiators. Hast du den Heizkörper im Kinderzimmer schon entlüftet? :: Have you already bled the radiator in the children's room?"],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich habe den Heizkörper geentlüftet. :: Ich habe den Heizkörper entlüftet."],["notes","Notes","ent- is never separated and the participle has no ge- : entlüftet . die Luft is the air; the key you use is der Entlüftungsschlüssel ."]]},{"u":"entschuldigung.html","t":"Entschuldigung","s":"excuse note / apology","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Muss ich eine Entschuldigung schreiben? :: Do I have to write an excuse note?"],["notes","Notes","Alone, Entschuldigung! means Excuse me! or Sorry! . At school, eine Entschuldigung is the note that explains why a child was absent."]]},{"u":"er.html","t":"er","s":"he / it","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte geben Sie ihm einen kurzen Zettel mit. :: Please give him a short note to take. Ich hole ihn um vier ab. :: I will pick him up at four."],["notes","Notes","er also stands for a masculine thing: der Ball, er ist rot ."]]},{"u":"erkaeltung.html","t":"Erkältung","s":"cold","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das ist nur eine Erkältung. :: It is only a cold."]]},{"u":"erste.html","t":"erste","s":"first","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Tochter geht in die erste Klasse. :: My daughter is in first grade. Am ersten Tag war sie sehr müde. :: On the first day she was very tired."],["notes","Notes","Ordinals: erste, zweite, dritte, vierte , then -te up to 19 and -ste from 20: zwanzigste ."]]},{"u":"erster-tag-im-buero.html","t":"Erster Tag im Büro","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Kollege: Hallo! Bist du neu hier? :: Hello! Are you new here? ich: Ja, heute ist mein erster Tag. :: Yes, today is my first day. Kollege: Herzlich willkommen! Woher kommst du? :: Welcome! Where are you from? ich: Ich komme aus Spanien. Ich wohne jetzt hier mit meiner Familie. :: I am from Spain. I live here now with my family. Kollege: Schön! Sprichst du schon gut Deutsch? :: Nice! Do you already speak German well? ich: Nur ein bisschen. Ich lerne noch. :: Only a little. I am still learning. Kollege: Kein Problem. Die Küche ist hier links. Möchtest du einen Kaffee? :: No problem. The kitchen is here on the left. Would you like a coffee? ich: Ja, gern. Danke! :: Yes, please. Thanks!"],["variations","Variations","6 ich: Ja, ein bisschen. Bitte sprich langsam. :: Yes, a little. Please speak slowly."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. In many offices colleagues say du from the first day. When unsure, wait until they use du first."]]},{"u":"erzaehlen.html","t":"erzählen","s":"to tell","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Erzähl mal! Wie war die Schule? :: Tell me! How was school?"]]},{"u":"es.html","t":"es","s":"it","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wo ist die Brotdose? Ich finde sie nicht. :: Where is the lunch box? I can't find it. Es regnet. Es ist schon spät. :: It's raining. It's already late."],["notes","Notes","es is for das words. For der and die words, it is er and sie . es also starts sentences about weather and time."]]},{"u":"essen.html","t":"essen","s":"to eat","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Können wir Pizza essen? :: Can we eat pizza?"]]},{"u":"etwas.html","t":"etwas","s":"something","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Müssen die Kinder etwas mitbringen? :: Do the children have to bring anything?"],["notes","Notes","Short form in speech: was . etwas before a noun means some : etwas Wasser ."]]},{"u":"euer.html","t":"euer","s":"your (plural informal)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte bringt eure Zahlen vom Oktober mit. :: Please bring your figures from October."],["notes","Notes","The e drops before an ending: eure , euren ."]]},{"u":"euro.html","t":"Euro","s":"euro","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das kostet zwei Euro. :: That costs two euros."],["notes","Notes","After a number the plural stays Euro : zehn Euro ."]]},{"u":"fahren.html","t":"fahren","s":"to drive / to go (by vehicle)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Fährst du am Dienstag zum Training? :: Are you driving to training on Tuesday? Wir sind mit dem Bus gefahren. :: We went by bus."],["notes","Notes","sein when you go somewhere; haben when you drive someone or something: Ich habe die Kinder gefahren ."]]},{"u":"fahrgemeinschaft.html","t":"Fahrgemeinschaft","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Mutter: Hallo! Fährst du am Dienstag zum Training? :: Hi! Are you driving to training on Tuesday? ich: Ja, warum? :: Yes, why? Mutter: Ich muss bis sechs arbeiten. Kannst du meine Tochter mitnehmen? :: I have to work until six. Can you take my daughter along? ich: Na klar, kein Problem. Ich hole sie um Viertel nach vier ab. :: Of course, no problem. I'll pick her up at quarter past four. Mutter: Danke! Und ich fahre dafür am Donnerstag. :: Thanks! And I'll drive on Thursday in return. ich: Abgemacht! :: Deal!"],["variations","Variations","2 ich: Nein, diese Woche kann ich leider nicht. Frag doch mal im Chat. :: No, sadly I can't this week. Why don't you ask in the chat."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. A Fahrgemeinschaft is a lift share: parents take turns driving the children."]]},{"u":"fahrkarte.html","t":"Fahrkarte","s":"ticket","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Eine Fahrkarte nach Berlin, bitte. :: A ticket to Berlin, please."],["notes","Notes","Also das Ticket ."]]},{"u":"fahrrad.html","t":"Fahrrad","s":"bicycle","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn fährt mit dem Fahrrad zur Schule. :: My son cycles to school."],["notes","Notes","In speech also das Rad ."]]},{"u":"falsch.html","t":"falsch","s":"wrong","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Diese Aufgabe ist falsch. Rechne noch einmal! :: This task is wrong. Do the sum again!"]]},{"u":"familie.html","t":"Familie","s":"family","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Familie wohnt in Deutschland. :: My family lives in Germany. Am Sonntag frühstückt die Familie zusammen. :: On Sunday the family has breakfast together."]]},{"u":"fehlermeldung.html","t":"Fehlermeldung","s":"error message","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","In der App erscheint eine Fehlermeldung. :: An error message appears in the app. Machen Sie bitte ein Foto der Fehlermeldung. :: Please take a photo of the error message."]]},{"u":"feierabend-machen.html","t":"Feierabend machen","s":"to finish work for the day","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Ich mache heute um vier Feierabend. :: I'm finishing work at four today. Schönen Feierabend! :: Enjoy your evening! (after work)"],["usage","Usage","Schönen Feierabend! is what colleagues say when someone goes home."]]},{"u":"feierabend.html","t":"Feierabend","s":"end of the working day","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Um fünf habe ich Feierabend. :: I finish work at five."]]},{"u":"feiern.html","t":"feiern","s":"to celebrate","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Samstag feiern wir den Geburtstag von unserem Sohn. :: On Saturday we are celebrating our son's birthday."]]},{"u":"fenster.html","t":"Fenster","s":"window","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mach bitte das Fenster auf! :: Please open the window!"]]},{"u":"fernsehen.html","t":"fernsehen","s":"to watch TV","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Darf ich noch zehn Minuten fernsehen? :: May I watch TV for ten more minutes?"]]},{"u":"fertig.html","t":"fertig","s":"ready / finished","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bist du fertig? Wir müssen los! :: Are you ready? We have to go! Ich mache die Präsentation morgen fertig. :: I'll finish the presentation tomorrow."],["notes","Notes","fertig sein : to be ready or finished. fertig machen : to finish something."]]},{"u":"feuerwehrzufahrt.html","t":"Feuerwehrzufahrt","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Photo"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["transcription","Transcription","Feuerwehrzufahrt Zuschauereingang Gas"],["meaning","Meaning","The round white sign with a red ring means: no vehicles of any kind ( Verbot für Fahrzeuge aller Art ). The sign below says why: this is the access road for the fire brigade ( Feuerwehrzufahrt ). It must always stay clear, so never park or stop here. The small yellow sign marks a gas valve under the ground. On the wall, an arrow shows the way to the spectators' entrance ( Zuschauereingang )."]]},{"u":"fieber.html","t":"Fieber","s":"fever / temperature","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Er hat Fieber und Husten. :: He has a fever and a cough."]]},{"u":"finden.html","t":"finden","s":"to find; to think of","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich finde meinen Schlüssel nicht. :: I can't find my key. Wie findest du das Buch? :: What do you think of the book?"]]},{"u":"fliegen.html","t":"fliegen","s":"to fly","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Im Sommer fliegen wir nach Spanien. :: In summer we fly to Spain."]]},{"u":"foerderung.html","t":"Förderung","s":"subsidy, grant","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die angegebene Förderung ist voraussichtlich und abhängig von Bewilligung sowie Auszahlung durch die KfW. :: The subsidy stated is an estimate and depends on approval and payment by the KfW. Die Förderung erhalten Sie separat direkt von der KfW. :: You receive the subsidy separately, directly from the KfW. Unsere Förderung ist bewilligt. :: Our subsidy has been approved."],["notes","Notes","A subsidy is bewilligt (approved) or abgelehnt (refused). The letter that approves it is the Zusage or Zusageschreiben ."]]},{"u":"frage-15-minuten-vor-dem-training.html","t":"Frage: 15 Minuten vor dem Training da sein?","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Vater: Hallo. Ich habe gehört das man 15min vor Trainings Beginn da sein soll. Stimmt das? :: Hello. I heard that you should be there 15 minutes before training starts. Is that true? Trainer: Hallo, wenn es sich einrichten lässt, ja. Wenn wir pünktlich starten möchten, ist das leider notwendig. Gruß, Herr M. :: Hello, if it can be arranged, yes. If we want to start on time, it is unfortunately necessary. Regards, Mr M. Vater: Ok. Kein Problem, wollte nur sichergehen. :: OK. No problem, I just wanted to make sure."],["variations","Variations","1 Vater: Hallo. Ich habe gehört, dass man 15 Minuten vor Trainingsbeginn da sein soll. Stimmt das? :: Hello. I heard that you should be there 15 minutes before training starts. Is that true?"],["notes","Notes","A real chat between another parent and the coach, kept word for word. The variation shows the correct spelling: dass (conjunction) with a comma, Trainingsbeginn as one word. wenn es sich einrichten lässt : if it can be arranged. Polite and useful. sichergehen : to make sure. Ich wollte nur sichergehen."]]},{"u":"fragen.html","t":"fragen","s":"to ask","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich frage die Lehrerin. :: I ask the teacher."],["notes","Notes","fragen takes the Akkusativ: Ich frage dich , not dir ."]]},{"u":"frau.html","t":"Frau","s":"woman; wife; Mrs","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Frau ist Lehrerin. :: My wife is a teacher."],["notes","Notes","Frau is also the title before a surname: Guten Tag, Frau A.!"]]},{"u":"frei.html","t":"frei","s":"free / available","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe drei Plätze frei. :: I have three free seats. Am Samstag habe ich frei. :: I'm off on Saturday."],["notes","Notes","frei can also mean free of charge , but usually that is kostenlos ."]]},{"u":"freuen.html","t":"freuen","s":"to be happy / to look forward","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Unsere Kinder freuen sich. :: Our children will be happy. Ich freue mich auf das Wochenende. :: I am looking forward to the weekend."],["notes","Notes","sich freuen auf : to look forward to. sich freuen über : to be happy about. Das freut mich! I'm glad!"]]},{"u":"freund.html","t":"Freund","s":"friend / boyfriend","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Sonntag grillen wir mit Freunden im Garten. :: On Sunday we are having a barbecue with friends in the garden."],["notes","Notes","mein Freund often means my boyfriend . For a friend people say ein Freund von mir ."]]},{"u":"freundin.html","t":"Freundin","s":"friend (woman) / girlfriend","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Freundin hat am Freitag Geburtstag. :: My friend has her birthday on Friday."]]},{"u":"freundlich.html","t":"freundlich","s":"friendly","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die neue Nachbarin ist sehr freundlich. :: The new neighbour is very friendly."]]},{"u":"freut-mich.html","t":"Freut mich!","s":"Nice to meet you!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Freut mich, Sie kennenzulernen. :: Nice to meet you. (Sie) Das freut mich! :: I'm glad!"],["usage","Usage","When someone tells you their name for the first time."]]},{"u":"frisch.html","t":"frisch","s":"fresh","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Brot ist ganz frisch. :: The bread is very fresh."]]},{"u":"frueh.html","t":"früh","s":"early","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kann ich heute früher gehen? :: Can I leave earlier today?"]]},{"u":"frueher-gehen.html","t":"Früher gehen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Entschuldigung, darf ich kurz stören? :: Excuse me, may I interrupt for a moment? Chefin: Ja, bitte. Was gibt's? :: Yes, please. What is it? ich: Meine Tochter ist krank. Die Schule hat gerade angerufen. Kann ich heute früher gehen? :: My daughter is ill. The school just called. Can I leave early today? Chefin: Natürlich, das ist kein Problem. Gute Besserung für Ihre Tochter! :: Of course, that's no problem. Get well soon to your daughter! ich: Danke. Ich mache die Präsentation morgen fertig. :: Thanks. I'll finish the presentation tomorrow. Chefin: Gut. Können Sie morgen von zu Hause arbeiten? :: Good. Can you work from home tomorrow? ich: Ja, das geht. Ich schreibe Ihnen eine E-Mail. :: Yes, that works. I'll write you an email."],["variations","Variations","4 Chefin: Hm, heute ist es schwierig. Können Sie bis drei Uhr bleiben? :: Hm, today is difficult. Can you stay until three?"],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. In Germany parents may stay at home with an ill child ( Kinderkrankentage ); the paediatrician gives a certificate for the employer."]]},{"u":"fruehstueck.html","t":"Frühstück","s":"breakfast","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Was gibt es zum Frühstück? :: What is there for breakfast?"]]},{"u":"fruehstuecken.html","t":"frühstücken","s":"to have breakfast","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Komm frühstücken! :: Come and have breakfast!"]]},{"u":"fuenf.html","t":"fünf","s":"five","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Noch fünf Minuten, bitte! :: Five more minutes, please!"]]},{"u":"fuenfte.html","t":"fünfte","s":"fifth","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Heute ist der fünfte Mai. :: Today is the fifth of May."]]},{"u":"fuenfzehn.html","t":"fünfzehn","s":"fifteen","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Bus kommt in fünfzehn Minuten. :: The bus comes in fifteen minutes."]]},{"u":"fuenfzehnte.html","t":"fünfzehnte","s":"fifteenth","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Termin ist am fünfzehnten Mai. :: The appointment is on the fifteenth of May."]]},{"u":"fuenfzig.html","t":"fünfzig","s":"fifty","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Jacke kostet fünfzig Euro. :: The jacket costs fifty euros."]]},{"u":"fuer.html","t":"für","s":"for","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe ein Paket für Sie. :: I have a parcel for you."]]},{"u":"fussball.html","t":"Fußball","s":"football","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn spielt jeden Samstag Fußball. :: My son plays football every Saturday."],["notes","Notes","Fußball spielen is the sport, without article. Der Fußball is also the ball itself."]]},{"u":"ganz.html","t":"ganz","s":"quite; whole; very","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mir geht es ganz gut. :: I am quite well. Das Brot ist ganz frisch. :: The bread is very fresh."]]},{"u":"gap-faellt-das-training-aus.html","t":"Fällt das Training aus?","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Gap"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-wanted-to-say","I wanted to say","Is training cancelled today because of the rain?"],["in-german","In German","Fällt das Training heute wegen des Regens aus?"]]},{"u":"gap-heute-holt-die-oma-ab.html","t":"Heute holt die Oma ab","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Gap"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-wanted-to-say","I wanted to say","Today grandma is picking up our daughter, not me."],["in-german","In German","Heute holt die Oma unsere Tochter ab, nicht ich."]]},{"u":"gap-paket-annehmen.html","t":"Paket annehmen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Gap"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-wanted-to-say","I wanted to say","Could you accept a parcel for me tomorrow? I'm at work all day."],["in-german","In German","Könnten Sie morgen ein Paket für mich annehmen? Ich bin den ganzen Tag bei der Arbeit."]]},{"u":"gap-sporttasche-vergessen.html","t":"Sporttasche vergessen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Gap"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-wanted-to-say","I wanted to say","My son forgot his sports bag at home. Can I bring it at five?"],["in-german","In German","Mein Sohn hat seine Sporttasche zu Hause vergessen. Kann ich sie um fünf bringen?"]]},{"u":"geben.html","t":"geben","s":"to give","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Was gibt es zum Frühstück? :: What is there for breakfast? Bei Fieber geben Sie ihm den Saft. :: If he has a fever, give him the syrup."],["notes","Notes","es gibt plus Akkusativ means there is or there are ."]]},{"u":"geburtstag.html","t":"Geburtstag","s":"birthday","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Freitag habe ich Geburtstag. Ich mache eine kleine Party. :: On Friday it is my birthday. I am having a small party."]]},{"u":"gefahr.html","t":"Gefahr","s":"danger","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Damit steigt die Gefahr durch herabfallende Äste und umfallende Bäume. :: So the danger from falling branches and falling trees rises. Erkennen Sie die Gefahr? :: Do you recognise the danger?"],["notes","Notes","Do not mix up die Gefahren (the dangers) with gefahren (participle of fahren ): Gefahren durch klimakranke Bäume and Hier wird schnell gefahren sound almost the same."]]},{"u":"gefahren-durch-klimakranke-baeume.html","t":"Gefahren durch klimakranke Bäume","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Photo"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["transcription","Transcription","Gefahren durch klimakranke Bäume Erkennen Sie die Gefahr? Liebe Waldgäste, Dürrephasen nehmen durch die Klimakrise zu und schädigen viele Bäume. Damit steigt die Gefahr durch herabfallende Äste und umfallende Bäume. Sie betreten den Wald auf eigene Gefahr. Daher: Seien Sie beim Waldbesuch besonders aufmerksam und schauen Sie nach oben in die Baumkronen. Achten Sie auf absterbende oder lose Baumteile und meiden Sie deren Nähe. Insbesondere bei Wind können sehr gefährliche Situationen entstehen. Im Notfall: 112. Nach Möglichkeit mit Nennung eines Rettungspunktes."],["meaning","Meaning","Dangers from trees made sick by the climate. Do you recognise the danger? Dear forest visitors, dry periods are increasing because of the climate crisis and damage many trees. So the danger from falling branches and falling trees rises. You enter the forest at your own risk. Therefore: be especially careful when you visit the forest and look up into the treetops. Watch out for dying or loose parts of trees and keep away from them. Above all when it is windy, very dangerous situations can arise. In an emergency call 112, and if possible name a rescue point ( Rettungspunkt ): the green signs with a number along forest roads, where an ambulance can find you."]]},{"u":"gefallen.html","t":"gefallen","s":"to please, to like","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Wohnung gefällt mir. :: I like the flat. Gefällt dir die Jacke? :: Do you like the jacket?"],["notes","Notes","The thing you like is the subject and the person is in the Dativ, like Spanish me gusta ."]]},{"u":"gegen.html","t":"gegen","s":"against","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Samstag spielen wir gegen die Mannschaft aus der Nachbarstadt. :: On Saturday we play against the team from the neighbouring town."],["notes","Notes","gegen eins also means around one o'clock ."]]},{"u":"gegenueber.html","t":"gegenüber","s":"opposite","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Café ist gegenüber der Schule. :: The café is opposite the school."]]},{"u":"gehen.html","t":"gehen","s":"to go / to walk","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir gehen heute zum Kinderarzt. :: We are going to the paediatrician today. Ich bin gestern zum Training gegangen. :: I went to training yesterday."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich habe nach Hause gegangen. :: Ich bin nach Hause gegangen."],["notes","Notes","Wie geht's? How are you? Das geht. That works."]]},{"u":"gelb.html","t":"gelb","s":"yellow","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Banane ist gelb. :: The banana is yellow."]]},{"u":"geld.html","t":"Geld","s":"money","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe kein Geld dabei. :: I have no money on me."]]},{"u":"genau.html","t":"genau","s":"exactly","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Genau! Das ist richtig. :: Exactly! That is right. Es ist genau acht Uhr. :: It is exactly eight o'clock."]]},{"u":"gerade.html","t":"gerade","s":"just / right now","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Schule hat gerade angerufen. :: The school just called."]]},{"u":"geradeaus.html","t":"geradeaus","s":"straight on","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Gehen Sie geradeaus und dann links. :: Go straight on and then left."]]},{"u":"gern-geschehen.html","t":"Gern geschehen.","s":"You're welcome.","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Bitte, gern geschehen! :: You're welcome! Bitte schön! :: You're welcome!"],["usage","Usage","The answer to Danke . Shorter: Gern! or Bitte!"]]},{"u":"gern.html","t":"gern","s":"gladly / like to","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ja, gern! :: Yes, gladly! Mein Sohn spielt gern Fußball. :: My son likes playing football."],["notes","Notes","Verb + gern says what you like doing: Ich spiele gern Fußball , I like playing football."]]},{"u":"geschichte.html","t":"Geschichte","s":"story","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Liest du mir noch eine Geschichte vor? :: Will you read me a story?"],["notes","Notes","Geschichte is also the school subject history."]]},{"u":"geschlossen.html","t":"geschlossen","s":"closed","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Sonntag ist die Bäckerei geschlossen. :: On Sunday the bakery is closed."],["notes","Notes","In speech people often say zu : Die Bäckerei ist zu."]]},{"u":"gestern.html","t":"gestern","s":"yesterday","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Gestern hatte er Fieber. :: Yesterday he had a fever."]]},{"u":"gesund.html","t":"gesund","s":"healthy","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Er ist wieder gesund und geht morgen in die Schule. :: He is healthy again and is going to school tomorrow."]]},{"u":"gewaehrleistung.html","t":"Gewährleistung","s":"statutory warranty","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Gewährleistung endet fünf Jahre nach der Abnahme. :: The statutory warranty ends five years after acceptance. Mängel melde ich vor dem Ende der Gewährleistung schriftlich. :: I report defects in writing before the statutory warranty ends."],["notes","Notes","die Gewährleistung is the seller's liability for defects by law. die Garantie is an extra promise, often from the manufacturer."]]},{"u":"gewinnen.html","t":"gewinnen","s":"to win","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wer gewinnt heute? :: Who is going to win today? Ihr habt gewonnen! :: You won!"]]},{"u":"glauben.html","t":"glauben","s":"to believe, to think","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich glaube, er ist krank. :: I think he is ill."]]},{"u":"gleich.html","t":"gleich","s":"in a moment / right away","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich komme gleich! :: I'm coming!"],["notes","Notes","As an adjective gleich means same : die gleiche Klasse ."]]},{"u":"gluecklich.html","t":"glücklich","s":"happy","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Nach dem Sieg waren alle Kinder glücklich. :: After the win all the children were happy."]]},{"u":"grillen-bei-freunden.html","t":"Grillen bei Freunden","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Freund: Wir grillen am Sonntag im Garten. Kommt ihr auch? :: We're having a barbecue in the garden on Sunday. Are you coming too? ich: Sehr gern! Sollen wir etwas mitbringen? :: We'd love to! Should we bring something? Freund: Vielleicht einen Salat? Getränke haben wir genug. :: Maybe a salad? We have enough drinks. ich: Kein Problem, ich mache einen Kartoffelsalat. Können die Kinder auch kommen? :: No problem, I'll make a potato salad. Can the children come too? Freund: Natürlich! Unsere Kinder freuen sich. :: Of course! Our children will be happy. ich: Super. Wann sollen wir da sein? :: Great. When should we be there? Freund: So gegen eins. Bis Sonntag! :: Around one. See you on Sunday!"],["variations","Variations","2 ich: Schade, am Sonntag können wir nicht. Wir haben schon etwas vor. :: Pity, we can't on Sunday. We already have plans."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. etwas vorhaben : to have plans. gegen eins : around one o'clock."]]},{"u":"gross.html","t":"groß","s":"big / tall","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn ist schon sehr groß. :: My son is already very tall. Unsere neue Wohnung ist groß. :: Our new flat is big."]]},{"u":"grosseltern.html","t":"Großeltern","s":"grandparents","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Wochenende besuchen wir die Großeltern. :: At the weekend we visit the grandparents."],["notes","Notes","die Oma and der Opa are the everyday words for grandmother and grandfather."]]},{"u":"gruen.html","t":"grün","s":"green","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Ampel ist grün. Wir können gehen. :: The traffic light is green. We can go."]]},{"u":"grundbuch.html","t":"Grundbuch","s":"land register","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B2"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bedingung ist, dass Sie im Grundbuch eingetragen sind. :: The condition is that you are registered in the land register. Erforderlicher Nachweis ist ein Grundbuchauszug und eine amtliche Meldebescheinigung. :: The proof required is an extract from the land register and an official certificate of registration. Wir bestellen einen Grundbuchauszug beim Grundbuchamt. :: We are ordering an extract from the land register at the land registry."],["notes","Notes","You are im Grundbuch eingetragen (registered in it) when you own the land. A copy of the entry is a Grundbuchauszug ."]]},{"u":"gruss-am-schultor.html","t":"Gruß am Schultor","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Mutter: Hallo! Na, wie geht's? :: Hi! So, how are you? ich: Hallo! Gut, danke. Und dir? :: Hi! Fine, thanks. And you? Mutter: Ganz gut, aber ein bisschen müde. Kommst du am Donnerstag zum Elternabend? :: Quite well, but a bit tired. Are you coming to the parents' evening on Thursday? ich: Ja, ich komme. Weißt du, wann er anfängt? :: Yes, I'm coming. Do you know when it starts? Mutter: Um halb acht, im Klassenzimmer. :: At half past seven, in the classroom. ich: Super, danke. Bis Donnerstag! :: Great, thanks. See you on Thursday!"],["variations","Variations","4 ich: Leider nicht, ich muss arbeiten. Kannst du mir danach erzählen, was die Lehrerin sagt? :: Sadly not, I have to work. Can you tell me afterwards what the teacher says?"],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Parents at the school gate usually say du to each other. Weißt du, wann er anfängt? After wann inside a sentence, the verb goes to the end."]]},{"u":"gut-gemacht.html","t":"Gut gemacht!","s":"Well done!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Weiter so! :: Keep it up! Super gespielt! :: Great game!"],["usage","Usage","To praise a child after training or after homework."]]},{"u":"gut.html","t":"gut","s":"good / well","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ihr habt gut gespielt. :: You played well. Das Team spielt heute sehr gut. :: The team is playing very well today."]]},{"u":"gute-besserung.html","t":"Gute Besserung!","s":"Get well soon!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Gute Besserung an deinen Sohn! :: Get well soon to your son! Gute Besserung für Ihre Tochter! :: Get well soon to your daughter!"],["usage","Usage","What you say to someone who is ill, or about someone who is ill."]]},{"u":"gute-nacht.html","t":"Gute Nacht","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Es ist acht Uhr. Zeit fürs Bett! :: It's eight o'clock. Time for bed! Kind: Schon? Darf ich noch zehn Minuten fernsehen? :: Already? May I watch TV for ten more minutes? ich: Nein, morgen ist Schule. Hast du die Zähne geputzt? :: No, there's school tomorrow. Have you brushed your teeth? Kind: Ja. Liest du mir noch eine Geschichte vor? :: Yes. Will you read me a story? ich: Gern, aber nur eine kurze. :: Gladly, but only a short one. Kind: Gute Nacht! Ich hab dich lieb. :: Good night! I love you. ich: Ich dich auch. Schlaf gut! :: Me too. Sleep well!"],["variations","Variations","3 ich: Na gut, zehn Minuten. Aber dann ist Schluss! :: All right, ten minutes. But then that's it!"],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Ich hab dich lieb is how family members say I love you . Ich liebe dich is for partners."]]},{"u":"haben.html","t":"haben","s":"to have","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Hast du heute Hausaufgaben? :: Do you have homework today? Heute Morgen hatte er 39 Grad. :: This morning he had a temperature of 39 degrees."]]},{"u":"halb.html","t":"halb","s":"half","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir müssen um halb acht los. :: We have to leave at half past seven."],["notes","Notes","halb acht is 7:30: half way to eight, not half past eight."]]},{"u":"halle.html","t":"Halle","s":"sports hall","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte seid immer 45 Minuten vor dem Spiel in der Halle. :: Please always be in the hall 45 minutes before the match."]]},{"u":"hallo.html","t":"hallo","s":"hello / hi","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Hallo! Na, wie geht's? :: Hi! So, how are you?"],["notes","Notes","Informal, to people you know. With Sie : Guten Tag ."]]},{"u":"halt-bei-bedarf.html","t":"Halt bei Bedarf","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Photo"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["transcription","Transcription","RB [Nummer] [Zugname] [Ort] - [Ort] Hbf 05:54 [Ort] Abfahrt 5:52 Weiterfahrt nach 5:54 [Ort] (Halt bei Bedarf) 6:00 [Ort] Hbf Standort im Zug"],["meaning","Meaning","The display inside a regional train (RB, Regionalbahn). It shows the line, the route and the clock (05:54). The train is at a station and left at 5:52 ( Abfahrt ). It goes on ( Weiterfahrt ) to the next stop at 5:54, where it only stops on request ( Halt bei Bedarf ), and arrives at the main station ( Hbf , Hauptbahnhof ) at 6:00. Standort im Zug shows where you are in the train."]]},{"u":"halten.html","t":"halten","s":"to hold / to save (a ball)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe drei Bälle gehalten. :: I saved three balls."]]},{"u":"halteverbot.html","t":"Halteverbot","s":"no-stopping zone","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","An Schultagen ist hier von 7 bis 9 Uhr Halteverbot. :: On school days there is no stopping here from 7 to 9. Das Halteverbot gilt nicht für Linienbusse. :: The no-stopping rule does not apply to scheduled buses."],["notes","Notes","Halten is stopping for up to three minutes, Parken is longer or leaving the car. A red cross on blue is the absolute ban ( absolutes Halteverbot ); a single red stripe is the limited one ( eingeschränktes Halteverbot ), where you may stop for three minutes but not park."]]},{"u":"handball.html","t":"Handball","s":"handball","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Tochter spielt Handball im Verein. :: My daughter plays handball in a club."]]},{"u":"handy.html","t":"Handy","s":"mobile phone","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Handy ist kaputt. :: My mobile phone is broken."],["notes","Notes","Handy looks English but is German only. In English it is a mobile or cell phone ."]]},{"u":"hauptwasserzufuhr.html","t":"Hauptwasserzufuhr","s":"main water supply","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bei einem starken Wasseraustritt drehe ich die Hauptwasserzufuhr ab. :: If a lot of water leaks out, I turn off the main water supply."],["notes","Notes","In everyday speech: den Haupthahn zudrehen ."]]},{"u":"haus.html","t":"Haus","s":"house","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Haus hat einen Garten. :: The house has a garden."],["notes","Notes","nach Hause is going home; zu Hause is being at home."]]},{"u":"hausaufgabe.html","t":"Hausaufgabe","s":"homework task","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Zuerst die Hausaufgaben, dann darfst du spielen. :: Homework first, then you may play. Hast du heute Hausaufgaben? :: Do you have homework today?"],["notes","Notes","Mostly used in the plural: Hausaufgaben machen , to do homework."]]},{"u":"hausaufgaben-machen.html","t":"Hausaufgaben machen","s":"to do homework","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Zuerst machst du die Hausaufgaben. :: First you do your homework. Hast du die Hausaufgaben schon gemacht? :: Have you done your homework yet?"],["usage","Usage","German uses machen , not tun , for homework."]]},{"u":"hausaufgaben.html","t":"Hausaufgaben","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Wie war's in der Schule? :: How was school? Kind: Gut. Wir haben in Mathe ein Spiel gemacht. :: Good. We played a game in maths. ich: Schön! Hast du heute Hausaufgaben? :: Nice! Do you have homework today? Kind: Ja, Deutsch und Mathe. Aber ich will zuerst spielen. :: Yes, German and maths. But I want to play first. ich: Zuerst die Hausaufgaben, dann darfst du spielen. :: Homework first, then you may play. Kind: Kannst du mir helfen? Die Aufgabe ist so schwer. :: Can you help me? The task is so hard. ich: Na klar. Zeig mal! :: Of course. Show me!"],["variations","Variations","2 Kind: Nicht so gut. Ich habe mein Heft vergessen. :: Not so good. I forgot my exercise book. 7 ich: Jetzt nicht, ich koche. Frag doch deine Schwester. :: Not now, I'm cooking. Why don't you ask your sister."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. dann darfst du spielen : after dann the verb comes right away, in position 2."]]},{"u":"hebel.html","t":"Hebel","s":"lever","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Öffnen Sie die drei grünen Hebel. :: Open the three green levers. Den unteren roten Hebel darf man nie öffnen. :: You must never open the lower red lever."],["notes","Notes","Also figurative: am längeren Hebel sitzen means to have the upper hand."]]},{"u":"heiss.html","t":"heiß","s":"hot","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Im Sommer ist es in der Halle sehr heiß. :: In summer it is very hot in the hall."]]},{"u":"heissen.html","t":"heißen","s":"to be called","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wie heißt du? :: What is your name? Wie heißt das auf Deutsch? :: What is that called in German?"]]},{"u":"heizkoerper.html","t":"Heizkörper","s":"radiator","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Heizkörper bleiben kalt. :: The radiators stay cold. Der Heizkörper im Bad wird nicht richtig warm. :: The radiator in the bathroom does not get properly warm."],["notes","Notes","Singular and plural look the same: der Heizkörper , die Heizkörper . In everyday speech many people just say die Heizung ."]]},{"u":"helfen.html","t":"helfen","s":"to help","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kannst du mir helfen? :: Can you help me?"],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Kannst du mich helfen? :: Kannst du mir helfen?"]]},{"u":"hell.html","t":"hell","s":"bright, light","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Wohnung ist schön hell. :: The flat is nice and bright."]]},{"u":"herzlich-willkommen.html","t":"Herzlich willkommen!","s":"Welcome!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Herzlich willkommen im Haus! :: Welcome to the house! Willkommen in Deutschland! :: Welcome to Germany!"],["usage","Usage","To greet a new neighbour, a new player or the guests of an evening."]]},{"u":"herzlichen-glueckwunsch.html","t":"Herzlichen Glückwunsch!","s":"Congratulations!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Herzlichen Glückwunsch zum Geburtstag! :: Happy birthday! Herzlichen Glückwunsch, ihr habt gewonnen! :: Congratulations, you won!"],["usage","Usage","For a birthday, a win or good news."]]},{"u":"heute.html","t":"heute","s":"today","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Heute ist ein besonderer Tag. :: Today is a special day."]]},{"u":"hier.html","t":"hier","s":"here","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wohnen Sie schon lange hier? :: Have you lived here long?"]]},{"u":"hinten.html","t":"hinten","s":"at the back","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Toilette ist hinten links. :: The toilet is at the back on the left."]]},{"u":"hinter.html","t":"hinter","s":"behind","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Mülltonnen stehen hinter dem Haus. :: The bins are behind the house."]]},{"u":"hinzufuegen.html","t":"hinzufügen","s":"to add","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte fügt mich zur WhatsApp-Gruppe hinzu. :: Please add me to the WhatsApp group. Der Trainer hat mich zur Gruppe hinzugefügt. :: The coach added me to the group."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Bitte hinzufügt mich zur Gruppe. :: Bitte fügt mich zur Gruppe hinzu."],["notes","Notes","zu + Dativ for the group: zur Gruppe (zu der Gruppe)."]]},{"u":"hitze.html","t":"Hitze","s":"heat","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kind A. kann heute wegen der großen Hitze nicht zum Training kommen. :: Child A. cannot come to training today because of the great heat. Bei dieser Hitze machen wir nur lockere Übungen. :: In this heat we only do light exercises."],["notes","Notes","hitzefrei is a day off school because of the heat."]]},{"u":"hoch.html","t":"hoch","s":"high","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wie hoch ist das Fieber? :: How high is the fever?"],["notes","Notes","Before a noun it loses the c : hohes Fieber ."]]},{"u":"hoeren.html","t":"hören","s":"to hear, to listen","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich höre gern Musik. :: I like listening to music."]]},{"u":"hoffentlich.html","t":"hoffentlich","s":"hopefully","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Hoffentlich gewinnen wir! :: Hopefully we'll win!"]]},{"u":"hundert.html","t":"hundert","s":"a hundred","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Fahrrad kostet hundert Euro. :: The bike costs a hundred euros."],["notes","Notes","hundertzwanzig is 120, zweihundert is 200."]]},{"u":"hunger.html","t":"Hunger","s":"hunger","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe Hunger. :: I am hungry."],["notes","Notes","Hunger haben : German uses haben , like Spanish tener hambre ."]]},{"u":"husten.html","t":"Husten","s":"cough","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn hat Husten und kann nicht schlafen. :: My son has a cough and cannot sleep."]]},{"u":"ich-komme-gleich.html","t":"Ich komme gleich!","s":"I'm coming!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Moment, ich komme gleich! :: Just a moment, I'm coming!"],["usage","Usage","gleich means in a moment ."]]},{"u":"ich-muss-los.html","t":"Ich muss los.","s":"I have to go.","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","So, ich muss los. :: Right, I have to go. Wir müssen um halb acht los. :: We have to leave at half past seven."],["usage","Usage","A friendly way to end a chat. los stands for losgehen or losfahren ."]]},{"u":"ich.html","t":"ich","s":"I","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kannst du mir helfen? :: Can you help me? Er ruft mich morgen an. :: He will call me tomorrow."]]},{"u":"ihr.html","t":"ihr","s":"you (plural informal)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kommt ihr auch? :: Are you coming too? Ich bringe euch einen Salat mit. :: I will bring you a salad."]]},{"u":"im-bus.html","t":"Im Bus","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Entschuldigung, fährt der Bus zum Bahnhof? :: Excuse me, does the bus go to the station? Busfahrer: Ja. Steigen Sie ein! :: Yes. Get on! ich: Eine Fahrkarte, bitte. Was kostet das? :: A ticket, please. How much is it? Busfahrer: Drei Euro. :: Three euros. ich: Wo muss ich aussteigen? :: Where do I have to get off? Busfahrer: An der nächsten Haltestelle. :: At the next stop. ich: Danke schön! :: Thank you!"],["variations","Variations","2 Busfahrer: Nein, nehmen Sie die Linie vier. :: No, take the number four."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. aussteigen is separable: Wo steige ich aus? In the question with muss it stays together at the end: Wo muss ich aussteigen?"]]},{"u":"im-cafe.html","t":"Im Café","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Kellner: Hallo! Was möchten Sie trinken? :: Hello! What would you like to drink? ich: Einen Kaffee mit Milch, bitte. :: A coffee with milk, please. Freundin: Und ich nehme einen Tee. :: And I'll have a tea. Kellner: Möchten Sie auch etwas essen? Der Kuchen ist sehr lecker. :: Would you like something to eat too? The cake is very tasty. ich: Ja, gern. Ein Stück Kuchen, bitte. :: Yes, please. A piece of cake, please. Kellner: Gern. Kommt sofort. :: Sure. Coming right away. ich: Wir möchten bitte bezahlen. :: We would like to pay, please. Kellner: Zusammen oder getrennt? :: Together or separately? ich: Zusammen, bitte. :: Together, please."],["variations","Variations","5 ich: Nein, danke. Nur den Kaffee. :: No, thanks. Just the coffee. 9 ich: Getrennt, bitte. :: Separately, please."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Zusammen oder getrennt? is the usual question when you pay in a group."]]},{"u":"im-leistungsumfang-enthalten.html","t":"im Leistungsumfang enthalten","s":"included in the scope of services","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["B2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Ggf. notwendige Erdarbeiten sind nicht im Leistungsumfang enthalten. :: Any earthworks that may be needed are not included in the scope of services. Ist die Entsorgung der Öl-Tanks im Leistungsumfang enthalten? :: Is the disposal of the oil tanks included in the scope of services? Die Wartung ist im Preis enthalten. :: Maintenance is included in the price."],["usage","Usage","Offers and contracts list what the company will do ( der Leistungsumfang ) and what it will not. Look for nicht enthalten before you sign. im Preis inbegriffen means the same in everyday language."]]},{"u":"im-supermarkt.html","t":"Im Supermarkt","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Entschuldigung, wo ist die Milch? :: Excuse me, where is the milk? Verkäufer: Die Milch ist hinten links. :: The milk is at the back on the left. ich: Danke. Und haben Sie auch Äpfel? :: Thank you. And do you also have apples? Verkäufer: Ja, die Äpfel sind vorne rechts. :: Yes, the apples are at the front on the right. ich: Was kostet ein Kilo? :: How much is a kilo? Verkäufer: Ein Kilo kostet zwei Euro fünfzig. :: A kilo costs two euros fifty. ich: Gut, danke schön! :: Good, thank you!"],["variations","Variations","2 Verkäufer: Tut mir leid, die Milch ist leider aus. :: Sorry, the milk has sold out."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Entschuldigung opens a question to a stranger. Euro stays the same in the plural: zwei Euro fünfzig ."]]},{"u":"immer.html","t":"immer","s":"always","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte seid immer pünktlich. :: Please always be on time."]]},{"u":"imperativ.html","t":"Imperativ","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Commands and requests. Add bitte to sound friendly. du : the stem, no du : Verbs with Komm ! Räum dein Zimmer auf! Zieh dich an! e to i keep it: Gib mir den Ball! Nimm die Jacke mit! ihr : the ihr form without ihr : Kommt ! Beeilt euch! Sie : the Sie form, verb first: Kommen Sie bitte um elf Uhr. Bringen Sie die Karte mit. sein is special: Sei leise! Seid pünktlich! Seien Sie bitte pünktlich."],["simple-german","Simple German","Imperativ: Komm! (du), Kommt! (ihr), Kommen Sie! (Sie). Mit bitte ist es freundlich."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Du komm bitte! :: Komm bitte! Gebe mir den Ball! :: Gib mir den Ball!"]]},{"u":"in-der-kaffeepause.html","t":"In der Kaffeepause","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Kollegin: Morgen! Möchtest du auch einen Kaffee? :: Morning! Would you like a coffee too? ich: Ja, gern. Mit Milch, ohne Zucker, bitte. :: Yes, please. With milk, no sugar. Kollegin: Wie war dein Wochenende? :: How was your weekend? ich: Schön, aber anstrengend. Meine Kinder hatten zwei Spiele. Und deins? :: Nice, but tiring. My children had two matches. And yours? Kollegin: Ruhig. Ich habe viel gelesen und geschlafen. :: Quiet. I read and slept a lot. ich: Das klingt gut! So, ich muss los. Um zehn habe ich einen Termin. :: That sounds good! Right, I have to go. At ten I have an appointment. Kollegin: Viel Erfolg! Bis später. :: Good luck! See you later."],["variations","Variations","3 Kollegin: Was hast du am Wochenende gemacht? :: What did you do at the weekend?"],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Morgen! alone is short for Guten Morgen! . Colleagues often say du ; ask when you are not sure."]]},{"u":"in-der-praxis.html","t":"In der Praxis","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Ärztin: Hallo! Was fehlt dir denn? :: Hello! What's wrong with you? Kind: Mein Hals tut weh. :: My throat hurts. Ärztin: Mach bitte mal den Mund auf. Ah ja, der Hals ist rot. :: Open your mouth, please. Ah yes, the throat is red. ich: Ist es schlimm? :: Is it bad? Ärztin: Nein, das ist nur eine Erkältung. Er soll viel trinken und drei Tage zu Hause bleiben. :: No, it's only a cold. He should drink a lot and stay at home for three days. ich: Braucht er Medikamente? :: Does he need medicine? Ärztin: Ich schreibe Ihnen ein Rezept für einen Fiebersaft. :: I'll write you a prescription for a fever syrup. ich: Brauchen wir eine Bescheinigung für die Schule? :: Do we need a certificate for school? Ärztin: Ja, die bekommen Sie vorne an der Anmeldung. :: Yes, you'll get it at the reception at the front."],["variations","Variations","5 Ärztin: Er hat eine Mittelohrentzündung. Er braucht ein Antibiotikum. :: He has a middle ear infection. He needs an antibiotic."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. The doctor says du to the child and Sie to the parent. For work, ask for the certificate for the employer too: Ich brauche auch eine Bescheinigung für meinen Arbeitgeber."]]},{"u":"in.html","t":"in","s":"in / into","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir gehen in die Halle. :: We are going into the hall. Wir sind in der Halle. :: We are in the hall."],["notes","Notes","in die Halle : where to, Akkusativ. in der Halle : where, Dativ."]]},{"u":"infinitiv-als-nomen.html","t":"Infinitiv als Nomen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Any infinitive can become a noun: capital letter, always neuter ( das ). Signs love it because it names an action without a person. Without an article the adjective takes -es ; in the genitive the noun takes -s . Unbefugtes Betreten und Befahren verboten! :: Entering and driving in without permission forbidden! Unbefugtes Parken auf eigene Gefahr! :: Parking without permission at your own risk! Der Sinn des Wanderns ist, unterwegs zu sein. :: The point of hiking is to be on the way."],["simple-german","Simple German","Aus einem Verb wird ein Nomen: parken wird das Parken . Großer Buchstabe, immer das . Genitiv: des Wanderns ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Das parken ist hier verboten. :: Das Parken ist hier verboten. Unbefugter Betreten verboten! :: Unbefugtes Betreten verboten!"]]},{"u":"infos-spanienfahrt-2027.html","t":"Infos zur Spanienfahrt 2027","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Text"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Es ist mal wieder so weit! Unsere Spanienfahrt über Ostern steht mal wieder an und dazu bekommt ihr im Folgenden alle wichtigen Infos! It's that time again! Our Easter trip to Spain is coming up again, and below you get all the important information! Wir werden im nächsten Jahr die Trofeo Mediterraneo besuchen (viel internationalere Mannschaften). Next year we will go to the Trofeo Mediterraneo (many more international teams). Abfahrt: 19.03.2027 abends zwischen 19 und 21 Uhr. Die genaue Abfahrtszeit wird noch bekannt gegeben. Departure: 19.03.2027 in the evening, between 7 and 9 pm. The exact departure time will be announced later. Ankunft: 27.03.2027 / 28.03.2027, nachts ca. 1:00 Uhr. Arrival: 27.03.2027 / 28.03.2027, at night, around 1 am. Abfahrtsort: [Ort]. Aufgrund der großen Anzahl an Teilnehmern, Baustellen usw. wird der Abfahrtsort voraussichtlich verlegt. Place of departure: [Town]. Because of the large number of participants, roadworks and so on, the place of departure will probably be moved. Die Kosten der Fahrt belaufen sich auf 670 € pro Teilnehmer. The trip costs 670 € per participant. Im Preis mit inbegriffen sind Bustransfer nach Spanien und zurück, Bustransfer vor Ort zu den Spielen und das Hotel vor Ort (Vollpension). The price includes the bus to Spain and back, the bus to the matches there and the hotel there (full board). Vollpension heißt Buffet am Morgen, Mittag und Abend. Full board means a buffet in the morning, at midday and in the evening. Im letzten Jahr konnten wir alle sonstigen Aktivitäten vor Ort ohne zusätzliche Kosten für jeden Einzelnen ermöglichen, wie z. B. eine Busfahrt nach Barcelona mit Stadtrundfahrt und Besichtigung des Camp Nou, einen Tag im Aktiv-Camp mit Lasertag und Fußballgolf und einen Teamtag am Strand. Last year we could offer all the other activities there at no extra cost for anyone, for example a bus trip to Barcelona with a city tour and a visit to the Camp Nou, a day at an activity camp with laser tag and footgolf, and a team day at the beach. Das kommt allerdings ganz darauf an, wie viele Sponsoren gefunden werden. However, that depends entirely on how many sponsors are found. Von daher bitten wir alle Eltern, Spieler und Bekannte, ausgiebig nach Sponsoren zu suchen, egal in welcher Form, und auch über kleine Spenden freuen wir uns sehr. So we ask all parents, players and friends to look hard for sponsors, in any form, and we are also very happy about small donations. Bei Fragen oder wenn ihr Erfolg bei der Suche hattet, schreibt gerne Herrn K. oder mich an! If you have questions or if your search was successful, feel free to write to Mr K. or to me! Um nicht ausschließlich auf Spenden und Sponsoren angewiesen zu sein, möchten wir auch selbst aktiv zur Finanzierung beitragen. So as not to depend only on donations and sponsors, we also want to contribute to the funding ourselves. Daher werden wir in diesem Jahr erneut an den Adventssamstagen einen Waffelverkauf vor den örtlichen Einkaufsmärkten organisieren. So this year we will again organise a waffle sale in front of the local supermarkets on the Saturdays of Advent. Zusätzlich findet im Rahmen der Wintervorbereitung Ende Februar wieder ein JSG-Tag statt, an dem alle teilnehmenden Mannschaften ein Spiel ausrichten. In addition, as part of the winter preparation, there will again be a JSG day at the end of February, on which all participating teams host a match. Die daraus erzielten Einnahmen kommen ebenfalls der Spanienfahrt zugute. The money raised from it also goes to the trip to Spain. Auch hierbei freuen wir uns über Unterstützung jeglicher Art. Nähere Informationen hierzu folgen. Here too we welcome support of any kind. More details will follow. Zur Anmeldung: Der Preis von 670 € wird von jedem Mitfahrer selbst per Überweisung getätigt. About registration: each participant pays the price of 670 € themselves by bank transfer. Diese Überweisung gilt als verbindliche Anmeldung und muss bis zum 31.10.2026 auf unten aufgeführtes Konto eingegangen sein. This transfer counts as a binding registration and must have reached the account below by 31.10.2026. Wir haben dieses Jahr zusätzlich die Herausforderung, dass der Veranstalter den Termin zur Anzahlung 2 Monate vorgezogen hat. This year we also have the challenge that the organiser has moved the deposit date forward by 2 months. Entsprechend bitten wir alle, bei denen die Teilnahme bereits klar und möglich ist, die Zahlung bis zum 16.10.2026 auszuführen. Vielen Dank für eure Hilfe. So we ask everyone whose participation is already clear and possible to make the payment by 16.10.2026. Many thanks for your help. Konto: [Verein]. IBAN: [IBAN]. Verwendungszweck: Vorname und Nachname des Kindes und Spanien 2027. Account: [Club]. IBAN: [IBAN]. Payment reference: the child's first name and surname and \"Spanien 2027\". Aus buchhalterischen Gründen bitten wir darum, die Überweisungen einzeln durchzuführen, wenn mehrere Mitfahrer aus einer Familie dabei sind. Fo"],["notes","Notes","The original had two small slips, cleaned up here: die zusätzliche die Herausforderung and mit in vielen unvergesslichen Momenten . The list of activities is written as one sentence. sich belaufen auf is formal for \"to come to, to amount to\": Die Kosten belaufen sich auf 670 €. angewiesen sein auf (+ Akkusativ): to depend on. zugutekommen (+ Dativ): to benefit. Die Einnahmen kommen der Spanienfahrt zugute. wird bekannt gegeben , gefunden werden , wird getätigt : the letter uses the passive a lot. See Passiv mit werden ."]]},{"u":"inneneinheit.html","t":"Inneneinheit","s":"indoor unit","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Den Druck lese ich am Manometer der Inneneinheit ab. :: I read the pressure on the gauge of the indoor unit."]]},{"u":"ins-bett-gehen.html","t":"ins Bett gehen","s":"to go to bed","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Um acht Uhr gehen die Kinder ins Bett. :: At eight o'clock the children go to bed. Zeit fürs Bett! :: Time for bed!"],["usage","Usage","ins is in das : movement, so Akkusativ. In bed is im Bett ."]]},{"u":"interessant.html","t":"interessant","s":"interesting","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Buch ist sehr interessant. :: The book is very interesting."]]},{"u":"ja.html","t":"ja","s":"yes","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ja, gern! :: Yes, gladly!"],["notes","Notes","Inside a sentence ja is also a particle that means as you know : Das ist ja toll!"]]},{"u":"jacke.html","t":"Jacke","s":"jacket","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Zieh die Jacke an, es ist kalt! :: Put your jacket on, it is cold!"]]},{"u":"jahr.html","t":"Jahr","s":"year","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn ist zehn Jahre alt. :: My son is ten years old."]]},{"u":"jeder.html","t":"jeder","s":"every / each","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Jeden Dienstag ist Training. :: There is training every Tuesday. Jedes Kind bringt eine Flasche Wasser mit. :: Every child brings a bottle of water."],["notes","Notes","Only singular. Endings like der, die, das : jeder, jede, jedes ."]]},{"u":"jemand.html","t":"jemand","s":"somebody","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kann jemand am Samstag fahren? :: Can somebody drive on Saturday?"]]},{"u":"jemanden-in-kenntnis-setzen.html","t":"jemanden in Kenntnis setzen","s":"to inform someone (formal)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["B2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Sie setzen die Firma A unverzüglich nach Zusage der Förderung in Kenntnis. :: You inform company A without delay once the subsidy is approved. Hiermit setze ich Sie in Kenntnis, dass die Förderung bewilligt wurde. :: I hereby inform you that the subsidy has been approved. Bitte setzen Sie uns über jede Änderung in Kenntnis. :: Please inform us of any change."],["usage","Usage","Contracts and official letters use it for informieren or Bescheid geben . The person is in the accusative; what you inform about comes with über or a dass clause. In your own e-mails, ich möchte Ihnen mitteilen, dass ... sounds less stiff."]]},{"u":"jetzt.html","t":"jetzt","s":"now","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir treffen uns jetzt am Dienstag. :: We are now meeting on Tuesday. Jetzt nicht, ich koche. :: Not now, I'm cooking."]]},{"u":"jung.html","t":"jung","s":"young","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Schwester ist noch jung. :: My sister is still young."]]},{"u":"kaeltemittel.html","t":"Kältemittel","s":"refrigerant","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B2"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Kältemittel R290 ist Propan und brennbar. :: The refrigerant R290 is propane and is flammable. Wenn Kältemittel austritt, halte ich Abstand. :: If refrigerant leaks out, I keep my distance."]]},{"u":"kaese.html","t":"Käse","s":"cheese","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich esse gern Brot mit Käse. :: I like eating bread with cheese."]]},{"u":"kaffee.html","t":"Kaffee","s":"coffee","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Möchtest du auch einen Kaffee? :: Would you like a coffee too?"]]},{"u":"kalt.html","t":"kalt","s":"cold","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Heute ist es kalt. Zieh die Jacke an! :: It's cold today. Put your jacket on! Mir ist kalt. :: I'm cold."],["notes","Notes","You feel cold with the Dativ: Mir ist kalt , not Ich habe kalt ."]]},{"u":"kaputt.html","t":"kaputt","s":"broken","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Heizung ist kaputt. :: The heating is broken."]]},{"u":"kaufen.html","t":"kaufen","s":"to buy","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich kaufe Brot und Milch. :: I buy bread and milk."]]},{"u":"kaufvertrag-waermepumpe-auf-raten.html","t":"Kaufvertrag: Wärmepumpe auf Raten","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Text"],"Level":["B2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Die Firma A finanziert Ihnen den Kauf der Wärmepumpe über einen Ratenkauf. Company A finances your purchase of the heat pump through a hire purchase. Bei dieser Finanzierung müssen Sie den Gesamtkaufpreis nicht sofort zahlen, sondern zahlen diesen zzgl. Zinsen in mehreren vereinbarten monatlichen Raten über eine vereinbarte Laufzeit. With this financing you do not have to pay the total purchase price at once: you pay it plus interest in several agreed monthly instalments over an agreed term. Die Laufzeit beträgt 15 Jahre beginnend mit dem Monat, der auf die Abnahme der Anlage folgt. Die Monatsraten werden zum 5. des jeweiligen Monats fällig. The term is 15 years, starting with the month after the acceptance of the system. The monthly instalments are due on the 5th of each month. Sondertilgungen (auch des gesamten Betrags) sind jederzeit möglich, keine Vorfälligkeitsentschädigung. Extra repayments (even of the whole amount) are possible at any time, with no early repayment penalty. 0 € Anzahlung: Sie zahlen erst nach Installation der Wärmepumpe. No down payment: you only pay after the heat pump has been installed. Die angegebene Förderung ist voraussichtlich und abhängig von Bewilligung sowie Auszahlung durch die KfW. The subsidy stated is an estimate and depends on approval and payment by the KfW. Der volle Gesamtkaufpreis ist an die Firma A zu zahlen; die Förderung erhalten Sie separat direkt von der KfW. The full purchase price must be paid to company A; you receive the subsidy separately, directly from the KfW. Ggf. notwendige Erdarbeiten sind nicht im Leistungsumfang enthalten. Any earthworks that may be needed are not included in the scope of services. Ggf. notwendige Entsorgung vorhandener Öl-Tanks ist nicht im Leistungsumfang enthalten. Any disposal of existing oil tanks that may be needed is not included in the scope of services. Die Montage, Installation und Inbetriebnahme werden voraussichtlich mehrere Tage in Anspruch nehmen. Fitting, installation and commissioning will probably take several days. Die Heizung und die Wasserversorgung auf dem Grundstück bzw. im Gebäude wird während dieses Zeitraums kalt sein. The heating and the water supply on the property or in the building will be cold during this period. Sie bestätigen, dass Sie die Firma A unverzüglich nach Zusage oder Ablehnung der Förderung in Kenntnis setzen und den entsprechenden Bescheid in Kopie übermitteln. You confirm that you will inform company A without delay once the subsidy is approved or refused, and send a copy of the decision. Dieser Kaufvertrag erlischt, sobald und soweit die KfW den Antrag zur Förderung nicht bewilligt, sondern mit einem Ablehnungsschreiben abgelehnt hat (auflösende Bedingung). This purchase contract ends as soon as and to the extent that the KfW does not approve the subsidy application but rejects it with a letter of refusal (condition subsequent). Der Käufer kann seine Vertragserklärung innerhalb von 14 Tagen ohne Angabe von Gründen widerrufen. The buyer can withdraw his contractual declaration within 14 days without giving reasons."],["notes","Notes","Short extracts of a long contract, in the order they appear. The company name is replaced by Firma A ; prices, numbers and the address are left out. zzgl. is zuzüglich (plus), ggf. is gegebenenfalls (if necessary), bzw. is beziehungsweise (or rather). ist ... zu zahlen is sein + zu + Infinitiv : it must be paid. To do: send the company a copy of the KfW approval letter."]]},{"u":"kein-problem.html","t":"Kein Problem!","s":"No problem!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Kein Problem, ich mache einen Salat. :: No problem, I'll make a salad. Das ist kein Problem. :: That's no problem."],["usage","Usage","An easy way to say yes to a request."]]},{"u":"kein.html","t":"kein","s":"no / not a","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe keine Zeit. :: I have no time. Das ist kein Problem. :: That is no problem."],["notes","Notes","kein negates a noun with ein or with no article. Everything else takes nicht ."]]},{"u":"keller.html","t":"Keller","s":"basement / cellar","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Handwerker reparieren die Heizung im Keller. :: The workmen are repairing the heating in the basement."]]},{"u":"kennen.html","t":"kennen","s":"to know (a person, a place)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kennst du meine Schwester? :: Do you know my sister?"],["notes","Notes","kennen is for people and places; wissen is for facts: Ich weiß es nicht."]]},{"u":"kind.html","t":"Kind","s":"child","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Kind geht in die zweite Klasse. :: My child is in second grade. Die Kinder spielen im Garten. :: The children are playing in the garden."]]},{"u":"kinderarzt.html","t":"Kinderarzt","s":"paediatrician","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir gehen heute zum Kinderarzt. :: We are going to the paediatrician today."],["notes","Notes","A woman is die Kinderärztin . In the practice you mostly talk to the Arzthelferin first."]]},{"u":"klasse.html","t":"Klasse","s":"class / grade","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Tochter geht in die Klasse 2b. :: My daughter is in class 2b."]]},{"u":"klein.html","t":"klein","s":"small / little","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Tochter ist noch klein. :: My daughter is still little. Am Freitag mache ich eine kleine Party. :: On Friday I'm having a small party."]]},{"u":"kochen.html","t":"kochen","s":"to cook","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Heute koche ich Nudeln. :: Today I am cooking pasta."]]},{"u":"koennen.html","t":"können","s":"can / to be able to","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kannst du mir helfen? :: Can you help me? Könnten Sie bitte die Musik leiser machen? :: Could you please turn the music down?"],["notes","Notes","A modal verb: the second verb goes to the end as an infinitive."]]},{"u":"kollegin.html","t":"Kollegin","s":"colleague (woman)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Kollegin trinkt jeden Morgen einen Kaffee mit mir. :: My colleague has a coffee with me every morning."],["notes","Notes","A man is der Kollege , plural die Kollegen ."]]},{"u":"kommen.html","t":"kommen","s":"to come","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kommst du am Donnerstag zum Elternabend? :: Are you coming to the parents' evening on Thursday? Ich komme gleich! :: I'm coming!"]]},{"u":"komparativ-und-superlativ.html","t":"Komparativ und Superlativ","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","To compare: add -er (comparative) and am ...-sten (superlative). Many short words get an umlaut. schnell, schneller, am schnellsten; stark, stärker, am stärksten; krank, kränker, am kränksten Irregular: gut, besser, am besten; gern, lieber, am liebsten; viel, mehr, am meisten . Compare with als : Die andere Mannschaft ist stärker Equal with als wir. so ... wie : Er ist so groß wie sein Bruder."],["simple-german","Simple German","Komparativ mit -er : schneller . Superlativ mit am ...-sten : am schnellsten . Vergleich mit als : besser als ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Er ist mehr schnell. :: Er ist schneller. Sie spielt besser wie ich. :: Sie spielt besser als ich."]]},{"u":"kopf.html","t":"Kopf","s":"head","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Kopf tut weh. :: My head hurts."]]},{"u":"kosten.html","t":"kosten","s":"to cost","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Was kostet das? :: How much is that? Die Äpfel kosten zwei Euro. :: The apples cost two euros."]]},{"u":"krank.html","t":"krank","s":"ill / sick","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Tochter ist krank. :: My daughter is ill."]]},{"u":"kuchen.html","t":"Kuchen","s":"cake","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Sonntag essen wir Kuchen. :: On Sunday we eat cake."]]},{"u":"kueche.html","t":"Küche","s":"kitchen","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir essen in der Küche. :: We eat in the kitchen."]]},{"u":"kunstrasen.html","t":"Kunstrasen","s":"artificial turf, artificial pitch","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Spiel ist am Sonntag um 11 Uhr auf dem Kunstrasen. :: The match is on Sunday at 11 on the artificial pitch. Auf Kunstrasen braucht man andere Schuhe. :: On artificial turf you need different boots."],["notes","Notes","Kunst (art, artificial) plus Rasen (lawn). The opposite is der Rasenplatz (grass pitch). For several pitches say die Kunstrasenplätze ."]]},{"u":"kurz.html","t":"kurz","s":"short","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Gern, aber nur eine kurze Geschichte. :: Gladly, but only a short story. Haben Sie kurz Zeit? :: Do you have a moment?"]]},{"u":"kurze-frage-an-die-lehrerin.html","t":"Kurze Frage an die Lehrerin","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Entschuldigung, Frau A., haben Sie kurz Zeit? :: Excuse me, Ms A., do you have a moment? Lehrerin: Ja, natürlich. Was gibt's? :: Yes, of course. What is it? ich: Mein Sohn hat morgen einen Termin beim Kinderarzt. Er kommt erst um zehn Uhr in die Schule. :: My son has an appointment at the paediatrician's tomorrow. He will only come to school at ten. Lehrerin: Kein Problem. Danke, dass Sie Bescheid sagen. :: No problem. Thank you for letting me know. ich: Muss ich eine Entschuldigung schreiben? :: Do I have to write an excuse note? Lehrerin: Ja, bitte geben Sie ihm einen kurzen Zettel mit. :: Yes, please give him a short note to take. ich: Mache ich. Vielen Dank! :: I will. Thank you very much!"],["variations","Variations","6 Lehrerin: Nein, das ist nicht nötig. :: No, that's not necessary."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Teachers are Sie and Frau or Herr with the family name. Frau A. is a placeholder. erst um zehn : erst means not before ."]]},{"u":"laerm.html","t":"Lärm","s":"noise","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Nach zehn Uhr soll es keinen Lärm geben. :: After ten o'clock there should be no noise."],["notes","Notes","From 22:00 to 6:00 is Nachtruhe : quiet time in most houses."]]},{"u":"lang.html","t":"lang","s":"long","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wie lange bleibt sie zu Hause? :: How long will she stay at home? Das Spiel war heute sehr lang. :: The match was very long today."],["notes","Notes","lange (with e ) is the adverb of time: Wohnen Sie schon lange hier?"]]},{"u":"lange.html","t":"lange","s":"for a long time","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich warte schon lange. :: I have been waiting for a long time. Wie lange dauert das? :: How long does that take?"],["notes","Notes","lange is the adverb of time; lang is the adjective: eine lange Hose ."]]},{"u":"langweilig.html","t":"langweilig","s":"boring","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mathe ist langweilig, sagt mein Sohn. :: Maths is boring, my son says."]]},{"u":"laufen.html","t":"laufen","s":"to run; to walk","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich laufe jeden Morgen. :: I go running every morning."]]},{"u":"laut.html","t":"laut","s":"loud","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Es wird vielleicht ein bisschen laut. :: It might get a bit loud. Ich mache die Musik sofort leiser. :: I will turn the music down right away."],["notes","Notes","The opposite is leise , quiet: leiser machen , to turn down."]]},{"u":"leben.html","t":"leben","s":"to live","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir leben in Deutschland. :: We live in Germany."],["notes","Notes","For where your flat is, wohnen is more usual: Wir wohnen im zweiten Stock."]]},{"u":"lecker.html","t":"lecker","s":"tasty","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Pizza ist lecker! :: The pizza is tasty!"]]},{"u":"ledig.html","t":"ledig","s":"single, unmarried","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Bruder ist ledig. :: My brother is single."],["notes","Notes","ledig is the word on forms. In conversation people also say Single ."]]},{"u":"leer.html","t":"leer","s":"empty","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Brotdose ist leer. Hast du alles gegessen? :: The lunch box is empty. Did you eat everything?"]]},{"u":"lehrerin.html","t":"Lehrerin","s":"teacher (woman)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Lehrerin hat heute angerufen. :: The teacher called today."],["notes","Notes","A man is der Lehrer , plural die Lehrer . You say Frau A. or Herr B. to a teacher."]]},{"u":"leicht.html","t":"leicht","s":"easy / light","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Hausaufgaben sind heute leicht. :: The homework is easy today."]]},{"u":"leider.html","t":"leider","s":"unfortunately","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Leider nicht, ich muss arbeiten. :: Sadly not, I have to work."]]},{"u":"leise.html","t":"leise","s":"quiet / soft","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte seid leise, das Baby schläft. :: Please be quiet, the baby is sleeping. Ich mache die Musik sofort leiser. :: I'll turn the music down right away."],["notes","Notes","The opposite is laut . leiser machen : to turn down."]]},{"u":"lernen.html","t":"lernen","s":"to learn / to study","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir lernen heute für den Test. :: Today we are studying for the test."]]},{"u":"lesen.html","t":"lesen","s":"to read","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe viel gelesen und geschlafen. :: I read and slept a lot."]]},{"u":"letzte.html","t":"letzte","s":"last","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Letzte Woche war ich krank. :: Last week I was ill."],["notes","Notes","It takes adjective endings: letzte Woche , letzten Sonntag , das letzte Mal ."]]},{"u":"lieben.html","t":"lieben","s":"to love","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich liebe dich. :: I love you."]]},{"u":"liegen.html","t":"liegen","s":"to lie (be lying)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Buch liegt auf dem Tisch. :: The book is on the table."]]},{"u":"links.html","t":"links","s":"on the left","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Halle ist hinter der Schule links. :: The hall is behind the school on the left."]]},{"u":"lust-haben.html","t":"Lust haben","s":"to feel like (doing) something","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Hast du Lust auf einen Kaffee? :: Do you fancy a coffee? Hast du Lust, ins Kino zu gehen? :: Do you feel like going to the cinema? Ich habe keine Lust. :: I don't feel like it."],["usage","Usage","To invite a friend, or to say you don't want to. auf plus Akkusativ for a thing; zu plus infinitive for an activity."]]},{"u":"lust.html","t":"Lust","s":"desire / wish","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Hast du Lust auf einen Kaffee? :: Do you fancy a coffee?"],["notes","Notes","Lust haben auf plus Akkusativ: to feel like something."]]},{"u":"lustig.html","t":"lustig","s":"funny","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Film war sehr lustig. :: The film was very funny."]]},{"u":"machen.html","t":"machen","s":"to do / to make","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir haben in Mathe ein Spiel gemacht. :: We played a game in maths. Ich mache einen Kartoffelsalat. :: I will make a potato salad."]]},{"u":"mal.html","t":"mal","s":"just (softens a request)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Zeig mal! :: Show me! Mach bitte mal den Mund auf. :: Open your mouth, please."],["notes","Notes","mal makes a request sound friendly and casual."]]},{"u":"man.html","t":"man","s":"one / you / people","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","In der Halle trägt man Hallenschuhe. :: In the hall you wear indoor shoes. Wie sagt man das auf Deutsch? :: How do you say that in German?"],["notes","Notes","man takes the er form of the verb. It is used much more than English one ."]]},{"u":"manchmal.html","t":"manchmal","s":"sometimes","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Manchmal fährt die Oma die Kinder zum Training. :: Sometimes grandma drives the children to training."]]},{"u":"mann.html","t":"Mann","s":"man; husband","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Mann arbeitet heute. :: My husband is working today."]]},{"u":"mannschaft.html","t":"Mannschaft","s":"team","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir werden die Trofeo Mediterraneo besuchen, mit viel internationaleren Mannschaften. :: We will go to the Trofeo Mediterraneo, with many more international teams. Alle teilnehmenden Mannschaften richten ein Spiel aus. :: All participating teams host a match. Die andere Mannschaft ist sehr stark. :: The other team is very strong."],["notes","Notes","Feminine because of -schaft . In club language you also hear das Team ."]]},{"u":"mein.html","t":"mein","s":"my","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn spielt Fußball, meine Tochter Handball. :: My son plays football, my daughter handball."],["notes","Notes","Endings like ein . The others: dein, sein, ihr, unser, euer, ihr, Ihr ."]]},{"u":"meistens.html","t":"meistens","s":"mostly / usually","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meistens holen wir die Kinder um vier ab. :: We usually pick up the children at four."]]},{"u":"meldet-euch-gerne.html","t":"meldet euch gerne","s":"feel free to get in touch","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Wenn es Probleme mit der Bezahlung gibt, meldet euch gerne. :: If there are problems with the payment, feel free to get in touch. Melde dich gerne, wenn du Fragen hast. :: Get in touch if you have questions. Melden Sie sich gerne bei uns. :: Feel free to contact us. (formal)"],["usage","Usage","sich melden is to get in touch. gerne makes it friendly: \"you are welcome to\". Club messages to parents usually use ihr ."]]},{"u":"milch.html","t":"Milch","s":"milk","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Milch ist im Kühlschrank. :: The milk is in the fridge."]]},{"u":"minute.html","t":"Minute","s":"minute","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich komme in fünf Minuten. :: I am coming in five minutes."]]},{"u":"mir-gehts-gut.html","t":"Mir geht's gut.","s":"I'm fine.","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Gut, danke. Und dir? :: Fine, thanks. And you? Es geht. :: So-so. Nicht so gut. Ich bin erkältet. :: Not so good. I have a cold."],["usage","Usage","The answer to Wie geht's? . mir is Dativ: literally it goes well for me ."]]},{"u":"mistake-am-samstag-wir-spielen-fussball.html","t":"Am Samstag wir spielen Fußball","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Am Samstag wir spielen Fußball."],["right","Right","Am Samstag spielen wir Fußball."],["why","Why","The verb is always in position 2. When the sentence starts with a time, the subject comes after the verb."]]},{"u":"mistake-das-ist-mein-tochter.html","t":"Das ist mein Tochter","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Das ist mein Tochter."],["right","Right","Das ist meine Tochter."],["why","Why","Tochter is feminine ( die Tochter ), so the possessive takes -e : meine ."]]},{"u":"mistake-das-ist-nicht-ein-problem.html","t":"Das ist nicht ein Problem","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Das ist nicht ein Problem."],["right","Right","Das ist kein Problem."],["why","Why","nicht ein becomes kein before a noun with ein or no article."]]},{"u":"mistake-der-kind.html","t":"Der Kind","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Der Kind ist krank."],["right","Right","Das Kind ist krank."],["why","Why","Kind is neuter: das Kind . Learn every noun with its article."]]},{"u":"mistake-du-mach-die-hausaufgaben.html","t":"Du mach die Hausaufgaben!","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Du mach die Hausaufgaben!"],["right","Right","Mach die Hausaufgaben!"],["why","Why","The du imperative has no pronoun: the verb comes first, without -st ."]]},{"u":"mistake-fuenfzigzwei.html","t":"Fünfzigzwei","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Das kostet fünfzigzwei Euro."],["right","Right","Das kostet zweiundfünfzig Euro."],["why","Why","From 21 to 99, the units come first: zweiundfünfzig , two-and-fifty."]]},{"u":"mistake-halb-sieben-fuer-sieben-uhr-dreissig.html","t":"Halb sieben für 7:30","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Es ist halb sieben. (meaning 7:30)"],["right","Right","Es ist halb acht. (7:30)"],["why","Why","halb acht is half an hour before eight. Spanish las siete y media counts from seven; German counts towards eight."]]},{"u":"mistake-ich-abhole-meine-tochter.html","t":"Ich abhole meine Tochter","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Ich abhole meine Tochter um vier."],["right","Right","Ich hole meine Tochter um vier ab."],["why","Why","abholen is separable: the verb is in position 2 and ab goes to the end."]]},{"u":"mistake-ich-habe-40-jahre.html","t":"Ich habe 40 Jahre","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Ich habe 40 Jahre."],["right","Right","Ich bin 40 Jahre alt."],["why","Why","Age goes with sein : you say how old you are . Spanish tener makes haben come to mind first."]]},{"u":"mistake-ich-habe-kalt.html","t":"Ich habe kalt","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Ich habe kalt."],["right","Right","Mir ist kalt."],["why","Why","Feeling cold or hot is mir ist kalt , mir ist warm , with the person in the Dativ. Spanish says tengo frío ."]]},{"u":"mistake-ich-habe-nicht-zeit.html","t":"Ich habe nicht Zeit","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Ich habe nicht Zeit."],["right","Right","Ich habe keine Zeit."],["why","Why","A noun without article is negated with kein , not nicht . Spanish no tengo tiempo uses one word for both."]]},{"u":"mistake-ich-habe-zum-training-gegangen.html","t":"Ich habe zum Training gegangen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Ich habe zum Training gegangen."],["right","Right","Ich bin zum Training gegangen."],["why","Why","gehen is movement from one place to another, so its Perfekt takes sein ."]]},{"u":"mistake-ich-mache-zu-die-tuer.html","t":"Ich mache zu die Tür","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Ich mache zu die Tür."],["right","Right","Ich mache die Tür zu."],["why","Why","zumachen is separable: the prefix zu goes to the end of the sentence."]]},{"u":"mistake-ich-muss-gehen-heute.html","t":"Ich muss gehen heute","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Ich muss gehen heute früher."],["right","Right","Ich muss heute früher gehen."],["why","Why","With a modal verb, the second verb goes to the end of the sentence, as an infinitive."]]},{"u":"mistake-ich-sehe-der-bus.html","t":"Ich sehe der Bus","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Ich sehe der Bus."],["right","Right","Ich sehe den Bus."],["why","Why","The object of sehen is in the Akkusativ: der becomes den . Only masculine nouns change."]]},{"u":"mistake-ich-spiele-mit-mein-sohn.html","t":"Ich spiele mit mein Sohn","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Ich spiele mit mein Sohn Fußball."],["right","Right","Ich spiele mit meinem Sohn Fußball."],["why","Why","mit always takes the Dativ: mein becomes meinem for der and das words."]]},{"u":"mistake-ich-warte-fuer-dich.html","t":"Ich warte für dich","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Ich warte für dich vor der Halle."],["right","Right","Ich warte vor der Halle auf dich."],["why","Why","warten takes auf plus Akkusativ. Spanish esperar needs no preposition, English uses for ."]]},{"u":"mistake-ich-weiss-nicht-wann-beginnt-das-spiel.html","t":"Ich weiß nicht, wann beginnt das Spiel","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Ich weiß nicht, wann beginnt das Spiel."],["right","Right","Ich weiß nicht, wann das Spiel beginnt."],["why","Why","Inside a sentence, after a question word, the verb goes to the end, as after weil and dass ."]]},{"u":"mistake-kannst-du-mich-helfen.html","t":"Kannst du mich helfen?","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Kannst du mich helfen?"],["right","Right","Kannst du mir helfen?"],["why","Why","helfen takes the Dativ: mir , dir , ihm . Spanish ayudarme makes the Akkusativ feel natural."]]},{"u":"mistake-morgen-ich-gehe-zum-training.html","t":"Morgen ich gehe zum Training","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Morgen ich gehe zum Training."],["right","Right","Morgen gehe ich zum Training."],["why","Why","The verb is always in position 2. When the sentence starts with a time, the subject comes after the verb."]]},{"u":"mistake-wo-du-wohnst.html","t":"Wo du wohnst?","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Mistake"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["wrong","Wrong","Wo du wohnst?"],["right","Right","Wo wohnst du?"],["why","Why","In a W-question the verb comes right after the question word, then the subject."]]},{"u":"mit.html","t":"mit","s":"with","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich spiele mit meinem Sohn Fußball. :: I play football with my son."]]},{"u":"mitbringen.html","t":"mitbringen","s":"to bring along","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Was bringen wir mit? :: What are we bringing? Ich bringe einen Kuchen mit. :: I am bringing a cake."]]},{"u":"mitgeben.html","t":"mitgeben","s":"to give someone something to take","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte geben Sie ihm einen Zettel mit. :: Please give him a note to take."]]},{"u":"mitkommen.html","t":"mitkommen","s":"to come along","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich kann gern als Begleitung mitkommen. :: I can come along as a helper."]]},{"u":"mitnehmen.html","t":"mitnehmen","s":"to take along","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kannst du meine Tochter mitnehmen? :: Can you take my daughter along?"]]},{"u":"mitspielen.html","t":"mitspielen","s":"to play (in a team) / to join in","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kann er am Samstag mitspielen? :: Can he play on Saturday?"]]},{"u":"mittags.html","t":"mittags","s":"at midday","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mittags essen die Kinder in der Schule. :: At midday the children eat at school."]]},{"u":"modalverben.html","t":"Modalverben","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","können, müssen, dürfen, wollen, sollen and möchten say whether you can, must, may or want to do something. The modal verb is in position 2; the other verb goes to the end as an infinitive. Ich kann heute nicht kommen . Du darfst noch zehn Minuten fernsehen . Wir müssen um halb acht los . ich and er/sie have the same form and no ending: ich kann, er kann; ich muss, sie muss ."],["simple-german","Simple German","Das Modalverb steht auf Position 2, das zweite Verb am Ende: Ich muss heute arbeiten. Bei ich und er gibt es keine Endung: ich kann, er kann ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich kann kommen nicht. :: Ich kann nicht kommen. Er kannt gut spielen. :: Er kann gut spielen."]]},{"u":"moegen.html","t":"mögen","s":"to like","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn mag Pizza. :: My son likes pizza. Möchtest du auch einen Kaffee? :: Would you like a coffee too?"],["notes","Notes","möchte (ich möchte, du möchtest, er möchte) is the polite would like and is used every day."]]},{"u":"monat.html","t":"Monat","s":"month","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Kurs dauert einen Monat. :: The course lasts a month."]]},{"u":"morgen.html","t":"morgen","s":"tomorrow","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Morgen gehe ich zum Training. :: Tomorrow I am going to training."],["notes","Notes","morgen is tomorrow. der Morgen is the morning: heute Morgen , this morning."]]},{"u":"morgens-vor-der-schule.html","t":"Morgens vor der Schule","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Guten Morgen! Aufstehen, es ist schon sieben Uhr. :: Good morning! Get up, it is already seven o'clock. Kind: Ich bin noch so müde. Noch fünf Minuten, bitte! :: I am still so tired. Five more minutes, please! ich: Nein, keine Zeit. Zieh dich bitte an! Dann komm frühstücken. :: No, no time. Please get dressed! Then come and have breakfast. Kind: Was gibt es zum Frühstück? :: What is there for breakfast? ich: Brot mit Käse und einen Apfel. Hast du deine Brotdose? :: Bread with cheese and an apple. Do you have your lunch box? Kind: Ja, sie ist im Schulranzen. :: Yes, it is in the school bag. ich: Gut. Putz noch schnell die Zähne. Wir müssen um halb acht los. :: Good. Quickly brush your teeth. We have to leave at half past seven. Kind: Okay, ich komme gleich! :: OK, I'm coming!"],["variations","Variations","2 Kind: Mir ist schlecht. Ich will heute nicht in die Schule. :: I feel sick. I don't want to go to school today. 6 Kind: Nein, ich finde sie nicht! :: No, I can't find it!"],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. halb acht is 7:30: half way to eight. los müssen means to have to leave. Zieh dich an and komm are commands to a child: the Imperativ with du ."]]},{"u":"morgens.html","t":"morgens","s":"in the morning, every morning","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Morgens trinke ich einen Kaffee. :: In the morning I drink a coffee."],["notes","Notes","With -s it means every morning: morgens , mittags , abends , nachts ."]]},{"u":"muede.html","t":"müde","s":"tired","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich bin noch so müde. :: I am still so tired."]]},{"u":"muell.html","t":"Müll","s":"rubbish","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Mittwoch kommt die Müllabfuhr. :: The rubbish collection comes on Wednesday."],["notes","Notes","Germans separate rubbish: paper, packaging, organic waste and the rest."]]},{"u":"muessen.html","t":"müssen","s":"must / to have to","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir müssen um halb acht los. :: We have to leave at half past seven. Ich muss bis sechs arbeiten. :: I have to work until six."],["notes","Notes","nicht müssen means not have to : Du musst nicht kommen , you don't have to come."]]},{"u":"mutter.html","t":"Mutter","s":"mother","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Heute fährt die Mutter von einem Freund die Kinder zum Training. :: Today the mother of a friend drives the children to training."]]},{"u":"na-klar.html","t":"Na klar!","s":"Of course!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Ja, klar! :: Yes, sure! Natürlich! :: Of course!"],["usage","Usage","A friendly yes . With people you say Sie to, Natürlich or Gern sounds better."]]},{"u":"na.html","t":"na","s":"well / so","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Na, wie geht's? :: So, how are you? Na ja. Noch fünf Minuten. :: Oh well. Five more minutes."],["notes","Notes","A friendly filler between people who know each other. Na klar! means of course! ."]]},{"u":"nach-dem-spiel.html","t":"Nach dem Spiel","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Herzlichen Glückwunsch! Ihr habt gewonnen! :: Congratulations! You won! Kind: Ja! Ich habe zwei Tore geschossen. :: Yes! I scored two goals. ich: Ich habe es gesehen. Du warst super! :: I saw it. You were great! Kind: Aber am Ende war ich sehr müde. :: But at the end I was very tired. ich: Das glaube ich. Hast du Hunger? :: I believe it. Are you hungry? Kind: Ja, großen Hunger! Können wir Pizza essen? :: Yes, really hungry! Can we eat pizza? ich: Okay, heute ist ein besonderer Tag. :: OK, today is a special day."],["variations","Variations","1 ich: Schade, ihr habt verloren. Aber ihr habt gut gespielt. :: Pity, you lost. But you played well."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Hunger haben : to be hungry. German uses haben here, like Spanish tener hambre ."]]},{"u":"nach-dem-training.html","t":"Nach dem Training","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Hallo! Wie war das Training heute? :: Hi! How was training today? Trainer: Super! Dein Sohn hat zwei Tore geschossen. :: Great! Your son scored two goals. ich: Wirklich? Das freut mich! :: Really? I'm glad! Trainer: Am Samstag haben wir ein Spiel. Kann er mitspielen? :: On Saturday we have a match. Can he play? ich: Ja, klar. Wann und wo ist das Spiel? :: Yes, sure. When and where is the match? Trainer: Um zehn Uhr auf unserem Platz. Er soll um halb zehn da sein. :: At ten o'clock on our pitch. He should be there at half past nine. ich: Okay. Muss er etwas mitbringen? :: OK. Does he have to bring anything? Trainer: Nur Schienbeinschoner, Fußballschuhe und eine Flasche Wasser. Das Trikot bekommt er von uns. :: Just shin pads, football boots and a bottle of water. He gets the shirt from us."],["variations","Variations","5 ich: Leider nicht, wir besuchen am Wochenende die Großeltern. :: Sadly not, we are visiting the grandparents at the weekend."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. In many clubs the coach and the parents say du to each other. Schienbeinschoner (shin pads) are required in every match."]]},{"u":"nach-dem-weg-fragen.html","t":"Nach dem Weg fragen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Entschuldigung, wo ist der Bahnhof, bitte? :: Excuse me, where is the station, please? Frau: Gehen Sie hier geradeaus und dann an der Ampel links. :: Go straight on here and then left at the traffic light. ich: Geradeaus und dann links. Ist es weit? :: Straight on and then left. Is it far? Frau: Nein, nicht weit. Nur fünf Minuten. :: No, not far. Only five minutes. ich: Vielen Dank! :: Thank you very much! Frau: Bitte schön! :: You're welcome!"],["variations","Variations","2 Frau: Tut mir leid, ich bin nicht von hier. :: Sorry, I am not from here. 4 Frau: Ja, ein bisschen. Nehmen Sie den Bus. :: Yes, a bit. Take the bus."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Repeating the way ( Geradeaus und dann links. ) is a good check that you understood."]]},{"u":"nach.html","t":"nach","s":"after / to","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Nach dem Training essen wir zusammen. :: After training we eat together."],["notes","Notes","nach Hause : home (where to). nach also goes with towns and countries: nach Berlin ."]]},{"u":"nachbar.html","t":"Nachbar","s":"neighbour","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Unsere Nachbarn feiern am Samstag eine Party. :: Our neighbours are having a party on Saturday."],["notes","Notes","A woman is die Nachbarin , plural die Nachbarinnen ."]]},{"u":"nachfuellen.html","t":"nachfüllen","s":"to top up","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich fülle Wasser nach, bis das Manometer 2 bar zeigt. :: I top up water until the gauge shows 2 bar. Fällt der Druck in 24 Stunden unter 0,8 bar, füllen Sie bitte kein Wasser mehr nach. :: If the pressure falls below 0.8 bar within 24 hours, please do not top up any more water. Hast du schon Wasser nachgefüllt? :: Have you topped up water yet?"],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich nachfülle Wasser. :: Ich fülle Wasser nach."],["notes","Notes","nach- is separable: ich fülle nach , nachgefüllt , nachzufüllen ."]]},{"u":"nachmittags.html","t":"nachmittags","s":"in the afternoon","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Nachmittags spielen die Kinder im Garten. :: In the afternoon the children play in the garden."]]},{"u":"nachts.html","t":"nachts","s":"at night","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Nachts ist es hier sehr ruhig. :: At night it is very quiet here."]]},{"u":"naechste.html","t":"nächste","s":"next","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Nächste Woche habe ich Urlaub. :: Next week I am on holiday. Wir steigen an der nächsten Haltestelle aus. :: We get off at the next stop."],["notes","Notes","It takes adjective endings: nächste Woche , nächsten Montag , das nächste Mal ."]]},{"u":"nah.html","t":"nah","s":"near / close","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Schule ist ganz nah. :: The school is very close. Die nächste Haltestelle ist am Marktplatz. :: The nearest stop is on the market square."],["notes","Notes","nächste also means next : nächste Woche , next week."]]},{"u":"name.html","t":"Name","s":"name","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wie ist Ihr Name? :: What is your name?"]]},{"u":"natuerlich.html","t":"natürlich","s":"of course / naturally","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Natürlich, das ist kein Problem. :: Of course, that's no problem."]]},{"u":"neben.html","t":"neben","s":"next to","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Sportplatz ist neben der Schule. :: The sports ground is next to the school."]]},{"u":"nebensatz-mit-weil-dass-wenn.html","t":"Nebensatz mit weil, dass, wenn","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","After weil (because), dass (that), wenn (if, when) and ob (whether), the conjugated verb goes to the end of the clause. A comma always separates the two clauses. Ich rufe an, weil meine Tochter krank ist . Danke, dass Sie Bescheid sagen . Ich weiß nicht, ob er heute mitspielen kann . Question words work the same way inside a sentence: Weißt du, wann das Spiel anfängt ? When the subordinate clause comes first, the main clause starts with its verb: Wenn es regnet, fällt das Training aus."],["simple-german","Simple German","Nach weil, dass, wenn, ob steht das Verb am Ende: ..., weil ich arbeiten muss."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich komme nicht, weil ich muss arbeiten. :: Ich komme nicht, weil ich arbeiten muss. Ich weiß nicht, wann beginnt das Spiel. :: Ich weiß nicht, wann das Spiel beginnt."]]},{"u":"nehmen.html","t":"nehmen","s":"to take","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich nehme einen Kaffee, bitte. :: I'll have a coffee, please."],["notes","Notes","When ordering, ich nehme means I'll have ."]]},{"u":"nein.html","t":"nein","s":"no","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Nein, keine Zeit. :: No, no time."],["notes","Notes","To say yes to a negative question, use doch ."]]},{"u":"nett.html","t":"nett","s":"kind / nice","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das ist sehr nett von Ihnen. :: That is very kind of you."]]},{"u":"neu.html","t":"neu","s":"new","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich bin die neue Nachbarin. :: I'm the new neighbour. Mein Sohn braucht neue Fußballschuhe. :: My son needs new football boots."]]},{"u":"neun.html","t":"neun","s":"nine","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Treffpunkt ist um neun Uhr am Vereinsheim. :: The meeting point is at nine o'clock at the clubhouse."]]},{"u":"neunte.html","t":"neunte","s":"ninth","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Heute ist der neunte Juni. :: Today is the ninth of June."]]},{"u":"neunzehn.html","t":"neunzehn","s":"nineteen","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Es ist neunzehn Uhr. :: It is seven p.m."]]},{"u":"neunzehnte.html","t":"neunzehnte","s":"nineteenth","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am neunzehnten ist die Schule zu Ende. :: On the nineteenth school ends."]]},{"u":"neunzig.html","t":"neunzig","s":"ninety","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Opa ist neunzig. :: Grandpa is ninety."]]},{"u":"nicht-oder-kein.html","t":"Nicht oder kein","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","kein negates a noun that would have ein or no article: Ich habe keine Zeit. Das ist kein Problem. Wir haben keinen Ball. nicht negates everything else: verbs, adjectives, names and nouns with der, die, das : Ich komme nicht . Das Training ist nicht heute. Das ist nicht der Trainer."],["simple-german","Simple German","kein vor Nomen ohne Artikel oder mit ein : keine Zeit . Sonst nicht : Ich komme nicht."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich habe nicht Zeit. :: Ich habe keine Zeit. Das ist nicht ein Problem. :: Das ist kein Problem."]]},{"u":"nicht.html","t":"nicht","s":"not","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich komme heute nicht. :: I'm not coming today. Das ist nicht schlimm. :: That's not bad."],["notes","Notes","nicht negates verbs, adjectives and nouns with der, die, das . A noun with ein or no article takes kein ."]]},{"u":"nichts.html","t":"nichts","s":"nothing","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das macht nichts. :: It doesn't matter. Ich habe nichts gehört. :: I didn't hear anything."]]},{"u":"nie.html","t":"nie","s":"never","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn räumt nie sein Zimmer auf. :: My son never tidies his room."]]},{"u":"niemand.html","t":"niemand","s":"nobody","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Niemand hat die Sporttasche gesehen. :: Nobody has seen the sports bag."]]},{"u":"noch.html","t":"noch","s":"still / yet / more","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich bin noch so müde. :: I'm still so tired. Noch fünf Minuten, bitte! :: Five more minutes, please!"],["notes","Notes","noch nicht : not yet. noch einmal : once more."]]},{"u":"notfall-hotline.html","t":"Notfall-Hotline","s":"emergency hotline","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Notfall-Hotline ist nur für technische Störungen. :: The emergency hotline is only for technical faults."]]},{"u":"null.html","t":"null","s":"zero","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Telefonnummer beginnt mit null. :: My phone number starts with zero."]]},{"u":"nur.html","t":"nur","s":"only / just","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Nur Schienbeinschoner, Fußballschuhe und eine Flasche Wasser. :: Just shin pads, football boots and a bottle of water."]]},{"u":"ob.html","t":"ob","s":"whether / if","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kannst du mir Bescheid sagen, ob ihr kommt? :: Can you let me know whether you are coming?"],["notes","Notes","ob for a yes-or-no question inside a sentence; wenn for a condition."]]},{"u":"oben.html","t":"oben","s":"upstairs / above","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die neue Nachbarin wohnt oben im zweiten Stock. :: The new neighbour lives upstairs on the second floor."]]},{"u":"oder.html","t":"oder","s":"or","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Spielst du Fußball oder Handball? :: Do you play football or handball?"]]},{"u":"offen.html","t":"offen","s":"open","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Supermarkt ist bis acht Uhr offen. :: The supermarket is open until eight o'clock. Das Fenster ist offen. :: The window is open."]]},{"u":"oft.html","t":"oft","s":"often","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir grillen im Sommer oft mit Freunden. :: In summer we often have barbecues with friends."]]},{"u":"oh.html","t":"oh","s":"oh","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Oh, gute Besserung! :: Oh, get well soon!"]]},{"u":"ohne.html","t":"ohne","s":"without","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mit Milch, ohne Zucker, bitte. :: With milk, no sugar, please."]]},{"u":"okay.html","t":"okay","s":"OK","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Okay, bis morgen! :: OK, see you tomorrow!"],["notes","Notes","Also written OK or o.k."]]},{"u":"paket.html","t":"Paket","s":"parcel","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe ein Paket für Sie. :: I have a parcel for you."]]},{"u":"passiv-mit-werden.html","t":"Passiv mit werden","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Club and school messages use the passive when what happens matters more than who does it : werden plus the participle at the end. With a modal verb, the modal is conjugated and werden goes to the end as an infinitive. Die Abfahrtszeit wird noch bekannt gegeben. :: The departure time will still be announced. Das Spiel wurde verschoben. :: The match was postponed. Das Spiel musste verschoben werden. :: The match had to be postponed. Without a subject, the passive says only that something happens: es wird or a word like hier comes first. Leider wird hier oft sehr schnell gefahren. :: Sadly, people often drive very fast here."],["simple-german","Simple German","Passiv: werden + Partizip. Wichtig ist, was passiert, nicht wer es macht. Mit Modalverb: muss ... verschoben werden ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Das Spiel musste verschoben wird. :: Das Spiel musste verschoben werden. Die Zeit wird bekannt geben. :: Die Zeit wird bekannt gegeben."]]},{"u":"pause.html","t":"Pause","s":"break","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","In der Pause essen die Kinder ihr Frühstück. :: In the break the children eat their snack."]]},{"u":"perfekt-mit-haben-oder-sein.html","t":"Perfekt mit haben oder sein","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","The Perfekt is the past tense of conversation: haben or sein in position 2, the participle at the end. Ich habe gestern Fußball gespielt . Wir sind mit dem Bus gefahren . Verbs of movement from one place to another and of change of state take sein : gehen, kommen, fahren, aufstehen, bleiben , and sein itself. Most others take haben . Participles: regular ge-...-t ( gespielt, gemacht ), irregular ge-...-en ( gegangen, geschossen ); no ge- for verbs in -ieren and with be- , ver- : trainiert, besucht, verloren ."],["simple-german","Simple German","Perfekt: haben oder sein plus Partizip am Ende. Bewegung oder Veränderung: mit sein : Ich bin gegangen. Sonst mit haben : Ich habe gespielt."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich habe zum Training gegangen. :: Ich bin zum Training gegangen. Wir haben gewinnt. :: Wir haben gewonnen."]]},{"u":"personalpronomen.html","t":"Personalpronomen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Nominativ Akkusativ Dativ ich mich mir du dich dir er ihn ihm sie sie ihr es es ihm wir uns uns ihr euch euch sie / Sie sie / Sie ihnen / Ihnen Ich rufe (Akkusativ, dich an anrufen ). Ich helfe (Dativ, dir helfen ). Gib mir den Ball! er and sie also stand for things: der Ball, . er ist weg; die Brotdose, ich finde sie nicht"],["simple-german","Simple German","ich, mich, mir; du, dich, dir; er, ihn, ihm; sie, sie, ihr . Nach anrufen : Akkusativ. Nach helfen : Dativ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Kannst du mich helfen? :: Kannst du mir helfen? Ich rufe ihm an. :: Ich rufe ihn an."]]},{"u":"platz.html","t":"Platz","s":"pitch / seat / square","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Spiel ist um zehn Uhr auf unserem Platz. :: The match is at ten o'clock on our pitch. Ich habe drei Plätze frei. :: I have three free seats."]]},{"u":"possessivartikel.html","t":"Possessivartikel","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Possessive articles say whose something is. They take the endings of ein . ich: mein , du: dein , er: sein , sie: ihr , wir: unser , ihr: euer , sie: ihr , Sie: Ihr mein Sohn, meine Tochter, mein Kind, meine Kinder. Ich spiele mit meinem Sohn. sein belongs to a man, ihr to a woman, whatever the gender of the thing: Sie holt ihren Sohn ab."],["simple-german","Simple German","mein, dein, sein, ihr, unser, euer, Ihr haben die Endungen von ein : meine Tochter, meinen Sohn ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Sie holt seinen Sohn ab. :: Sie holt ihren Sohn ab. Mein Tochter ist krank. :: Meine Tochter ist krank."]]},{"u":"praesens.html","t":"Präsens","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","The present tense: take the stem ( spiel- ) and add the ending for the person. ich spiel e , du spiel st , er/sie spiel t , wir spiel en , ihr spiel t , sie/Sie spiel en Some irregular verbs change their vowel with du and er/sie : fahren, du fährst ; helfen, du hilfst ; lesen, du liest . Stems that end in -t or -d add an e : du arbeitest, er wartet . The present tense also speaks about the future when a time is given: Morgen rufe ich dich an."],["simple-german","Simple German","Präsens: Stamm plus Endung: -e, -st, -t, -en, -t, -en . Manche Verben ändern den Vokal bei du und er : du fährst, er hilft ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Du fahrst zum Training. :: Du fährst zum Training. Er arbeit viel. :: Er arbeitet viel."]]},{"u":"praeteritum-von-sein-und-haben.html","t":"Präteritum von sein und haben","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","For sein , haben and the modal verbs, Germans use the Präteritum in speech instead of the Perfekt. sein : ich war, du warst, er war, wir waren, ihr wart, sie waren haben : ich hatte, du hattest, er hatte, wir hatten, ihr hattet, sie hatten Wie war dein Wochenende? Heute Morgen hatte er Fieber. Ich konnte nicht kommen."],["simple-german","Simple German","sein und haben in der Vergangenheit: ich war, ich hatte . Man sagt Ich war krank , nicht Ich bin krank gewesen ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Wie ist dein Wochenende gewesen? :: Wie war dein Wochenende?"]]},{"u":"privatgrundstueck.html","t":"Privatgrundstück","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Photo"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["transcription","Transcription","Privatgrundstück Unbefugtes Betreten und Befahren verboten! Unbefugtes Parken auf eigene Gefahr! Eingeschränkter Winterdienst! [Landkreis]"],["meaning","Meaning","Private property. Entering on foot or by car without permission is forbidden. If you park here without permission, you do so at your own risk: the owner is not responsible for damage and may have your car towed. The snow and ice are only partly cleared in winter ( Winterdienst is the clearing service)."]]},{"u":"puenktlich.html","t":"pünktlich","s":"on time / punctual","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte seid immer pünktlich. :: Please always be on time. Der Bus ist heute nicht pünktlich. :: The bus is not on time today."]]},{"u":"putzen.html","t":"putzen","s":"to clean / to brush","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Hast du die Zähne geputzt? :: Have you brushed your teeth?"]]},{"u":"rechts.html","t":"rechts","s":"on the right","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Toilette ist hier rechts. :: The toilet is here on the right."]]},{"u":"reflexive-verben.html","t":"Reflexive Verben","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Some verbs need a reflexive pronoun: the action goes back to the subject. mich, dich, sich, uns, euch, sich Ich ziehe mich an. Zieh dich an! Wir treffen uns um drei. Die Kinder freuen sich . Common ones: sich anziehen, sich beeilen, sich freuen, sich treffen, sich ausruhen, sich anmelden ."],["simple-german","Simple German","Reflexive Verben haben ein Pronomen: ich freue mich, du freust dich, er freut sich ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich freue auf das Spiel. :: Ich freue mich auf das Spiel. Wir treffen um drei. :: Wir treffen uns um drei."]]},{"u":"regen.html","t":"Regen","s":"rain","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Morgen kommt Regen. :: Rain is coming tomorrow."]]},{"u":"regnen.html","t":"regnen","s":"to rain","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Heute regnet es. :: It is raining today."],["notes","Notes","Always with es : Es regnet."]]},{"u":"reisen.html","t":"reisen","s":"to travel","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Im Sommer reisen wir nach Spanien. :: In summer we travel to Spain."]]},{"u":"reservierung-waermepumpe-foerderung-und-vollmacht.html","t":"Reservierung einer Wärmepumpe: Förderung und Vollmacht","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Text"],"Level":["B2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Der Kunde reserviert hiermit ein Wärmepumpensystem für das Gebäude auf dem Grundstück [Adresse]. The customer hereby reserves a heat pump system for the building on the property [address]. Bitte prüfen Sie die nachstehenden förderrelevanten Angaben gründlich. Sie dienen als Grundlage des Angebotes und der Förderung. Please check the following details relevant to the subsidy carefully. They are the basis of the offer and of the subsidy. Bedingung ist, dass Sie im Grundbuch eingetragen sind und der Bauantrag zum Zeitpunkt der Antragsstellung mindestens 5 Jahre zurückliegt. The condition is that you are registered in the land register and that the building application was made at least 5 years before the subsidy application. Bedingung ist, dass Sie als Eigentümer die Wohneinheit zum Zeitpunkt der Antragsstellung als Haupt- bzw. alleinige Wohnung bewohnen. The condition is that, as the owner, you live in the dwelling as your main or only home at the time of the application. Erforderlicher Nachweis ist ein Grundbuchauszug und eine amtliche Meldebescheinigung. The proof required is an extract from the land register and an official certificate of registration. Ich werde für den Erwerb und den Einbau der Wärmepumpe auch keinen Antrag auf steuerliche oder sonstige Förderung stellen. I will also not apply for any tax or other subsidy for the purchase and installation of the heat pump. Die Parteien bevollmächtigen sich gegen- und wechselseitig, in ihrem Namen Erklärungen gegenüber der Firma A abzugeben sowie entgegenzunehmen. The parties authorise each other to make and receive declarations to and from company A in their name. Diese Vollmacht tritt mit Unterzeichnung in Kraft und bleibt bis zu ihrem ausdrücklichen Widerruf in Schriftform gegenüber der Firma A gültig. This power of attorney comes into force when it is signed and stays valid until it is expressly revoked in writing to company A."],["notes","Notes","Extracts of a reservation signed before the contract. The company name is replaced by Firma A and the address by a placeholder; prices and personal data are left out. Antrag stellen and beantragen mean the same: to apply. in Kraft treten : to come into force. Widerruf is the noun of widerrufen ."]]},{"u":"rezept.html","t":"Rezept","s":"prescription / recipe","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich schreibe Ihnen ein Rezept für einen Saft. :: I will write you a prescription for a syrup."]]},{"u":"richtig.html","t":"richtig","s":"right / correct","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ist die Antwort richtig? :: Is the answer right? Ja, das ist richtig. :: Yes, that is right."],["notes","Notes","A person is right with recht haben , not richtig ."]]},{"u":"rot.html","t":"rot","s":"red","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Ampel ist rot. Wir warten. :: The traffic light is red. We wait."]]},{"u":"ruhig.html","t":"ruhig","s":"quiet / calm","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Haus ist sehr ruhig. :: The house is very quiet."]]},{"u":"sagen.html","t":"sagen","s":"to say","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Was sagt die Lehrerin? :: What does the teacher say?"]]},{"u":"sauber.html","t":"sauber","s":"clean","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das T-Shirt ist wieder sauber. :: The T-shirt is clean again."]]},{"u":"schade.html","t":"Schade!","s":"What a pity!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Schade, ihr habt verloren. :: Pity, you lost. Das ist aber schade! :: That's a real pity!"],["usage","Usage","When something did not work out."]]},{"u":"schieberegler.html","t":"Schieberegler","s":"slider","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mit dem Schieberegler in der App stelle ich die Heizung wärmer. :: With the slider in the app I turn the heating up. Schieben Sie den Schieberegler im Urlaub nach links. :: Move the slider to the left when you are on holiday."]]},{"u":"schiedsrichter.html","t":"Schiedsrichter","s":"referee","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Schiedsrichter hat recht. :: The referee is right."]]},{"u":"schiessen.html","t":"schießen","s":"to shoot","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Dein Sohn hat zwei Tore geschossen. :: Your son scored two goals."],["notes","Notes","ein Tor schießen : to score a goal."]]},{"u":"schlafen.html","t":"schlafen","s":"to sleep","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Schlaf gut! :: Sleep well! Meine Kinder können nicht schlafen. :: My children cannot sleep."]]},{"u":"schlecht.html","t":"schlecht","s":"bad","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Wetter ist heute schlecht. :: The weather is bad today. Mir geht es schlecht. :: I am not feeling well."]]},{"u":"schlimm.html","t":"schlimm","s":"bad / serious","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ist es schlimm? :: Is it bad? Nicht so schlimm! :: Never mind!"]]},{"u":"schluessel.html","t":"Schlüssel","s":"key","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich finde meinen Schlüssel nicht. :: I can't find my key."]]},{"u":"schmecken.html","t":"schmecken","s":"to taste","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das schmeckt sehr gut! :: That tastes very good! Schmeckt es dir? :: Do you like it?"]]},{"u":"schmutzig.html","t":"schmutzig","s":"dirty","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Nach dem Training sind die Schuhe immer schmutzig. :: After training the boots are always dirty."]]},{"u":"schnell.html","t":"schnell","s":"fast / quick","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Putz noch schnell die Zähne. :: Quickly brush your teeth."]]},{"u":"schoen.html","t":"schön","s":"nice / beautiful","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Wetter ist heute schön. :: The weather is nice today. Einen schönen Tag noch! :: Have a nice day!"]]},{"u":"schoenes-wochenende.html","t":"Schönes Wochenende!","s":"Have a nice weekend!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Danke, gleichfalls! :: Thanks, you too! Einen schönen Tag noch! :: Have a nice day!"],["usage","Usage","Said on Friday at work or at the school gate. The answer is Danke, gleichfalls!"]]},{"u":"schon.html","t":"schon","s":"already","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Es ist schon sieben Uhr. :: It is already seven o'clock."]]},{"u":"schreiben.html","t":"schreiben","s":"to write","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich schreibe der Lehrerin eine Nachricht. :: I write the teacher a message."]]},{"u":"schuh.html","t":"Schuh","s":"shoe","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wo sind meine Schuhe? :: Where are my shoes?"]]},{"u":"schule.html","t":"Schule","s":"school","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wie war's in der Schule? :: How was school? Morgen ist Schule. :: There is school tomorrow."]]},{"u":"schulranzen.html","t":"Schulranzen","s":"school bag","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Brotdose ist im Schulranzen. :: The lunch box is in the school bag."],["notes","Notes","In the first school years German children carry a Schulranzen on their back."]]},{"u":"schwarz.html","t":"schwarz","s":"black","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Handy ist schwarz. :: My mobile phone is black. Ich trinke den Kaffee schwarz. :: I drink my coffee black."]]},{"u":"schwer.html","t":"schwer","s":"difficult / heavy","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Aufgabe ist so schwer. :: The task is so hard."],["notes","Notes","The opposite is leicht : easy, light."]]},{"u":"schwester.html","t":"Schwester","s":"sister","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Schwester hat zwei Kinder. :: My sister has two children."]]},{"u":"schwimmen.html","t":"schwimmen","s":"to swim","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Im Sommer schwimmen wir im See. :: In summer we swim in the lake."]]},{"u":"sechs.html","t":"sechs","s":"six","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir fangen um sechs Uhr an. :: We start at six o'clock."]]},{"u":"sechste.html","t":"sechste","s":"sixth","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am sechsten Dezember ist Nikolaus. :: On the sixth of December it is St Nicholas' Day."]]},{"u":"sechzehn.html","t":"sechzehn","s":"sixteen","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn ist sechzehn. :: My son is sixteen."],["notes","Notes","Not sechszehn : the s of sechs drops."]]},{"u":"sechzehnte.html","t":"sechzehnte","s":"sixteenth","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Heute ist der sechzehnte April. :: Today is the sixteenth of April."]]},{"u":"sechzig.html","t":"sechzig","s":"sixty","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Vater ist sechzig. :: My father is sixty."],["notes","Notes","Not sechszig ."]]},{"u":"sehen.html","t":"sehen","s":"to see","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Siehst du den Bus? :: Can you see the bus?"]]},{"u":"sehr.html","t":"sehr","s":"very / very much","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das ist sehr nett von Ihnen. :: That's very kind of you."]]},{"u":"sein-zu-infinitiv.html","t":"sein + zu + Infinitiv","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["B2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Contracts and official letters say what must (or can ) be done with sein + zu + infinitive at the end. It works like a passive with müssen or können : nobody is named. With a separable verb, zu goes between the prefix and the verb: abzugeben . Der volle Gesamtkaufpreis ist an die Firma A zu zahlen. :: The full purchase price must be paid to company A. Über die Abnahme ist ein Protokoll zu erstellen. :: A record must be made of the acceptance. Die Lieferung ist vom Kunden auf einem Lieferschein zu bestätigen. :: The delivery must be confirmed by the customer on a delivery note. Das Formular ist bis Freitag abzugeben. :: The form must be handed in by Friday."],["simple-german","Simple German","ist ... zu zahlen = muss bezahlt werden . Man sagt nicht, wer es macht."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Der Preis ist an die Firma zu gezahlt. :: Der Preis ist an die Firma zu zahlen. Das Formular ist bis Freitag zu abgeben. :: Das Formular ist bis Freitag abzugeben."]]},{"u":"sein.html","t":"sein","s":"to be","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Tochter ist krank. :: My daughter is ill. Du warst super! :: You were great!"],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich habe 40 Jahre. :: Ich bin 40 Jahre alt."]]},{"u":"seit.html","t":"seit","s":"since / for","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir wohnen seit drei Jahren hier. :: We have lived here for three years."],["notes","Notes","German uses the present tense with seit where English uses have been ."]]},{"u":"sekretariat.html","t":"Sekretariat","s":"school office","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich rufe im Sekretariat an, wenn mein Kind krank ist. :: I call the school office when my child is ill."]]},{"u":"selten.html","t":"selten","s":"rarely","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich esse selten Fleisch. :: I rarely eat meat."],["notes","Notes","From least to most: nie , selten , manchmal , oft , immer ."]]},{"u":"sich.html","t":"sich","s":"oneself / each other","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Kinder freuen sich. :: The children are happy. Die Eltern treffen sich am Donnerstag. :: The parents meet on Thursday."],["notes","Notes","The reflexive pronoun of er, sie, es, sie (plural) and Sie . The others are mich, dich, uns, euch ."]]},{"u":"sicherung.html","t":"Sicherung","s":"fuse","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Schalten Sie die Sicherung auch im Urlaub nicht aus. :: Do not switch off the fuse even on holiday. Die Sicherung ist rausgeflogen. :: The fuse has tripped."],["notes","Notes","rausfliegen is colloquial for a fuse that trips. In IT, die Sicherung ( die Datensicherung ) is a backup."]]},{"u":"sie.html","t":"sie","s":"she / it / they","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich hole sie um Viertel nach vier ab. :: I will pick her up at quarter past four."],["notes","Notes","With a capital letter, Sie is the polite you : Können Sie mir helfen? Its Dativ is Ihnen ."]]},{"u":"sieben.html","t":"sieben","s":"seven","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Sie ist die Nummer sieben, im Tor. :: She is number seven, in goal."],["notes","Notes","Not to be confused with the verb sieben (to sieve), which you will hardly need."]]},{"u":"siebte.html","t":"siebte","s":"seventh","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn ist in der siebten Klasse. :: My son is in seventh grade."],["notes","Notes","Not siebente in everyday German: siebte ."]]},{"u":"siebzehn.html","t":"siebzehn","s":"seventeen","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Geschäft macht um siebzehn Uhr zu. :: The shop closes at five p.m."],["notes","Notes","Not siebenzehn : the en of sieben drops."]]},{"u":"siebzehnte.html","t":"siebzehnte","s":"seventeenth","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am siebzehnten fahren wir in den Urlaub. :: On the seventeenth we go on holiday."]]},{"u":"siebzig.html","t":"siebzig","s":"seventy","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Oma ist siebzig Jahre alt. :: My grandma is seventy years old."],["notes","Notes","Not siebenzig ."]]},{"u":"situation-am-schultor.html","t":"Am Schultor","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Short talks with other parents and the teacher when you bring or pick up your child."],["i-can","I can","Ich kann andere Eltern begrüßen und fragen, wie es ihnen geht. :: I can greet other parents and ask how they are. Ich kann die Lehrerin kurz etwas fragen. :: I can ask the teacher a quick question. Ich kann sagen, dass mein Kind später kommt oder früher geht. :: I can say that my child is coming later or leaving earlier."]]},{"u":"situation-bei-der-arbeit.html","t":"Bei der Arbeit","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Small talk with colleagues and short requests to the boss."],["i-can","I can","Ich kann in der Kaffeepause über das Wochenende sprechen. :: I can talk about the weekend in the coffee break. Ich kann fragen, ob ich früher gehen kann. :: I can ask whether I can leave earlier. Ich kann eine kurze E-Mail über einen Termin verstehen. :: I can understand a short email about a meeting."]]},{"u":"situation-beim-kinderarzt.html","t":"Beim Kinderarzt","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Getting an appointment and talking to the paediatrician when a child is ill."],["i-can","I can","Ich kann am Telefon einen Termin vereinbaren. :: I can make an appointment on the phone. Ich kann sagen, was mein Kind hat und seit wann. :: I can say what is wrong with my child and since when. Ich kann fragen, was wir tun sollen und ob wir ein Rezept bekommen. :: I can ask what we should do and whether we get a prescription."]]},{"u":"situation-einkaufen.html","t":"Einkaufen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Shopping for the family: the bakery, the supermarket, paying at the till."],["i-can","I can","Ich kann beim Bäcker Brot und Brötchen kaufen. :: I can buy bread and rolls at the bakery. Ich kann fragen, was etwas kostet. :: I can ask what something costs. Ich kann sagen, wie ich bezahle. :: I can say how I am paying."]]},{"u":"situation-elternabend.html","t":"Elternabend","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","The evening meeting of the parents of a class with the teacher, a few times a year."],["i-can","I can","Ich kann auf eine Einladung antworten. :: I can reply to an invitation. Ich kann eine Frage zum Ausflug stellen. :: I can ask a question about the trip. Ich kann meine Hilfe anbieten. :: I can offer my help."]]},{"u":"situation-fussballspiel.html","t":"Fußballspiel","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-can","I can","Ich kann verstehen, wann und wo das Treffen vor dem Spiel ist. :: I can understand when and where the meeting before the match is. Ich kann verstehen, dass ein Spiel verschoben wurde und wann der neue Termin ist. :: I can understand that a match was postponed and when the new date is. Ich kann fragen, ob mein Sohn am Wochenende spielt. :: I can ask whether my son is playing at the weekend."]]},{"u":"situation-fussballtraining.html","t":"Fußballtraining","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-can","I can","Ich kann dem Trainer schreiben, dass mein Sohn heute nicht zum Training kommt. :: I can write to the coach that my son is not coming to training today. Ich kann fragen, wann die Kinder zum Training da sein sollen. :: I can ask when the children should be at training. Ich kann eine Nachricht des Trainers in der WhatsApp-Gruppe verstehen. :: I can understand a message from the coach in the WhatsApp group. Ich kann den Trainer fragen, wie das Training war. :: I can ask the coach how training was. Ich kann fragen, wann und wo das nächste Spiel ist. :: I can ask when and where the next match is. Ich kann eine Fahrgemeinschaft mit anderen Eltern organisieren. :: I can organise a lift share with other parents."]]},{"u":"situation-handballspiel.html","t":"Handballspiel","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Handball matches at the weekend: on the stand with other parents and with your child after the game."],["i-can","I can","Ich kann auf der Tribüne über das Spiel sprechen. :: I can talk about the match on the stand. Ich kann nach dem Spiel gratulieren oder trösten. :: I can congratulate or comfort after the match. Ich kann den Spielplan lesen. :: I can read the match schedule."]]},{"u":"situation-heizungstausch.html","t":"Heizungstausch","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-can","I can","Ich kann die wichtigsten Punkte im Kaufvertrag verstehen: Raten, Abnahme und Förderung. :: I can understand the main points of the purchase contract: instalments, acceptance and subsidy. Ich kann den Monteuren den Heizungsraum und den Zählerschrank zeigen. :: I can show the fitters the boiler room and the meter cabinet. Ich kann fragen, wie lange die Montage dauert und wann die Abnahme ist. :: I can ask how long the installation takes and when the acceptance is. Ich kann der Firma mitteilen, dass die Förderung bewilligt ist. :: I can tell the company that the subsidy has been approved."]]},{"u":"situation-im-treppenhaus.html","t":"Im Treppenhaus","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Meeting the neighbours in the stairwell: greetings, parcels, noise and notes on the wall."],["i-can","I can","Ich kann mich einer neuen Nachbarin vorstellen. :: I can introduce myself to a new neighbour. Ich kann ein Paket für die Nachbarn annehmen und abgeben. :: I can accept a parcel for the neighbours and hand it over. Ich kann höflich sagen, dass etwas zu laut ist. :: I can say politely that something is too loud. Ich kann einen Zettel der Hausverwaltung verstehen. :: I can understand a note from the property management."]]},{"u":"situation-kind-krank-melden.html","t":"Kind krank melden","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Calling the school office in the morning when your child is ill."],["i-can","I can","Ich kann am Telefon sagen, wer ich bin und in welche Klasse mein Kind geht. :: I can say on the phone who I am and which class my child is in. Ich kann sagen, was mein Kind hat und wie lange es zu Hause bleibt. :: I can say what is wrong with my child and how long they will stay at home. Ich kann mich am Telefon verabschieden. :: I can say goodbye on the phone."]]},{"u":"situation-mannschaftsfahrt.html","t":"Mannschaftsfahrt","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-can","I can","Ich kann die Infos zur Fahrt verstehen: Abfahrt, Kosten, Anmeldung. :: I can understand the trip information: departure, costs, registration. Ich kann fragen, ob man in Raten zahlen kann. :: I can ask whether you can pay in instalments. Ich kann beim Waffelverkauf meine Hilfe anbieten. :: I can offer my help at the waffle sale."]]},{"u":"situation-mit-freunden.html","t":"Mit Freunden","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Making plans with friends: a coffee, a barbecue, a birthday party."],["i-can","I can","Ich kann einen Freund oder eine Freundin einladen. :: I can invite a friend. Ich kann eine Einladung annehmen oder höflich absagen. :: I can accept an invitation or decline politely. Ich kann fragen, was ich mitbringen soll. :: I can ask what I should bring."]]},{"u":"situation-parken.html","t":"Parken","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-can","I can","Ich kann ein Halteverbot mit Zusatzzeichen verstehen. :: I can understand a no-stopping sign with an extra plate. Ich kann fragen, ob ich hier kurz halten darf. :: I can ask whether I may stop here for a moment. Ich kann verstehen, wo ich auf keinen Fall parken darf. :: I can understand where I must never park."]]},{"u":"situation-unterwegs.html","t":"Unterwegs","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Getting around town: asking the way, taking the bus, finding a stop."],["i-can","I can","Ich kann nach dem Weg fragen und die Antwort verstehen. :: I can ask the way and understand the answer. Ich kann fragen, wo ich aussteigen muss. :: I can ask where I have to get off."]]},{"u":"situation-waermepumpe-pruefen.html","t":"Wärmepumpe prüfen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-can","I can","Ich kann den Anlagendruck ablesen und Wasser nachfüllen. :: I can read the system pressure and top up water. Ich kann die Heizkörper entlüften. :: I can bleed the radiators. Ich kann der Notfall-Hotline eine Störung beschreiben. :: I can describe a fault to the emergency hotline."]]},{"u":"situation-wanderung.html","t":"Wanderung","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-can","I can","Ich kann Warnschilder am Wanderweg und im Wald verstehen. :: I can understand warning signs on the trail and in the forest. Ich kann im Notfall die 112 anrufen und einen Rettungspunkt nennen. :: In an emergency I can call 112 and name a rescue point."]]},{"u":"situation-zu-hause.html","t":"Zu Hause","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Everyday life with the children: getting up, breakfast, homework, bedtime and house rules."],["i-can","I can","Ich kann die Kinder am Morgen wecken und sagen, was sie tun müssen. :: I can wake the children in the morning and tell them what to do. Ich kann fragen, wie es in der Schule war. :: I can ask how school was. Ich kann bei den Hausaufgaben helfen und einfache Regeln sagen. :: I can help with homework and state simple rules. Ich kann Gute Nacht sagen und eine kurze Geschichte vorlesen. :: I can say good night and read a short story aloud."]]},{"u":"situation-zugfahrt.html","t":"Zugfahrt","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Situation"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["i-can","I can","Ich kann auf der Anzeige im Zug lesen, wann und wo der Zug hält. :: I can read on the display in the train when and where the train stops. Ich kann den Halteknopf drücken, wenn der Zug nur bei Bedarf hält. :: I can press the stop button when the train only stops on request. Ich kann fragen, ob dieser Zug zum Hauptbahnhof fährt. :: I can ask whether this train goes to the main station."]]},{"u":"sitzen.html","t":"sitzen","s":"to sit","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir sitzen in der Küche. :: We are sitting in the kitchen."]]},{"u":"sofort.html","t":"sofort","s":"immediately","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich mache die Musik sofort leiser. :: I'll turn the music down right away."]]},{"u":"sohn.html","t":"Sohn","s":"son","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn spielt am Samstag Fußball. :: My son plays football on Saturday."]]},{"u":"sollen.html","t":"sollen","s":"should / to be supposed to","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Er soll um halb zehn da sein. :: He should be there at half past nine. Sollen wir etwas mitbringen? :: Should we bring something?"]]},{"u":"sondern.html","t":"sondern","s":"but (rather)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Morgen arbeite ich nicht im Büro, sondern von zu Hause. :: Tomorrow I'm not working in the office but from home."],["notes","Notes","After a negation, sondern gives the right alternative. Otherwise but is aber ."]]},{"u":"sonst.html","t":"sonst","s":"otherwise / else","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Beeil dich, sonst kommen wir zu spät. :: Hurry up, otherwise we'll be late."]]},{"u":"spaet.html","t":"spät","s":"late","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wie spät ist es? :: What time is it?"]]},{"u":"spannend.html","t":"spannend","s":"exciting","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Zehn zu zehn. Es ist sehr spannend! :: Ten all. It's very exciting!"]]},{"u":"spende.html","t":"Spende","s":"donation","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Auch über kleine Spenden freuen wir uns sehr. :: We are also very happy about small donations. Wir möchten nicht ausschließlich auf Spenden angewiesen sein. :: We don't want to depend only on donations."]]},{"u":"spiel.html","t":"Spiel","s":"match / game","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Samstag haben wir ein Spiel. :: On Saturday we have a match."],["notes","Notes","Heimspiel : home match. Auswärtsspiel : away match."]]},{"u":"spielen.html","t":"spielen","s":"to play","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Tochter spielt Handball. :: My daughter plays handball. Ihr habt gut gespielt. :: You played well."]]},{"u":"spielplan-der-handballmannschaft.html","t":"Spielplan der Handballmannschaft","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Text"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Spielplan der Mädchen, D-Jugend Match schedule of the girls, under-13 team Samstag, 14. November: Heimspiel um 11 Uhr in unserer Sporthalle. Saturday 14 November: home match at 11 o'clock in our sports hall. Sonntag, 22. November: Auswärtsspiel um 15 Uhr. Abfahrt mit dem Bus um 13:30 Uhr an der Halle. Sunday 22 November: away match at 3 pm. The bus leaves at 1.30 pm at the hall. Bitte seid immer 45 Minuten vor dem Spiel in der Halle. Please always be in the hall 45 minutes before the match. Beim Heimspiel verkaufen die Eltern Kuchen und Getränke. Wer backt einen Kuchen? At the home match the parents sell cake and drinks. Who will bake a cake? Bitte tragt euch in die Liste an der Tür ein. Please put your name on the list on the door."],["notes","Notes","A model text, written for this course. A real one names people: replace them with placeholders before you save it. Heimspiel : home match. Auswärtsspiel : away match. seid and tragt euch ein are commands to the players: the Imperativ with ihr ."]]},{"u":"spielverlegung-pokal-und-bezirksliga.html","t":"Nachricht des Trainers: zwei Spiele verlegt","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Text"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Hallo liebe Eltern! Hello, dear parents! Wetterbedingt konnten wir ja heute Nachmittag nicht spielen. Because of the weather we could not play this afternoon. Somit musste das Spiel verschoben werden. So the match had to be postponed. Hinzu kommt, dass wir am nächsten Samstag 22.08.26 unser erstes reguläres Bezirksligaspiel hätten. On top of that, next Saturday, 22.08.26, we would have our first regular Bezirksliga match. Am 22.08.26 ist aber das Schulfest am Gymnasium und hier sind 7 SpielerInnen von uns betroffen. But on 22.08.26 there is the school festival at the Gymnasium, and 7 of our players are affected. Somit haben wir für beide Spiele neue Termine, die euch bitte vormerken solltet: So we have new dates for both matches, which you should please note down: Pokalspiel (Termin alt 15.08.26): Verein A II gegen JSG B. Termin neu: Montag 17.08.26, 19.15 Uhr in Ort C. Treffen um 18.15 Uhr in Ort C! Cup match (old date 15.08.26): Club A II against JSG B. New date: Monday 17.08.26, 19:15 in Town C. Meeting at 18:15 in Town C! Bezirksligaspiel (Termin alt 22.08.26): Verein A II gegen JSG B. Termin neu: Sonntag 23.08.26, 11.00 Uhr, Kunstrasen in Ort D. Treffen um 10.00 Uhr in Ort D. League match (old date 22.08.26): Club A II against JSG B. New date: Sunday 23.08.26, 11:00, artificial pitch in Town D. Meeting at 10:00 in Town D. Beste Grüße Best regards"],["notes","Notes","Treffen is the time the players meet, usually one hour before Anpfiff (kick-off). Put the meeting time in the calendar, not the kick-off. die euch bitte vormerken solltet is a slip of the coach: correct is die ihr euch bitte vormerken solltet . vormerken is reflexive here (sich etwas vormerken). SpielerInnen with a capital I is a gender-neutral spelling: male and female players. musste verschoben werden is the passive with a modal verb: see the grammar entry Passiv mit werden ."]]},{"u":"sporttasche.html","t":"Sporttasche","s":"sports bag","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn hat seine Sporttasche zu Hause vergessen. :: My son forgot his sports bag at home."]]},{"u":"sprechen.html","t":"sprechen","s":"to speak","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich spreche ein bisschen Deutsch. :: I speak a little German. Sprechen Sie Englisch? :: Do you speak English?"]]},{"u":"stadt.html","t":"Stadt","s":"town, city","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Samstag gehen wir in die Stadt. :: On Saturday we go into town."]]},{"u":"stark.html","t":"stark","s":"strong","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das andere Team ist sehr stark. :: The other team is very strong."]]},{"u":"stehen.html","t":"stehen","s":"to stand; to be (upright)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Auto steht vor dem Haus. :: The car is parked in front of the house."],["notes","Notes","Southern Germany says ich bin gestanden , the north ich habe gestanden ."]]},{"u":"stoerung.html","t":"Störung","s":"fault","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bei einer Störung rufe ich die Notfall-Hotline an. :: In case of a fault I call the emergency hotline. Entschuldigen Sie die Störung. :: Sorry to disturb you."],["notes","Notes","die Störung is a technical fault, but also an interruption: you say Entschuldigen Sie die Störung when you knock on a door or interrupt someone."]]},{"u":"strasse.html","t":"Straße","s":"street","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir wohnen in einer ruhigen Straße. :: We live in a quiet street."]]},{"u":"stunde.html","t":"Stunde","s":"hour","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Training dauert zwei Stunden. :: Training lasts two hours."]]},{"u":"suchen.html","t":"suchen","s":"to look for","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich suche den Bahnhof. :: I am looking for the station."],["notes","Notes","No preposition: Ich suche den Bahnhof , not für den Bahnhof ."]]},{"u":"suess.html","t":"süß","s":"sweet; cute","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Kuchen ist sehr süß. :: The cake is very sweet. Das Baby ist so süß! :: The baby is so cute!"]]},{"u":"supermarkt.html","t":"Supermarkt","s":"supermarket","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich gehe schnell in den Supermarkt. :: I am just popping to the supermarket."]]},{"u":"systemtrenner.html","t":"Systemtrenner","s":"backflow preventer","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B2"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Systemtrenner sind zwei grüne Hebel. :: There are two green levers on the backflow preventer. Der Systemtrenner trennt das Trinkwasser vom Heizungswasser. :: The backflow preventer separates the drinking water from the heating water."]]},{"u":"tag.html","t":"Tag","s":"day","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Guten Tag! :: Hello! Er bleibt drei Tage zu Hause. :: He stays at home for three days."]]},{"u":"tanzen.html","t":"tanzen","s":"to dance","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Tochter tanzt gern. :: My daughter likes dancing."]]},{"u":"tausend.html","t":"tausend","s":"thousand","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Auto kostet fünftausend Euro. :: The car costs five thousand euros."],["notes","Notes","Written together with the number before it: zweitausend , dreitausend ."]]},{"u":"tee.html","t":"Tee","s":"tea","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Möchtest du einen Tee? :: Would you like a tea?"]]},{"u":"telefonieren.html","t":"telefonieren","s":"to talk on the phone","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich telefoniere mit meiner Mutter. :: I am on the phone with my mother."],["notes","Notes","With mit + Dativ: mit meiner Mutter ."]]},{"u":"telefonnummer.html","t":"Telefonnummer","s":"phone number","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wie ist Ihre Telefonnummer? :: What is your phone number?"]]},{"u":"termin-am-telefon.html","t":"Termin am Telefon","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Arzthelferin: Praxis Dr. A., guten Tag! :: Dr A.'s practice, hello! ich: Guten Tag! Ich brauche einen Termin für meinen Sohn. :: Hello! I need an appointment for my son. Arzthelferin: Was hat er? :: What is wrong with him? ich: Er hat Fieber und Husten. :: He has a fever and a cough. Arzthelferin: Können Sie heute um elf Uhr kommen? :: Can you come today at eleven o'clock? ich: Ja, das geht. Danke! :: Yes, that works. Thank you! Arzthelferin: Wie alt ist Ihr Sohn? :: How old is your son? ich: Er ist acht Jahre alt. :: He is eight years old. Arzthelferin: Danke. Bis später! :: Thank you. See you later!"],["variations","Variations","6 ich: Um elf kann ich leider nicht. Geht es auch am Nachmittag? :: Sadly I can't at eleven. Is the afternoon possible too?"],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Das geht means that works . Geht es auch ...? asks for another time."]]},{"u":"termin-beim-kinderarzt.html","t":"Termin beim Kinderarzt","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Arzthelferin: Kinderarztpraxis, guten Morgen. :: Paediatric practice, good morning. ich: Guten Morgen. Mein Sohn ist krank. Ich brauche heute einen Termin. :: Good morning. My son is ill. I need an appointment today. Arzthelferin: Was hat er denn? :: What's wrong with him? ich: Er hat seit gestern Fieber und Husten. :: He has had a fever and a cough since yesterday. Arzthelferin: Wie hoch ist das Fieber? :: How high is the fever? ich: Heute Morgen hatte er 39 Grad. :: This morning he had 39 degrees. Arzthelferin: Kommen Sie bitte um elf Uhr. Bringen Sie die Versichertenkarte mit. :: Please come at eleven o'clock. Bring the health insurance card. ich: Gut, um elf Uhr. Vielen Dank! :: Good, at eleven o'clock. Thank you very much!"],["variations","Variations","7 Arzthelferin: Heute ist leider alles voll. Kommen Sie morgen um acht in die offene Sprechstunde. :: Sadly everything is full today. Come to the open consultation tomorrow at eight."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Versichertenkarte (also Gesundheitskarte ): the card of the health insurance. Bring it every quarter, and the U-Heft for check-ups."]]},{"u":"termin.html","t":"Termin","s":"appointment","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich brauche heute einen Termin. :: I need an appointment today. Mein Sohn hat morgen einen Termin beim Kinderarzt. :: My son has an appointment at the paediatrician's tomorrow."],["notes","Notes","False friend: Termin is not a term ; it is an appointment with a fixed time."]]},{"u":"teuer.html","t":"teuer","s":"expensive","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Fußballschuhe sind leider sehr teuer. :: Unfortunately the football boots are very expensive."],["notes","Notes","The e drops before an ending: ein teures Trikot , teurer ."]]},{"u":"tisch.html","t":"Tisch","s":"table","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Essen steht auf dem Tisch. :: The food is on the table."]]},{"u":"tochter.html","t":"Tochter","s":"daughter","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Meine Tochter ist krank und bleibt heute zu Hause. :: My daughter is ill and is staying at home today."]]},{"u":"toilette.html","t":"Toilette","s":"toilet","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wo ist die Toilette, bitte? :: Where is the toilet, please?"]]},{"u":"toll.html","t":"toll","s":"great","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Spiel war toll! :: The match was great!"]]},{"u":"tor.html","t":"Tor","s":"goal","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Dein Sohn hat zwei Tore geschossen. :: Your son scored two goals. Sie ist die Nummer sieben, im Tor. :: She is number seven, in goal."]]},{"u":"trainer.html","t":"Trainer","s":"coach","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bei anderen Fragen sprecht gerne eure Trainer an. :: For other questions, feel free to talk to your coaches. Ich schreibe dem Trainer eine Nachricht. :: I'm writing a message to the coach. Der Trainer schreibt alles in den Chat. :: The coach writes everything in the chat."],["false-friends","False friends","der Trainer is the coach, a person. Sports shoes are die Turnschuhe or die Sportschuhe , not Trainer ."]]},{"u":"trainieren.html","t":"trainieren","s":"to train","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn trainiert am Dienstag und am Donnerstag. :: My son trains on Tuesday and Thursday."],["notes","Notes","Verbs ending in -ieren have no ge- in the Perfekt: trainiert ."]]},{"u":"training.html","t":"Training","s":"training, practice","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kind A. kann heute leider nicht zum Training kommen. :: Child A. sadly cannot come to training today. Das Training beginnt um 17.45 Uhr. :: Training starts at 5:45 pm. Beim nächsten Training ist er wieder dabei. :: He'll be there again at the next training. Wie war das Training heute? :: How was training today? Heute ist kein Training. Es regnet. :: There is no training today. It is raining."],["pronunciation","Pronunciation","Said the English way: TRAI-ning , with a German r ."]]},{"u":"traurig.html","t":"traurig","s":"sad","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Sohn ist traurig. Heute ist kein Training. :: My son is sad. There is no training today."]]},{"u":"treffen-verb.html","t":"treffen","s":"to meet","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir treffen uns um drei im Café. :: We meet at three in the café."],["notes","Notes","sich treffen : to meet each other. jemanden treffen : to meet someone."]]},{"u":"treffen.html","t":"Treffen","s":"meeting, meeting time","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Treffen um 18.15 Uhr in Ort C! :: Meeting at 18:15 in Town C! Das Treffen ist eine Stunde vor dem Anpfiff. :: The meeting is one hour before kick-off."],["notes","Notes","In a match message Treffen is when the players must be there, not when the match starts. The noun is the infinitive of sich treffen , so it is neuter."]]},{"u":"trennbare-verben.html","t":"Trennbare Verben","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Some verbs have a prefix that splits off: anrufen, abholen, aufstehen, mitbringen . In a main clause the verb is in position 2 and the prefix goes to the end. Ich hole die Kinder um vier ab . Wann fängt das Training an ? With a modal verb, or after weil and dass , the verb stays together at the end: Ich muss die Kinder abholen. ..., weil das Training um vier anfängt. In the Perfekt, ge- goes between the prefix and the verb: abgeholt, angerufen, aufgestanden . The stress is always on the prefix: AB-holen ."],["simple-german","Simple German","Bei trennbaren Verben steht das Präfix am Satzende: Ich rufe dich an. Im Perfekt: Ich habe dich angerufen."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich abhole meine Tochter um vier. :: Ich hole meine Tochter um vier ab. Ich habe die Schule geanruft. :: Ich habe die Schule angerufen."]]},{"u":"treppenhaus.html","t":"Treppenhaus","s":"stairwell","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Im Treppenhaus hängt ein Zettel. :: There is a note hanging in the stairwell."]]},{"u":"trikot.html","t":"Trikot","s":"team shirt","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Trikot bekommt er von uns. :: He gets the shirt from us."]]},{"u":"trinken.html","t":"trinken","s":"to drink","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Du musst viel trinken. :: You have to drink a lot."]]},{"u":"trotzdem.html","t":"trotzdem","s":"anyway / nevertheless","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Es regnet, trotzdem findet das Spiel statt. :: It's raining, but the match is taking place anyway."],["notes","Notes","After trotzdem at the start, the verb comes right away."]]},{"u":"tschuess.html","t":"tschüss","s":"bye","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bis morgen, tschüss! :: See you tomorrow, bye!"],["notes","Notes","Informal goodbye. Formal: Auf Wiedersehen ."]]},{"u":"tuer.html","t":"Tür","s":"door","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mach bitte die Tür zu! :: Please close the door!"]]},{"u":"ueber.html","t":"über","s":"over / above / about","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Lampe ist über dem Tisch. :: The lamp is above the table. Das Bild hängt über dem Sofa. :: The picture hangs above the sofa."],["notes","Notes","über plus Akkusativ also means about : über den Ausflug sprechen ."]]},{"u":"uebermorgen.html","t":"übermorgen","s":"the day after tomorrow","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Übermorgen haben wir einen Termin. :: The day after tomorrow we have an appointment."]]},{"u":"ueberqueren.html","t":"überqueren","s":"to cross","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Überqueren Sie die Straße möglichst zügig und auf direktem Weg. :: Cross the road as quickly as possible and straight across. Die Kinder überqueren die Straße an der Ampel. :: The children cross the road at the traffic lights."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich habe die Straße geüberquert. :: Ich habe die Straße überquert."],["notes","Notes","über- is not separable here: ich überquere , participle without ge- . The sign also uses queren with the same meaning: Der Wanderweg quert hier eine Straße."]]},{"u":"ueberweisung.html","t":"Überweisung","s":"bank transfer","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Preis wird von jedem Mitfahrer selbst per Überweisung getätigt. :: Each participant pays the price themselves by bank transfer. Diese Überweisung gilt als verbindliche Anmeldung. :: This transfer counts as a binding registration."],["false-friends","False friends","At the doctor, die Überweisung is a referral to a specialist."]]},{"u":"uhr.html","t":"Uhr","s":"clock, watch; o'clock","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Es ist acht Uhr. :: It is eight o'clock. Wie viel Uhr ist es? :: What time is it?"],["notes","Notes","Uhr is the clock and the hour on the clock. A length of time is Stunde : zwei Stunden ."]]},{"u":"uhrzeit-und-zeitangaben.html","t":"Uhrzeit und Zeitangaben","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Clock time with um : um acht Uhr, um halb acht (7:30), um Viertel nach vier (4:15), um Viertel vor fünf (4:45). Days and parts of the day with am : am Montag, am Wochenende, am Nachmittag (but in der Nacht ). Months and seasons with im : im Dezember, im Sommer . From... to: von neun bis zwölf Uhr . By a day: bis Mittwoch . halb looks forward to the next hour: halb acht is 7:30, not 8:30."],["simple-german","Simple German","um acht Uhr, am Montag, im Dezember. halb acht = 7:30."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Am acht Uhr :: Um acht Uhr In Montag :: Am Montag"]]},{"u":"um.html","t":"um","s":"at (clock time) / around","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir fangen um sechs Uhr an. :: We start at six o'clock."]]},{"u":"umsteigen.html","t":"umsteigen","s":"to change (trains, buses)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am Bahnhof müssen wir umsteigen. :: We have to change at the station."]]},{"u":"und.html","t":"und","s":"and","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Sie hat Fieber und bleibt heute zu Hause. :: She has a fever and is staying at home today."]]},{"u":"unser.html","t":"unser","s":"our","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Spiel ist auf unserem Platz. :: The match is on our pitch."],["notes","Notes","Endings like ein ."]]},{"u":"unten.html","t":"unten","s":"downstairs / below","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir wohnen unten im Erdgeschoss. :: We live downstairs on the ground floor."]]},{"u":"unter.html","t":"unter","s":"under / below","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Schuhe stehen unter dem Bett. :: The shoes are under the bed."]]},{"u":"urlaub.html","t":"Urlaub","s":"holiday, vacation","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Im August habe ich Urlaub. :: In August I am on holiday."]]},{"u":"vater.html","t":"Vater","s":"father","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Vater holt die Kinder um vier Uhr ab. :: The father picks up the children at four o'clock."]]},{"u":"verabredung-am-wochenende.html","t":"Verabredung am Wochenende","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Freundin: Hey! Hast du am Samstag Zeit? :: Hey! Are you free on Saturday? ich: Am Vormittag nicht, da hat mein Sohn ein Spiel. Aber am Nachmittag habe ich Zeit. :: Not in the morning, my son has a match then. But in the afternoon I'm free. Freundin: Trinken wir einen Kaffee in der Stadt? :: Shall we have a coffee in town? ich: Ja, gern! Um wie viel Uhr? :: Yes, I'd love to! What time? Freundin: Um drei? Im Café am Marktplatz? :: At three? In the café on the market square? ich: Perfekt. Bis Samstag! :: Perfect. See you on Saturday!"],["variations","Variations","4 ich: Leider nicht, ich habe keine Zeit. Vielleicht nächste Woche? :: Sadly not, I'm not free. Maybe next week?"],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. da here means then : am Vormittag, da hat mein Sohn ein Spiel ."]]},{"u":"verb-an-position-2.html","t":"Verb an Position 2","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","In a German main clause the conjugated verb is always the second element. The first element can be the subject, a time or a place; when it is not the subject, the subject comes right after the verb. Ich / gehe morgen zum Training. Morgen / gehe ich zum Training. Am Samstag haben wir ein Spiel. In yes-or-no questions and in commands the verb comes first: Kommst du mit? Komm bitte!"],["simple-german","Simple German","Im Hauptsatz steht das Verb auf Position 2. Heute spielt mein Sohn Fußball. Bei Ja-Nein-Fragen steht das Verb am Anfang."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Morgen ich gehe zum Training. :: Morgen gehe ich zum Training. Am Samstag wir haben ein Spiel. :: Am Samstag haben wir ein Spiel."]]},{"u":"vergessen.html","t":"vergessen","s":"to forget","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe mein Heft vergessen. :: I forgot my exercise book."]]},{"u":"verheiratet.html","t":"verheiratet","s":"married","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich bin verheiratet und habe zwei Kinder. :: I am married and have two children."]]},{"u":"verlieren.html","t":"verlieren","s":"to lose","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Schade, ihr habt verloren. :: Pity, you lost."]]},{"u":"verschieben.html","t":"verschieben","s":"to postpone, to move","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Somit musste das Spiel verschoben werden. :: So the match had to be postponed. Wir verschieben das Training auf Donnerstag. :: We are moving training to Thursday."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Das Spiel ist verschiebt. :: Das Spiel ist verschoben."],["notes","Notes","verlegen is used the same way: Das Spiel wurde verlegt. verschieben auf + Akkusativ gives the new date."]]},{"u":"verstehen.html","t":"verstehen","s":"to understand","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das verstehe ich nicht. Bitte noch einmal. :: I don't understand that. Once more, please."],["notes","Notes","No ge- in the participle: verstanden ."]]},{"u":"verwendungszweck.html","t":"Verwendungszweck","s":"payment reference","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Verwendungszweck: Vorname und Nachname des Kindes und Spanien 2027. :: Payment reference: the child's first name and surname and \"Spanien 2027\". Bitte geben Sie die Rechnungsnummer als Verwendungszweck an. :: Please give the invoice number as the payment reference."],["notes","Notes","The field on a bank transfer that says what the money is for. Copy it exactly, or the club cannot match your payment."]]},{"u":"viel-spass.html","t":"Viel Spaß!","s":"Have fun!","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Viel Spaß beim Feiern! :: Have fun celebrating! Viel Erfolg! :: Good luck! (with a task) Viel Glück! :: Good luck!"],["usage","Usage","beim plus a verb as a noun says what to have fun with: beim Spiel , beim Grillen ."]]},{"u":"viel.html","t":"viel","s":"much / a lot","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Du musst viel trinken. :: You have to drink a lot. Wir brauchen mehr Autos. :: We need more cars."],["notes","Notes","Before a noun: viel Zeit , viele Kinder ."]]},{"u":"vielleicht.html","t":"vielleicht","s":"maybe","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Vielleicht nächste Woche? :: Maybe next week?"]]},{"u":"vier.html","t":"vier","s":"four","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich hole sie um Viertel nach vier ab. :: I'll pick her up at quarter past four."]]},{"u":"vierte.html","t":"vierte","s":"fourth","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir wohnen im vierten Stock. :: We live on the fourth floor."]]},{"u":"viertel.html","t":"Viertel","s":"quarter","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich hole sie um Viertel nach vier ab. :: I will pick her up at quarter past four. Das Training fängt um Viertel vor fünf an. :: Training starts at quarter to five."]]},{"u":"vierzehn.html","t":"vierzehn","s":"fourteen","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Kurs hat vierzehn Leute. :: The course has fourteen people."]]},{"u":"vierzehnte.html","t":"vierzehnte","s":"fourteenth","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am vierzehnten Februar ist Valentinstag. :: The fourteenth of February is Valentine's Day."]]},{"u":"vierzig.html","t":"vierzig","s":"forty","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich bin vierzig Jahre alt. :: I am forty years old."]]},{"u":"voll.html","t":"voll","s":"full","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Heute ist leider alles voll. :: Sadly everything is full today."]]},{"u":"vollpension.html","t":"Vollpension","s":"full board","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Vollpension heißt Buffet am Morgen, Mittag und Abend. :: Full board means a buffet in the morning, at midday and in the evening. Das Hotel ist mit Vollpension im Preis inbegriffen. :: The hotel with full board is included in the price."],["notes","Notes","Halbpension is half board: breakfast and dinner."]]},{"u":"von.html","t":"von","s":"from / of","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das ist sehr nett von Ihnen. :: That is very kind of you."]]},{"u":"vor.html","t":"vor","s":"in front of / before / ago","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte seid 45 Minuten vor dem Spiel in der Halle. :: Please be in the hall 45 minutes before the match. Ich warte vor der Halle auf dich. :: I'm waiting for you in front of the hall."],["notes","Notes","With time it always takes the Dativ: vor dem Spiel , vor zwei Jahren (two years ago)."]]},{"u":"vorgestern.html","t":"vorgestern","s":"the day before yesterday","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Vorgestern war ich beim Arzt. :: The day before yesterday I was at the doctor's."]]},{"u":"vorlesen.html","t":"vorlesen","s":"to read aloud","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Liest du mir noch eine Geschichte vor? :: Will you read me a story?"]]},{"u":"vormerken.html","t":"vormerken","s":"to note down, to make a note of","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir haben neue Termine, die ihr euch bitte vormerken solltet. :: We have new dates, which you should please note down. Ich merke mir den Termin vor. :: I'm making a note of the date."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich vormerke mir den Termin. :: Ich merke mir den Termin vor."],["notes","Notes","With a thing as object the reflexive pronoun is in the dative: ich merke mir etwas vor . Without sich it means to reserve or put on a list: Ich habe Sie für Montag vorgemerkt."]]},{"u":"vormittags.html","t":"vormittags","s":"in the morning (before noon)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Vormittags arbeite ich im Büro. :: In the mornings I work in the office."]]},{"u":"vorne.html","t":"vorne","s":"at the front","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Eingang ist vorne. :: The entrance is at the front."],["notes","Notes","Also vorn , the same word."]]},{"u":"w-fragen.html","t":"W-Fragen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","Questions with a question word put the word first and the verb second. Wer? Was? Wann? Wo? Wohin? Woher? Wie? Warum? Wie viel? Um wie viel Uhr? Wann fängt das Training an? Wo ist das Spiel? Wer kann fahren? Was fehlt dir? Yes-or-no questions start with the verb: Hast du Zeit? Kommt ihr auch?"],["simple-german","Simple German","W-Frage: Fragewort, dann Verb: Wann kommst du? Ja-Nein-Frage: Verb am Anfang: Kommst du?"],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Wann das Training fängt an? :: Wann fängt das Training an? Wo du wohnst? :: Wo wohnst du?"]]},{"u":"waehrend.html","t":"während","s":"during","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Während des Spiels sitzen die Eltern auf der Tribüne. :: During the match the parents sit on the stand."]]},{"u":"waermepumpe.html","t":"Wärmepumpe","s":"heat pump","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Firma A finanziert Ihnen den Kauf der Wärmepumpe über einen Ratenkauf. :: Company A finances your purchase of the heat pump through a hire purchase. Sie zahlen erst nach Installation der Wärmepumpe. :: You only pay after the heat pump has been installed. Unsere alte Ölheizung wird durch eine Wärmepumpe ersetzt. :: Our old oil heating is being replaced by a heat pump."],["notes","Notes","A compound noun takes the article of its last part: die Wärme + die Pumpe = die Wärmepumpe ."]]},{"u":"wann.html","t":"wann","s":"when","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wann fängt das Training an? :: When does training start? Weißt du, wann er anfängt? :: Do you know when it starts?"],["notes","Notes","wann asks for a time. For when in a statement, use wenn or als ."]]},{"u":"warm.html","t":"warm","s":"warm","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Kinder brauchen warme Kleidung. :: The children need warm clothes. Von neun bis zwölf Uhr gibt es kein warmes Wasser. :: From nine to twelve there is no hot water."],["notes","Notes","warmes Wasser is hot water from the tap."]]},{"u":"warten.html","t":"warten","s":"to wait","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich warte vor der Halle auf dich. :: I am waiting for you in front of the hall."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich warte für dich. :: Ich warte auf dich."]]},{"u":"wartung.html","t":"Wartung","s":"maintenance","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die regelmäßige Wartung ist für die Garantie wichtig. :: Regular maintenance is important for the warranty. Die Firma macht die Wartung spätestens alle 24 Monate. :: The company does the maintenance at least every 24 months."],["notes","Notes","warten means to wait, but also to service a machine: eine Anlage warten . In IT: das Wartungsfenster is a maintenance window."]]},{"u":"warum.html","t":"warum","s":"why","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ja, warum? :: Yes, why?"],["notes","Notes","The answer often starts with weil ."]]},{"u":"was-fehlt-dir.html","t":"Was fehlt dir?","s":"What's wrong with you?","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Was fehlt Ihnen? :: What's wrong with you? (Sie) Was hat er denn? :: What's wrong with him?"],["usage","Usage","The doctor's question. The answer often uses wehtun : Mein Hals tut weh."]]},{"u":"was-gibts.html","t":"Was gibt's?","s":"What's up? / What is it?","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Ja, bitte. Was gibt's? :: Yes, please. What is it? Was gibt's Neues? :: What's new?"],["usage","Usage","When someone wants to talk to you. gibt's is gibt es ."]]},{"u":"was.html","t":"was","s":"what","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Was gibt es zum Frühstück? :: What is there for breakfast? Was ist los? :: What's the matter?"],["notes","Notes","In speech was also means something : Träum was Schönes!"]]},{"u":"waschen.html","t":"waschen","s":"to wash","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich wasche heute die T-Shirts. :: I am washing the T-shirts today."]]},{"u":"wasser.html","t":"Wasser","s":"water","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ein Glas Wasser, bitte. :: A glass of water, please."]]},{"u":"wasseruhr.html","t":"Wasseruhr","s":"water meter","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Haupthahn ist direkt neben der Wasseruhr. :: The main tap is right next to the water meter."],["notes","Notes","Here die Uhr is a meter, not a clock. der Wasserzähler means the same."]]},{"u":"wechselpraepositionen.html","t":"Wechselpräpositionen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","in, an, auf, unter, über, vor, hinter, neben, zwischen take two cases. Wohin? (where to, movement) takes the Akkusativ: Wir gehen in die Halle. Ich lege den Ball auf den Tisch. Wo? (where, place) takes the Dativ: Wir sind in der Halle. Der Ball liegt auf dem Tisch. Short forms: ins = in das , im = in dem , am = an dem . Ins Bett gehen but im Bett liegen ."],["simple-german","Simple German","Wohin? Akkusativ: in die Schule . Wo? Dativ: in der Schule ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Wir gehen in der Halle. :: Wir gehen in die Halle. Ich bin in die Schule. :: Ich bin in der Schule."]]},{"u":"wegen.html","t":"wegen","s":"because of","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wegen Regen fällt das Training heute leider aus. :: Because of rain, training is cancelled today."],["notes","Notes","In writing with the Genitiv: wegen des Regens . In speech often with the Dativ, or with no article."]]},{"u":"wehtun.html","t":"wehtun","s":"to hurt","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mein Hals tut weh. :: My throat hurts."],["notes","Notes","Mir tut der Bauch weh : my tummy hurts. The person who feels the pain is in the Dativ."]]},{"u":"weil.html","t":"weil","s":"because","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich rufe an, weil meine Tochter krank ist. :: I am calling because my daughter is ill."],["notes","Notes","After weil the conjugated verb goes to the end: weil sie krank . ist"]]},{"u":"weit.html","t":"weit","s":"far / wide","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ist die Halle weit von hier? :: Is the hall far from here?"]]},{"u":"welcher.html","t":"welcher","s":"which","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Welche Schuhe brauchst du? :: Which shoes do you need?"],["notes","Notes","Endings like der, die, das : welcher, welche, welches ."]]},{"u":"wenig.html","t":"wenig","s":"little / not much","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich habe heute wenig Zeit. :: I have little time today."]]},{"u":"wenn-es-sich-einrichten-laesst.html","t":"wenn es sich einrichten lässt","s":"if it can be arranged, if possible","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["B1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Hallo, wenn es sich einrichten lässt, ja. :: Hello, if it can be arranged, yes. Ich komme, wenn es sich einrichten lässt. :: I'll come if I can make it work."],["usage","Usage","A polite yes with a condition: you would like it, but you understand it may not always work. wenn möglich is shorter."]]},{"u":"wenn.html","t":"wenn","s":"if / when","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte rufen Sie wieder an, wenn sie länger krank ist. :: Please call again if she is ill for longer."]]},{"u":"wer.html","t":"wer","s":"who","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wer kann fahren? :: Who can drive? Wen rufst du an? :: Who are you calling?"]]},{"u":"wetter.html","t":"Wetter","s":"weather","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wie ist das Wetter heute? :: What is the weather like today?"]]},{"u":"wichtig.html","t":"wichtig","s":"important","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Versichertenkarte ist sehr wichtig. :: The health insurance card is very important."]]},{"u":"widerrufen.html","t":"widerrufen","s":"to withdraw, to revoke","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["B2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Käufer kann seine Vertragserklärung innerhalb von 14 Tagen ohne Angabe von Gründen widerrufen. :: The buyer can withdraw his contractual declaration within 14 days without giving reasons. Hiermit widerrufe ich den abgeschlossenen Vertrag. :: I hereby withdraw from the contract I concluded. Die Vollmacht bleibt bis zu ihrem Widerruf gültig. :: The power of attorney stays valid until it is revoked."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","Ich rufe den Vertrag wider. :: Ich widerrufe den Vertrag. Ich habe den Vertrag gewiderrufen. :: Ich habe den Vertrag widerrufen."],["notes","Notes","wider- (against) is not separated here, so the participle has no ge- . Do not mix it up with wieder (again). The noun is der Widerruf , the period is the Widerrufsfrist ."]]},{"u":"wie-gehts.html","t":"Wie geht's?","s":"How are you?","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Wie geht es dir? :: How are you? (du) Wie geht es Ihnen? :: How are you? (Sie)"],["usage","Usage","The everyday question when you meet someone you know. Germans expect a real, short answer."]]},{"u":"wie-spaet-ist-es.html","t":"Wie spät ist es?","s":"What time is it?","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Wie viel Uhr ist es? :: What time is it? Es ist halb acht. :: It's half past seven."],["usage","Usage","Both questions mean the same."]]},{"u":"wie-steht-es.html","t":"Wie steht es?","s":"What's the score?","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Zwölf zu zehn für uns. :: Twelve to ten for us. Es steht unentschieden. :: It's a draw."],["usage","Usage","On the stand during a match. The score is said with zu : drei zu eins ."]]},{"u":"wie-wars-in-der-schule.html","t":"Wie war's in der Schule?","s":"How was school?","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Wie war das Training? :: How was training? Wie war dein Wochenende? :: How was your weekend?"],["usage","Usage","The question when a child comes home. war's is war es ."]]},{"u":"wie.html","t":"wie","s":"how","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wie war das Training heute? :: How was training today? Um wie viel Uhr? :: What time?"],["notes","Notes","wie viel : how much. wie viele : how many. so groß wie : as big as."]]},{"u":"wieder.html","t":"wieder","s":"again","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte rufen Sie wieder an. :: Please call again."]]},{"u":"wiederholen.html","t":"wiederholen","s":"to repeat","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Können Sie das bitte wiederholen? :: Can you repeat that, please?"],["notes","Notes","Not separable: Ich wiederhole , participle wiederholt ."]]},{"u":"wir.html","t":"wir","s":"we","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Unsere Nachbarn laden uns zum Grillen ein. :: Our neighbours invite us to a barbecue."]]},{"u":"wirklich.html","t":"wirklich","s":"really","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wirklich? Das freut mich! :: Really? I'm glad!"]]},{"u":"wissen.html","t":"wissen","s":"to know (a fact)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich weiß es noch nicht. :: I don't know yet."],["notes","Notes","wissen is for facts; kennen is for people and places."]]},{"u":"wo.html","t":"wo","s":"where","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wann und wo ist das Spiel? :: When and where is the match?"],["notes","Notes","wo? asks for a place: Dativ after in, an, auf ."]]},{"u":"woche.html","t":"Woche","s":"week","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Nächste Woche habe ich Urlaub. :: Next week I am on holiday."]]},{"u":"wochenende.html","t":"Wochenende","s":"weekend","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wie war dein Wochenende? :: How was your weekend?"]]},{"u":"woher.html","t":"woher","s":"where from","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Woher kommen Sie? :: Where are you from?"]]},{"u":"wohin.html","t":"wohin","s":"where to","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wohin fahrt ihr am Wochenende? :: Where are you going at the weekend?"],["notes","Notes","wohin? asks for a direction: Akkusativ after in, an, auf ."]]},{"u":"wohnen.html","t":"wohnen","s":"to live (somewhere)","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich wohne im zweiten Stock. :: I live on the second floor."],["notes","Notes","wohnen is where you live; leben is to be alive, or to live in a country."]]},{"u":"wohnung.html","t":"Wohnung","s":"flat / apartment","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Unsere Wohnung ist im Erdgeschoss. :: Our flat is on the ground floor."]]},{"u":"wollen.html","t":"wollen","s":"to want","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich will zuerst spielen. :: I want to play first."],["notes","Notes","Ich will sounds direct. To ask politely, say Ich möchte ."]]},{"u":"zaehne-putzen.html","t":"Zähne putzen","s":"to brush one's teeth","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Putz bitte die Zähne! :: Please brush your teeth! Hast du die Zähne geputzt? :: Have you brushed your teeth?"],["usage","Usage","German says die Zähne putzen , the teeth, not my teeth ."]]},{"u":"zahlen.html","t":"Zahlen","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Grammar"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["explanation","Explanation","0 null, 1 eins, 2 zwei, 3 drei, 4 vier, 5 fünf, 6 sechs, 7 sieben, 8 acht, 9 neun, 10 zehn, 11 elf, 12 zwölf From 13 to 19: number plus -zehn : dreizehn, vierzehn , but sechzehn and siebzehn . From 21 the units come first: einundzwanzig (21), fünfunddreißig (35). Tens: zwanzig, dreißig, vierzig, fünfzig, sechzig, siebzig, achtzig, neunzig, hundert . Ordinals for dates and floors: der erste, zweite, dritte, vierte , then -te up to 19 and -ste from 20. am 19. November is read am neunzehnten November ."],["simple-german","Simple German","21 ist einundzwanzig : zuerst die Eins, dann die Zwanzig. Ordinalzahlen: erste, zweite, dritte ."],["typical-mistakes","Typical mistakes","zwanzigeins :: einundzwanzig der dreite Stock :: der dritte Stock"]]},{"u":"zahn.html","t":"Zahn","s":"tooth","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Putz bitte noch schnell die Zähne. :: Please quickly brush your teeth."]]},{"u":"zehn.html","t":"zehn","s":"ten","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Darf ich noch zehn Minuten fernsehen? :: May I watch TV for ten more minutes?"]]},{"u":"zehnte.html","t":"zehnte","s":"tenth","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Am zehnten habe ich Geburtstag. :: My birthday is on the tenth."]]},{"u":"zeigen.html","t":"zeigen","s":"to show","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Kannst du mir den Weg zeigen? :: Can you show me the way?"],["notes","Notes","The person is in the Dativ, the thing in the Akkusativ: mir den Weg ."]]},{"u":"zeit-haben.html","t":"Zeit haben","s":"to have time / to be free","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Hast du am Samstag Zeit? :: Are you free on Saturday? Haben Sie kurz Zeit? :: Do you have a moment? Ich habe leider keine Zeit. :: Sadly I'm not free."],["usage","Usage","To ask whether someone is free. No time is keine Zeit , not nicht Zeit ."]]},{"u":"zeit.html","t":"Zeit","s":"time","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Hast du am Samstag Zeit? :: Do you have time on Saturday? Ich habe leider keine Zeit. :: Sadly I have no time."]]},{"u":"zettel-im-treppenhaus.html","t":"Zettel im Treppenhaus","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Text"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","Liebe Nachbarn, Dear neighbours, am Samstag ab neun Uhr kommen die Handwerker. Sie reparieren die Heizung im Keller. On Saturday from nine o'clock the workmen are coming. They will repair the heating in the basement. Von neun bis zwölf Uhr gibt es kein warmes Wasser. From nine to twelve there will be no hot water. Bitte stellen Sie keine Fahrräder und Kinderwagen vor die Kellertür. Please do not put bicycles or prams in front of the basement door. Vielen Dank für Ihr Verständnis! Thank you for your understanding! Ihre Hausverwaltung Your property management"],["notes","Notes","A model text, written for this course. A real one names people: replace them with placeholders before you save it. Hausverwaltung : the company that looks after the building for the owner. Nothing to answer: keep the hall in front of the basement free on Saturday."]]},{"u":"zettel.html","t":"Zettel","s":"note / slip of paper","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Bitte geben Sie ihm einen kurzen Zettel mit. :: Please give him a short note to take."]]},{"u":"zimmer.html","t":"Zimmer","s":"room","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["das"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Räum bitte dein Zimmer auf! :: Please tidy up your room!"]]},{"u":"zu-hause-bleiben.html","t":"zu Hause bleiben","s":"to stay at home","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Chunk"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["variants","Variants","Sie bleibt heute zu Hause. :: She is staying at home today. Er muss drei Tage zu Hause bleiben. :: He has to stay at home for three days."],["usage","Usage","zu Hause : at home. nach Hause : home, where to."]]},{"u":"zu-laut.html","t":"Zu laut","s":"","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Conversation"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["","","ich: Entschuldigung, es ist schon elf Uhr. Könnten Sie bitte die Musik leiser machen? :: Excuse me, it's already eleven o'clock. Could you please turn the music down? Nachbar: Oh, Entschuldigung! Ist es so laut? :: Oh, sorry! Is it that loud? ich: Ja, leider. Meine Kinder können nicht schlafen. :: Yes, unfortunately. My children can't sleep. Nachbar: Das tut mir leid. Ich mache sie sofort leiser. :: I'm sorry. I'll turn it down right away. ich: Danke, das ist nett. Gute Nacht! :: Thanks, that's kind. Good night!"],["variations","Variations","4 Nachbar: Wir feiern heute. Es dauert nur noch eine halbe Stunde. :: We're celebrating today. It will only go on for another half hour."],["notes","Notes","A model conversation: written to practise, not one that happened. Könnten Sie bitte ...? is the polite way to ask. From ten in the evening the house rules ask for quiet ( Nachtruhe )."]]},{"u":"zu.html","t":"zu","s":"to","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir gehen heute zum Kinderarzt. :: We are going to the paediatrician today."],["notes","Notes","zum is zu dem , zur is zu der . zu Hause means at home."]]},{"u":"zuerst.html","t":"zuerst","s":"first","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Zuerst die Hausaufgaben, dann darfst du spielen. :: Homework first, then you may play."]]},{"u":"zufahrt.html","t":"Zufahrt","s":"access road","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["B1"],"Article":["die"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Die Feuerwehrzufahrt muss immer frei bleiben. :: The fire brigade access must always stay clear. Die Zufahrt zum Parkplatz ist heute gesperrt. :: The access to the car park is closed today."],["notes","Notes","A car parked in a Feuerwehrzufahrt is towed away ( abgeschleppt ). Einfahrt is the way in, Ausfahrt the way out; Einfahrt freihalten on a garage door means: do not block it."]]},{"u":"zug.html","t":"Zug","s":"train","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"],"Article":["der"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der Zug kommt um zehn Uhr an. :: The train arrives at ten o'clock."]]},{"u":"zumachen.html","t":"zumachen","s":"to close","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Verb"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Mach bitte die Tür zu! :: Please close the door!"]]},{"u":"zurueck.html","t":"zurück","s":"back","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich bin um sechs Uhr zurück. :: I will be back at six o'clock."]]},{"u":"zusammen.html","t":"zusammen","s":"together","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Wir frühstücken am Sonntag zusammen. :: We have breakfast together on Sunday."],["notes","Notes","Hallo zusammen! greets a whole group."]]},{"u":"zwanzig.html","t":"zwanzig","s":"twenty","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","In der Klasse sind zwanzig Kinder. :: There are twenty children in the class."],["notes","Notes","Tens and units are said backwards: 21 is einundzwanzig , one-and-twenty."]]},{"u":"zwanzigste.html","t":"zwanzigste","s":"twentieth","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Heute ist der zwanzigste Oktober. :: Today is the twentieth of October."],["notes","Notes","From zwanzig on, ordinals end in -ste : zwanzigste , dreißigste ."]]},{"u":"zwei.html","t":"zwei","s":"two","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Dein Sohn hat zwei Tore geschossen. :: Your son scored two goals."],["notes","Notes","On the phone people often say zwo so it is not confused with drei ."]]},{"u":"zweite.html","t":"zweite","s":"second","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Ich wohne im zweiten Stock. :: I live on the second floor."]]},{"u":"zwischen.html","t":"zwischen","s":"between","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A2"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Das Café ist zwischen der Bank und dem Supermarkt. :: The café is between the bank and the supermarket."]]},{"u":"zwoelf.html","t":"zwölf","s":"twelve","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Zwölf zu zehn für uns. :: Twelve to ten for us."]]},{"u":"zwoelfte.html","t":"zwölfte","s":"twelfth","k":"","c":"","f":{"Type":["Word"],"Level":["A1"]},"w":[],"g":[],"x":[["examples","Examples","Der zwölfte Monat ist Dezember. :: The twelfth month is December."]]}];
